// Official SAT question bank items (cropped from the user's PDF exports) with a worked answer key.
const BANK = [{"id":"2c3aefc9","k":17,"diff":"Hard","type":"spr","img":"bank/2c3aefc9_q.png","e":"Let RS = x, so PS = x + 8. Pythagorean theorem: x^2 + (x+8)^2 = 2344, so x^2 + 8x - 1140 = 0 and x = 30. QR is opposite PS, so QR = 30 + 8 = 38.","ad":"38","a":38.0},{"id":"e89f63bf","k":16,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":"bank/e89f63bf_q.png","e":"The angles of a triangle sum to 180°, so the third angle is 180° − 64° = 116°.","cimg":["bank/e89f63bf_A.png","bank/e89f63bf_B.png","bank/e89f63bf_C.png","bank/e89f63bf_D.png"],"a":2},{"id":"ecc98c87","k":16,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":"bank/ecc98c87_q.png","e":"Angles w and y are corresponding angles (both above line k, to the right of the vertical lines). If y = w = 147, the corresponding angles are congruent, so r ∥ s. Choices A and D are always true, and C would mean the lines are not parallel.","cimg":["bank/ecc98c87_A.png","bank/ecc98c87_B.png","bank/ecc98c87_C.png","bank/ecc98c87_D.png"],"a":1},{"id":"d12bca0a","k":18,"diff":"Hard","type":"mc","img":"bank/d12bca0a_q.png","e":"(8, 0) is on the circle, so r = 8. Then 2^2 + k^2 = 64, so k^2 = 60 and k = √60.","cimg":["bank/d12bca0a_A.png","bank/d12bca0a_B.png","bank/d12bca0a_C.png","bank/d12bca0a_D.png"],"a":3},{"id":"1fe41c6b","k":15,"diff":"Hard","type":"mc","img":"bank/1fe41c6b_q.png","e":"The area ratio is 2520/630 = 4, so the scale factor is √4 = 2. Perimeters scale by 2: n = 2(210) = 420.","cimg":["bank/1fe41c6b_A.png","bank/1fe41c6b_B.png","bank/1fe41c6b_C.png","bank/1fe41c6b_D.png"],"a":3},{"id":"1dc7e423","k":16,"diff":"Hard","type":"mc","img":"bank/1dc7e423_q.png","e":"If B = 32° and R = 96°, then C = 180 − 52 − 32 = 96° and Q = 180 − 52 − 96 = 32°. Triangle ABC has angles 52°, 32°, 96°, the same as PQR, so the triangles are similar by AA.","cimg":["bank/1dc7e423_A.png","bank/1dc7e423_B.png","bank/1dc7e423_C.png","bank/1dc7e423_D.png"],"a":2},{"id":"408b39ea","k":18,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":"bank/408b39ea_q.png","e":"The center is (3, −16) and r = 17, so x-values on the circle run from 3 − 17 = −14 to 3 + 17 = 20. q = −17 is outside that range.","cimg":["bank/408b39ea_A.png","bank/408b39ea_B.png","bank/408b39ea_C.png","bank/408b39ea_D.png"],"a":0},{"id":"124bc42b","k":15,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":"bank/124bc42b_q.png","e":"Area = length × width = 7 × 2 = 14.","cimg":["bank/124bc42b_A.png","bank/124bc42b_B.png","bank/124bc42b_C.png","bank/124bc42b_D.png"],"a":2},{"id":"30aa51b7","k":15,"diff":"Hard","type":"spr","img":"bank/30aa51b7_q.png","e":"The vertices are (4, 5), (7, 1), (−1, −5), and (−4, −1). One side runs from (4, 5) to (7, 1), length √(3² + 4²) = 5. The adjacent side runs from (4, 5) to (−4, −1), length √(8² + 6²) = 10. Area = 5 × 10 = 50.","ad":"50","a":50.0},{"id":"8493fd10","k":18,"diff":"Hard","type":"mc","img":"bank/8493fd10_q.png","e":"Complete the square: (x + √t/2)² + (y − 1/2)² = 65 + t/4 + 1/4. Set r² = 83: t/4 = 17.75, so t = 71.","cimg":["bank/8493fd10_A.png","bank/8493fd10_B.png","bank/8493fd10_C.png","bank/8493fd10_D.png"],"a":1},{"id":"2757549e","k":17,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":"bank/2757549e_q.png","e":"Since BC ∥ DE, angle x equals angle E. AD = √(245² − 147²) = 196, so tan x = AD/DE = 196/147.","cimg":["bank/2757549e_A.png","bank/2757549e_B.png","bank/2757549e_C.png","bank/2757549e_D.png"],"a":2},{"id":"c4a9c94d","k":17,"diff":"Hard","type":"spr","img":"bank/c4a9c94d_q.png","e":"Angle CAD equals angle B (both are complementary to angle BAD). In right triangle ABD, tan B = AD/BD, so AD = 1.3 × 5 = 6.5.","ad":"6.5","a":6.5},{"id":"f389569d","k":17,"diff":"Hard","type":"mc","img":"bank/f389569d_q.png","e":"Height = (√3/2)s, so (√3/2)s = 39√3 gives s = 78. Perimeter = 3 × 78 = 234.","cimg":["bank/f389569d_A.png","bank/f389569d_B.png","bank/f389569d_C.png","bank/f389569d_D.png"],"a":2},{"id":"e3158182","k":17,"diff":"Hard","type":"mc","img":"bank/e3158182_q.png","e":"sin p = cos t means p and t are complementary: p = π/2 − t. g(0) = p(8)^0 + 6t = p + 6t = π/2 − t + 6t = 5t + π/2.","cimg":["bank/e3158182_A.png","bank/e3158182_B.png","bank/e3158182_C.png","bank/e3158182_D.png"],"a":3},{"id":"267f82b5","k":18,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":"bank/267f82b5_q.png","e":"The center is (19, 17), and r² = 64k², so r = 8k (k > 0).","cimg":["bank/267f82b5_A.png","bank/267f82b5_B.png","bank/267f82b5_C.png","bank/267f82b5_D.png"],"a":1},{"id":"179edb12","k":15,"diff":"Hard","type":"spr","img":"bank/179edb12_q.png","e":"r = 18/2 = 9. V = (1/3)πr²h = (1/3)π(81)(22) = 594π, so n = 594.","ad":"594","a":594.0},{"id":"b5d62bba","k":16,"diff":"Hard","type":"mc","img":"bank/b5d62bba_q.png","e":"LM ∥ PQ makes triangles LMR and QPR similar, with ratio RP/MR = 14/8 = 7/4. Areas scale by (7/4)² = 49/16, so the area is 36 × 49/16 = 441/4.","cimg":["bank/b5d62bba_A.png","bank/b5d62bba_B.png","bank/b5d62bba_C.png","bank/b5d62bba_D.png"],"a":3},{"id":"c8ab85ad","k":15,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":"bank/c8ab85ad_q.png","e":"The area of a square is side², so the area is 35².","cimg":["bank/c8ab85ad_A.png","bank/c8ab85ad_B.png","bank/c8ab85ad_C.png","bank/c8ab85ad_D.png"],"a":3},{"id":"98e02472","k":17,"diff":"Hard","type":"spr","img":"bank/98e02472_q.png","e":"The right angle is at Y. In triangle XYR, angle XYR = 90° − X, which equals angle Z. So b = a. sin a = 12/13 gives a 5-12-13 triangle, so tan b = 12/5 = 2.4.","ad":"2.4","a":2.4},{"id":"e6c557f9","k":15,"diff":"Hard","type":"mc","img":"bank/e6c557f9_q.png","e":"Surface area scales with the square of the edge length: n = (3/88)² = 9/7,744.","cimg":["bank/e6c557f9_A.png","bank/e6c557f9_B.png","bank/e6c557f9_C.png","bank/e6c557f9_D.png"],"a":0},{"id":"4a141e77","k":16,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":"bank/4a141e77_q.png","e":"The x° angle and the 72° angle are vertical angles, so x = 72.","cimg":["bank/4a141e77_A.png","bank/4a141e77_B.png","bank/4a141e77_C.png","bank/4a141e77_D.png"],"a":1},{"id":"7ce2e728","k":16,"diff":"Hard","type":"mc","img":"bank/7ce2e728_q.png","e":"With B = G, a second pair of equal angles (I or II) proves similarity by AA. Statement III gives two proportional sides, but angle B is not the angle between AB and AC, so it does not establish SAS.","cimg":["bank/7ce2e728_A.png","bank/7ce2e728_B.png","bank/7ce2e728_C.png","bank/7ce2e728_D.png"],"a":1},{"id":"f3f06c3a","k":15,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":"bank/f3f06c3a_q.png","e":"Area = xy = 7 × 5 = 35.","cimg":["bank/f3f06c3a_A.png","bank/f3f06c3a_B.png","bank/f3f06c3a_C.png","bank/f3f06c3a_D.png"],"a":2},{"id":"a5ff1a96","k":18,"diff":"Hard","type":"mc","img":"bank/a5ff1a96_q.png","e":"Circle M has center (4, 5) and r = 3. Circle P has r = 6, so r² = 36: (x − 4)² + (y − 5)² = 36.","cimg":["bank/a5ff1a96_A.png","bank/a5ff1a96_B.png","bank/a5ff1a96_C.png","bank/a5ff1a96_D.png"],"a":1},{"id":"186fdbca","k":18,"diff":"Easy","type":"spr","img":"bank/186fdbca_q.png","e":"The radius is half the diameter: 12.6 / 2 = 6.3.","ad":"6.3","a":6.3},{"id":"73e1b793","k":15,"diff":"Hard","type":"spr","img":"bank/73e1b793_q.png","e":"The volume ratio is 972/36 = 27, so the length ratio is ∛27 = 3. The edge of Q is 12/3 = 4.","ad":"4","a":4.0},{"id":"cab8f907","k":15,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":"bank/cab8f907_q.png","e":"Area = (1/2)(9)(4) = 18.","cimg":["bank/cab8f907_A.png","bank/cab8f907_B.png","bank/cab8f907_C.png","bank/cab8f907_D.png"],"a":0},{"id":"9fdc4eaa","k":15,"diff":"Hard","type":"mc","img":"bank/9fdc4eaa_q.png","e":"Base area = 70,560 − 38,160 = 32,400, so the base side is 180. Each lateral face has area 38,160/4 = 9,540 = (1/2)(180)(slant), so the slant height is 106. Height = √(106² − 90²) = √3,136 = 56.","cimg":["bank/9fdc4eaa_A.png","bank/9fdc4eaa_B.png","bank/9fdc4eaa_C.png","bank/9fdc4eaa_D.png"],"a":0},{"id":"f6ca90cc","k":15,"diff":"Hard","type":"spr","img":"bank/f6ca90cc_q.png","e":"V = base area × height = 10² × 58 = 5,800.","ad":"5800","a":5800.0},{"id":"7a11ceea","k":16,"diff":"Hard","type":"mc","img":"bank/7a11ceea_q.png","e":"Angles ACB and DCE are vertical angles, and angle A = 90°. Statement I alone gives only angles (AA), which proves similarity but not congruence. Statement II alone gives AC = DC but no second angle at D. Together they would give ASA, but neither is sufficient by itself.","cimg":["bank/7a11ceea_A.png","bank/7a11ceea_B.png","bank/7a11ceea_C.png","bank/7a11ceea_D.png"],"a":3},{"id":"25cc5327","k":15,"diff":"Medium","type":"spr","img":"bank/25cc5327_q.png","e":"V = (1/3)(27)(2)(7) = 126.","ad":"126","a":126.0},{"id":"858809e7","k":16,"diff":"Hard","type":"mc","img":"bank/858809e7_q.png","e":"EG ∥ CD, so triangle AEF ~ triangle ACD with ratio EF/CD = 0.5, which makes F the midpoint of AD. Triangle DFG ~ triangle DAB with ratio DF/DA = 0.5, so FG = 0.5AB (II is true). Then AB = 2(2.25CD) = 4.5CD = 9EF, so I is false. EF/FG = 2/9 but AF/FD = 1, so III is false.","cimg":["bank/858809e7_A.png","bank/858809e7_B.png","bank/858809e7_C.png","bank/858809e7_D.png"],"a":1},{"id":"de9148c4","k":17,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":"bank/de9148c4_q.png","e":"By the Pythagorean theorem, the legs squared sum to the hypotenuse squared: 12² + 3² = c².","cimg":["bank/de9148c4_A.png","bank/de9148c4_B.png","bank/de9148c4_C.png","bank/de9148c4_D.png"],"a":2},{"id":"4fb972f2","k":17,"diff":"Hard","type":"spr","img":"bank/4fb972f2_q.png","e":"RS² = SQ² − QR² = 16(82) − 16 = 1,296, so RS = 36.","ad":"36","a":36.0},{"id":"d21270da","k":16,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":"bank/d21270da_q.png","e":"The 24° angle and the x° angle are alternate interior angles. If x = 24, they are congruent, so r ∥ s.","cimg":["bank/d21270da_A.png","bank/d21270da_B.png","bank/d21270da_C.png","bank/d21270da_D.png"],"a":1},{"id":"149021da","k":18,"diff":"Hard","type":"spr","img":"bank/149021da_q.png","e":"Arc length = (45/360)(2πr) = πr/4. Setting πr/4 = 4π gives r = 16.","ad":"16","a":16.0},{"id":"11301fb6","k":18,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":"bank/11301fb6_q.png","e":"To convert radians to degrees, multiply by 180°/π: −(5/6)π · (180°/π).","cimg":["bank/11301fb6_A.png","bank/11301fb6_B.png","bank/11301fb6_C.png","bank/11301fb6_D.png"],"a":1},{"id":"697b3954","k":16,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":"bank/697b3954_q.png","e":"Corresponding parts: AB ↔ BD and BC ↔ DE. So BD = r = 54 and BC = s = 26, and CD = BD − BC = 54 − 26 = 28.","cimg":["bank/697b3954_A.png","bank/697b3954_B.png","bank/697b3954_C.png","bank/697b3954_D.png"],"a":2},{"id":"4757123b","k":15,"diff":"Hard","type":"spr","img":"bank/4757123b_q.png","e":"Areas of similar figures scale by the square of the length ratio: 41² = 1,681.","ad":"1681","a":1681.0},{"id":"ffc39dc5","k":16,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":"bank/ffc39dc5_q.png","e":"Both pairs of opposite sides are congruent, so CDEF is a parallelogram and DC ∥ FE. Alternate interior angles give ∠CDF = ∠DFE = y = 30°. So ∠CDE = 65° + 30° = 95°.","cimg":["bank/ffc39dc5_A.png","bank/ffc39dc5_B.png","bank/ffc39dc5_C.png","bank/ffc39dc5_D.png"],"a":2},{"id":"8364487a","k":16,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":"bank/8364487a_q.png","e":"A dilation preserves angle measures, so angle V′ = angle V = 25°.","cimg":["bank/8364487a_A.png","bank/8364487a_B.png","bank/8364487a_C.png","bank/8364487a_D.png"],"a":0},{"id":"17049054","k":15,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":"bank/17049054_q.png","e":"Square X has area 9² = 81. The total area is 81 + 32 = 113.","cimg":["bank/17049054_A.png","bank/17049054_B.png","bank/17049054_C.png","bank/17049054_D.png"],"a":1},{"id":"42155bac","k":15,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":"bank/42155bac_q.png","e":"V = base area × height, so h = 2,187/81 = 27.","cimg":["bank/42155bac_A.png","bank/42155bac_B.png","bank/42155bac_C.png","bank/42155bac_D.png"],"a":0},{"id":"1b687ae3","k":15,"diff":"Medium","type":"spr","img":"bank/1b687ae3_q.png","e":"A = (1/2)bh, so 36 = (1/2)(b)(2) and b = 36.","ad":"36","a":36.0},{"id":"0013adbd","k":16,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":"bank/0013adbd_q.png","e":"The 134° angle and x° are same-side interior angles (both between the lines, left of t). If x = 46, they sum to 180°, so j ∥ k. w = 134 is always true (vertical angles), y = 46 or z = 134 would mean the lines are not parallel.","cimg":["bank/0013adbd_A.png","bank/0013adbd_B.png","bank/0013adbd_C.png","bank/0013adbd_D.png"],"a":0},{"id":"1dacfb94","k":16,"diff":"Hard","type":"spr","img":"bank/1dacfb94_q.png","e":"BF is the axis of symmetry, so F is the midpoint of AC and BF ⊥ AC. Since AO = BO, ∠BAO = ∠ABO; combined with ∠OAF = 30° this forces ∠BAC = 60°, so ABC is equilateral with side 81. Then BO = AO = 27√3 and BF = 81√3/2, so BO/BF = 2/3. DE ∥ AC, so BE = (2/3)(81) = 54.","ad":"54","a":54.0},{"id":"10e059a6","k":18,"diff":"Hard","type":"mc","img":"bank/10e059a6_q.png","e":"B = 36 · π/216 = π/6, and cos(π/6) = √3/2.","cimg":["bank/10e059a6_A.png","bank/10e059a6_B.png","bank/10e059a6_C.png","bank/10e059a6_D.png"],"a":3},{"id":"9f9112ab","k":18,"diff":"Hard","type":"spr","img":"bank/9f9112ab_q.png","e":"60° = 60 · π/180 = π/3 radians, so n = 3.","ad":"3","a":3.0},{"id":"6c67dd47","k":17,"diff":"Hard","type":"mc","img":"bank/6c67dd47_q.png","e":"The height from Z is XZ sin 54° = 19 sin 54°. Area = (1/2)(26)(19 sin 54°) = 247 sin 54°.","cimg":["bank/6c67dd47_A.png","bank/6c67dd47_B.png","bank/6c67dd47_C.png","bank/6c67dd47_D.png"],"a":2},{"id":"27f1db42","k":18,"diff":"Hard","type":"spr","img":"bank/27f1db42_q.png","e":"Circle F has r = 5, so circle G has r = 7 and p = 7² = 49.","ad":"49","a":49.0},{"id":"44d67c6c","k":18,"diff":"Hard","type":"spr","img":"bank/44d67c6c_q.png","e":"Circle A: (x − 5)² + (y − 4)² = 41 + 14n. Circle B has the same center and r_B² = (11 − 5)² + (8 − 4)² = 52. Since r_B = 2r_A, r_A² = 52/4 = 13, so 41 + 14n = 13 and n = −2.","ad":"-2","a":-2.0},{"id":"28ff3966","k":9,"diff":"Hard","type":"mc","img":"bank/28ff3966_q.png","e":"The original side represents 55 × 19 = 1,045 miles. The new side is 55 × 1.65 = 90.75 inches, so 1 inch represents 1,045/90.75 ≈ 11.52 miles.","cimg":["bank/28ff3966_A.png","bank/28ff3966_B.png","bank/28ff3966_C.png","bank/28ff3966_D.png"],"a":1},{"id":"3e1bd4e2","k":13,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":"bank/3e1bd4e2_q.png","e":"The margin of error is the distance from the mean to either end of the interval: 17.32 − 16.59 = 0.73.","cimg":["bank/3e1bd4e2_A.png","bank/3e1bd4e2_B.png","bank/3e1bd4e2_C.png","bank/3e1bd4e2_D.png"],"a":0},{"id":"f6c18a66","k":10,"diff":"Hard","type":"mc","img":"bank/f6c18a66_q.png","e":"Set A (11 values) in order: 0, 0, 3, 3, 4, 4, 5, 5, 6, 7, 13, so the median is the 6th value, 4. Set B (10 values) has median (4 + 4)/2 = 4. The medians are equal.","cimg":["bank/f6c18a66_A.png","bank/f6c18a66_B.png","bank/f6c18a66_C.png","bank/f6c18a66_D.png"],"a":2},{"id":"d73a67d7","k":10,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":"bank/d73a67d7_q.png","e":"Choice D's values are clustered most tightly around the mean (three 54s, with 53 and 55), so it has the smallest standard deviation.","cimg":["bank/d73a67d7_A.png","bank/d73a67d7_B.png","bank/d73a67d7_C.png","bank/d73a67d7_D.png"],"a":3},{"id":"89ff6a0a","k":12,"diff":"Hard","type":"spr","img":"bank/89ff6a0a_q.png","e":"Excluding group 2 leaves 12 + 8 + 3 + 10 + 32 + 0 = 65 buttons. Of these, 12 + 8 + 10 + 32 = 62 have a diameter ≤ 30 mm. Probability = 62/65 ≈ 0.9538.","ad":"62/65","tol":0.0011,"a":0.9538461538461539},{"id":"8bb94668","k":9,"diff":"Hard","type":"mc","img":"bank/8bb94668_q.png","e":"a = 59c. c = 0.00008b, so b = c/0.00008 = 12,500c. a + b = 59c + 12,500c = 12,559c.","cimg":["bank/8bb94668_A.png","bank/8bb94668_B.png","bank/8bb94668_C.png","bank/8bb94668_D.png"],"a":3},{"id":"dbd89c59","k":11,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":"bank/dbd89c59_q.png","e":"The data start near 43 at x = 0 and increase, so the model is y = 43(1.04)^x (growth, not decay).","cimg":["bank/dbd89c59_A.png","bank/dbd89c59_B.png","bank/dbd89c59_C.png","bank/dbd89c59_D.png"],"a":1},{"id":"b3547a10","k":11,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":"bank/b3547a10_q.png","e":"The line rises about 60 seeds germinated for every 100 more seeds planted (slope ≈ 0.6). The slope is in seeds germinated per seed planted, not per day.","cimg":["bank/b3547a10_A.png","bank/b3547a10_B.png","bank/b3547a10_C.png","bank/b3547a10_D.png"],"a":2},{"id":"4c5ea142","k":8,"diff":"Hard","type":"mc","img":"bank/4c5ea142_q.png","e":"The rate is 87/m mm per month. k years = 12k months, so the growth is 87(12k)/m = 1,044k/m.","cimg":["bank/4c5ea142_A.png","bank/4c5ea142_B.png","bank/4c5ea142_C.png","bank/4c5ea142_D.png"],"a":3},{"id":"1b96c116","k":8,"diff":"Hard","type":"mc","img":"bank/1b96c116_q.png","e":"1 square foot = 12 × 12 = 144 square inches, so 3,168/144 = 22 square feet.","cimg":["bank/1b96c116_A.png","bank/1b96c116_B.png","bank/1b96c116_C.png","bank/1b96c116_D.png"],"a":0},{"id":"2bab1399","k":13,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":"bank/2bab1399_q.png","e":"A larger random sample gives a more precise estimate, so the margin of error is likely to be lower. The sample size doesn't push the average up or down.","cimg":["bank/2bab1399_A.png","bank/2bab1399_B.png","bank/2bab1399_C.png","bank/2bab1399_D.png"],"a":0},{"id":"f496d2c0","k":12,"diff":"Hard","type":"mc","img":"bank/f496d2c0_q.png","e":"At least 18 seats covers 21% + 29% + 24% = 74% of rooms. P(greater than 65 | at least 18) = 24/74 ≈ 0.32.","cimg":["bank/f496d2c0_A.png","bank/f496d2c0_B.png","bank/f496d2c0_C.png","bank/f496d2c0_D.png"],"a":1},{"id":"da978ee6","k":13,"diff":"Hard","type":"mc","img":"bank/da978ee6_q.png","e":"Doubling the sample size reduces the margin of error, so it is less than 2.13%.","cimg":["bank/da978ee6_A.png","bank/da978ee6_B.png","bank/da978ee6_C.png","bank/da978ee6_D.png"],"a":3},{"id":"6feae9c3","k":9,"diff":"Hard","type":"mc","img":"bank/6feae9c3_q.png","e":"Percent increase = (3.49t − t)/t × 100% = 249%.","cimg":["bank/6feae9c3_A.png","bank/6feae9c3_B.png","bank/6feae9c3_C.png","bank/6feae9c3_D.png"],"a":2},{"id":"559476f4","k":10,"diff":"Easy","type":"spr","img":"bank/559476f4_q.png","e":"The bar for data value 2 reaches a frequency of 6.","ad":"6","a":6.0},{"id":"70a2776f","k":11,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":"bank/70a2776f_q.png","e":"The temperature drops about 10 degrees over about 60 meters, a slope of roughly −0.17.","cimg":["bank/70a2776f_A.png","bank/70a2776f_B.png","bank/70a2776f_C.png","bank/70a2776f_D.png"],"a":0},{"id":"cf2be18d","k":10,"diff":"Hard","type":"mc","img":"bank/cf2be18d_q.png","e":"There are 7 values, so the median is the 4th value: b = 29. The mean is 36, so the sum is 252 and a + c = 252 − (26 + 29 + 29 + 31 + 47) = 90. The range is c − a = 72. Solving gives c = 81.","cimg":["bank/cf2be18d_A.png","bank/cf2be18d_B.png","bank/cf2be18d_C.png","bank/cf2be18d_D.png"],"a":2},{"id":"de799680","k":8,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":"bank/de799680_q.png","e":"76 cm/s × 10 mm/cm = 760 mm/s.","cimg":["bank/de799680_A.png","bank/de799680_B.png","bank/de799680_C.png","bank/de799680_D.png"],"a":2},{"id":"98818acf","k":9,"diff":"Hard","type":"spr","img":"bank/98818acf_q.png","e":"A 131% increase multiplies by 1 + 1.31 = 2.31, so b = 2.31.","ad":"2.31","a":2.31},{"id":"f01108a8","k":7,"diff":"Hard","type":"mc","img":"bank/f01108a8_q.png","e":"a/7 > 1, so 9(a/7)^(x+c) is an increasing exponential that takes every positive value exactly once. Subtracting b > 0 moves the asymptote to y = −b, so the graph crosses the x-axis exactly once.","cimg":["bank/f01108a8_A.png","bank/f01108a8_B.png","bank/f01108a8_C.png","bank/f01108a8_D.png"],"a":1},{"id":"71b74a44","k":7,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":"bank/71b74a44_q.png","e":"At purchase, x = 0, and y = 7,400(0.87)^0 = 7,400.","cimg":["bank/71b74a44_A.png","bank/71b74a44_B.png","bank/71b74a44_C.png","bank/71b74a44_D.png"],"a":2},{"id":"46308566","k":6,"diff":"Hard","type":"spr","img":"bank/46308566_q.png","e":"Rewrite as r² + (q − 2)r + 55 = 0. There are no real solutions when the discriminant is negative: (q − 2)² < 220. Since 14² = 196 < 220 < 225 = 15², q − 2 ≤ 14, so the largest integer is q = 16.","ad":"16","a":16.0},{"id":"38c90632","k":5,"diff":"Hard","type":"spr","img":"bank/38c90632_q.png","e":"p(x + 51) + wx = 29x + 102. Constants: 51p = 102, so p = 2. x-terms: p + w = 29, so w = 27.","ad":"27","a":27.0},{"id":"3cf2698e","k":7,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":"bank/3cf2698e_q.png","e":"The count starts at 830 and doubles every 25 minutes: f(x) = 830(2)^(x/25).","cimg":["bank/3cf2698e_A.png","bank/3cf2698e_B.png","bank/3cf2698e_C.png","bank/3cf2698e_D.png"],"a":1},{"id":"e833de9a","k":6,"diff":"Hard","type":"mc","img":"bank/e833de9a_q.png","e":"At x = −5, 25 + y² = 36 and y < 0, so y = −√11. Substitute into the line: −√11 = −5m + b/4, so b = 20m − 4√11.","cimg":["bank/e833de9a_A.png","bank/e833de9a_B.png","bank/e833de9a_C.png","bank/e833de9a_D.png"],"a":3},{"id":"58b4c6f3","k":7,"diff":"Hard","type":"mc","img":"bank/58b4c6f3_q.png","e":"h(0) = 1 + b = 10, so b = 9. h(2) = a² + 9 = 13, so a = 2 (a > 0). ab = 18.","cimg":["bank/58b4c6f3_A.png","bank/58b4c6f3_B.png","bank/58b4c6f3_C.png","bank/58b4c6f3_D.png"],"a":1},{"id":"7bbfbe70","k":7,"diff":"Hard","type":"mc","img":"bank/7bbfbe70_q.png","e":"A 24% decrease leaves 76% each period, so the factor is 0.76, and the exponent t/22.96 counts the 22.96-minute periods.","cimg":["bank/7bbfbe70_A.png","bank/7bbfbe70_B.png","bank/7bbfbe70_C.png","bank/7bbfbe70_D.png"],"a":3},{"id":"5da5c665","k":6,"diff":"Hard","type":"mc","img":"bank/5da5c665_q.png","e":"By the quadratic formula, x = (5 ± √(25 + 80))/8 = (5 ± √105)/8. The greatest solution is 5/8 + √105/8.","cimg":["bank/5da5c665_A.png","bank/5da5c665_B.png","bank/5da5c665_C.png","bank/5da5c665_D.png"],"a":1},{"id":"a1e65979","k":7,"diff":"Hard","type":"mc","img":"bank/a1e65979_q.png","e":"f(x) = k(x − 1)² + 9 and f(2) = k + 9 = 33, so k = 24. f(−2) = 24(9) + 9 = 225 and f(0) = 24 + 9 = 33, so the difference is 192.","cimg":["bank/a1e65979_A.png","bank/a1e65979_B.png","bank/a1e65979_C.png","bank/a1e65979_D.png"],"a":2},{"id":"00165291","k":5,"diff":"Hard","type":"spr","img":"bank/00165291_q.png","e":"Expanding (3x² + a)(2x² + b) requires ab = 35 and 3b + 2a = 31. The integer solution is a = 5, b = 7. For the other factorization, cd = 35 and 3d + 2c = 31 give 3d² − 31d + 70 = 0, so d = 10/3 and c = 21/2. a + c = 5 + 10.5 = 15.5.","ad":"15.5","a":15.5},{"id":"6bd40794","k":6,"diff":"Medium","type":"spr","img":"bank/6bd40794_q.png","e":"Set each factor equal to 0: x = 16, 10, −7, or −17. The positive solutions are 10 and 16 (either is accepted).","ad":"10 or 16","a":10.0,"alts":[10.0,16.0]},{"id":"c8db0e19","k":6,"diff":"Hard","type":"mc","img":"bank/c8db0e19_q.png","e":"Multiply both sides by y: 1/(4x) + xy²z = 1/(3z). Then xy²z = (4x − 3z)/(12xz), so y² = (4x − 3z)/(12x²z²). Take the positive square root.","cimg":["bank/c8db0e19_A.png","bank/c8db0e19_B.png","bank/c8db0e19_C.png","bank/c8db0e19_D.png"],"a":1},{"id":"5f10c095","k":6,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":"bank/5f10c095_q.png","e":"The parabola has zeros at 2 and 8 and vertex (5, 8), so y = −(8/9)(x − 2)(x − 8). The horizontal line is at y = 64/9 ≈ 7.1, which meets the parabola at x = 4 and x = 6. Of the choices, only 4 is possible.","cimg":["bank/5f10c095_A.png","bank/5f10c095_B.png","bank/5f10c095_C.png","bank/5f10c095_D.png"],"a":0},{"id":"5acbdc30","k":7,"diff":"Hard","type":"mc","img":"bank/5acbdc30_q.png","e":"Each step multiplies by 0.19, which is 19% of the previous value, an 81% decrease. p = 81.","cimg":["bank/5acbdc30_A.png","bank/5acbdc30_B.png","bank/5acbdc30_C.png","bank/5acbdc30_D.png"],"a":3},{"id":"c95686e9","k":7,"diff":"Hard","type":"spr","img":"bank/c95686e9_q.png","e":"h(0) = b = 19.36. Setting −16t² + 19.36 = 0 gives t² = 1.21, so t = 1.1.","ad":"1.1","a":1.1},{"id":"769b612d","k":7,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":"bank/769b612d_q.png","e":"10,000 = 10^4, so 5x − 8 = 4 and x = 12/5.","cimg":["bank/769b612d_A.png","bank/769b612d_B.png","bank/769b612d_C.png","bank/769b612d_D.png"],"a":1},{"id":"7bf77c19","k":7,"diff":"Hard","type":"mc","img":"bank/7bf77c19_q.png","e":"p(0) = a + b and r(0) = a(4.1)^b. Neither value appears by itself as a single constant or coefficient in either equation.","cimg":["bank/7bf77c19_A.png","bank/7bf77c19_B.png","bank/7bf77c19_C.png","bank/7bf77c19_D.png"],"a":3},{"id":"f123e039","k":6,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":"bank/f123e039_q.png","e":"The line passes through the origin with a positive slope of 5, so y = 5x. The parabola has vertex (0, −8) and passes through (±3, 1), so y = x² − 8.","cimg":["bank/f123e039_A.png","bank/f123e039_B.png","bank/f123e039_C.png","bank/f123e039_D.png"],"a":3},{"id":"04887c7b","k":5,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":"bank/04887c7b_q.png","e":"(2x + 3)(7x − 2) = 14x² + 17x − 6. Subtracting 5x + 6 gives 14x² + 12x − 12, so b = 12.","cimg":["bank/04887c7b_A.png","bank/04887c7b_B.png","bank/04887c7b_C.png","bank/04887c7b_D.png"],"a":1},{"id":"91aa9aa9","k":5,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":"bank/91aa9aa9_q.png","e":"9x² + 6 − 8x² = x² + 6.","cimg":["bank/91aa9aa9_A.png","bank/91aa9aa9_B.png","bank/91aa9aa9_C.png","bank/91aa9aa9_D.png"],"a":3},{"id":"f8871ccd","k":5,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":"bank/f8871ccd_q.png","e":"2(x − 9/2) = 2x − 9, and (2x − 9)(x + 8) = 2x² + 16x − 9x − 72 = 2x² + 7x − 72.","cimg":["bank/f8871ccd_A.png","bank/f8871ccd_B.png","bank/f8871ccd_C.png","bank/f8871ccd_D.png"],"a":1},{"id":"9a1f1941","k":6,"diff":"Hard","type":"mc","img":"bank/9a1f1941_q.png","e":"An absolute value can never be negative, so |4x − 3| = −9 has no solutions.","cimg":["bank/9a1f1941_A.png","bank/9a1f1941_B.png","bank/9a1f1941_C.png","bank/9a1f1941_D.png"],"a":0},{"id":"30596346","k":6,"diff":"Hard","type":"spr","img":"bank/30596346_q.png","e":"The solutions are x = k, 4, and −4. Their sum is k = 59.","ad":"59","a":59.0},{"id":"fe62f031","k":7,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":"bank/fe62f031_q.png","e":"Shifting a graph up 4 units adds 4 to the output: g(x) = 3x⁵ + 4.","cimg":["bank/fe62f031_A.png","bank/fe62f031_B.png","bank/fe62f031_C.png","bank/fe62f031_D.png"],"a":0},{"id":"efc469c4","k":5,"diff":"Hard","type":"mc","img":"bank/efc469c4_q.png","e":"At x = 1, the rewritten form equals (a + b + c)/6. The original at x = 1 is −14(9) + 6(4) = −102, so a + b + c = 6(−102) = −612.","cimg":["bank/efc469c4_A.png","bank/efc469c4_B.png","bank/efc469c4_C.png","bank/efc469c4_D.png"],"a":0},{"id":"2289b199","k":5,"diff":"Hard","type":"mc","img":"bank/2289b199_q.png","e":"The expression equals n^(17/3) p^(5/3) / (5n² · p) = n^(11/3) p^(2/3) / 5. Expression I simplifies to the same thing (subtract exponents), and II is ∛(n¹¹p²)/5 = n^(11/3) p^(2/3)/5. Both are equivalent.","cimg":["bank/2289b199_A.png","bank/2289b199_B.png","bank/2289b199_C.png","bank/2289b199_D.png"],"a":2},{"id":"d4572f55","k":1,"diff":"Hard","type":"mc","img":"bank/d4572f55_q.png","e":"y increases by 23 each time x increases by 17, so the slope is 23/17. At x = 0, y = t + 46, so y = (23/17)x + t + 46.","cimg":["bank/d4572f55_A.png","bank/d4572f55_B.png","bank/d4572f55_C.png","bank/d4572f55_D.png"],"a":3},{"id":"107d0c62","k":2,"diff":"Hard","type":"spr","img":"bank/107d0c62_q.png","e":"0.10(90) + 0.20y = 0.17(90 + y), so 9 + 0.20y = 15.3 + 0.17y. Then 0.03y = 6.3 and y = 210.","ad":"210","a":210.0},{"id":"55ea0659","k":0,"diff":"Hard","type":"mc","img":"bank/55ea0659_q.png","e":"Rearranged, the equation is x(r − 28) = 23. If r = 28 there is no solution; otherwise there is exactly one. So r cannot be 28.","cimg":["bank/55ea0659_A.png","bank/55ea0659_B.png","bank/55ea0659_C.png","bank/55ea0659_D.png"],"a":3},{"id":"59813abf","k":3,"diff":"Hard","type":"mc","img":"bank/59813abf_q.png","e":"Dividing by 38 gives x − y = 2n. For no solution, the second line must be parallel but different: x − y = c with c ≠ 2n. 4x − 4y = 4n means x − y = n, which works. (Choice A is the same line.)","cimg":["bank/59813abf_A.png","bank/59813abf_B.png","bank/59813abf_C.png","bank/59813abf_D.png"],"a":3},{"id":"088bc84e","k":0,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":"bank/088bc84e_q.png","e":"Divide both sides by 2: 5x = 3.","cimg":["bank/088bc84e_A.png","bank/088bc84e_B.png","bank/088bc84e_C.png","bank/088bc84e_D.png"],"a":2},{"id":"f8fa0cf0","k":0,"diff":"Medium","type":"spr","img":"bank/f8fa0cf0_q.png","e":"9r = 7r + 49, so 2r = 49 and r = 24.5.","ad":"24.5","a":24.5},{"id":"30b1e186","k":4,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":"bank/30b1e186_q.png","e":"If x < 0 and y > 0, then 5x − 7y is negative, so it can never exceed 35.","cimg":["bank/30b1e186_A.png","bank/30b1e186_B.png","bank/30b1e186_C.png","bank/30b1e186_D.png"],"a":3},{"id":"1a2a0f59","k":1,"diff":"Hard","type":"mc","img":"bank/1a2a0f59_q.png","e":"Session 1 costs $0, session 2 costs $12.70, and the other x − 2 sessions cost $25.40 each: f(x) = 25.40(x − 2) + 12.70.","cimg":["bank/1a2a0f59_A.png","bank/1a2a0f59_B.png","bank/1a2a0f59_C.png","bank/1a2a0f59_D.png"],"a":1},{"id":"d914abec","k":4,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":"bank/d914abec_q.png","e":"17 + 10x > 20 + 9.5x, so 0.5x > 3 and x > 6.","cimg":["bank/d914abec_A.png","bank/d914abec_B.png","bank/d914abec_C.png","bank/d914abec_D.png"],"a":3},{"id":"ea8bd66f","k":3,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":"bank/ea8bd66f_q.png","e":"Substitute: 5x − 12x = −14, so x = 2 and y = 8. x + y = 10.","cimg":["bank/ea8bd66f_A.png","bank/ea8bd66f_B.png","bank/ea8bd66f_C.png","bank/ea8bd66f_D.png"],"a":3},{"id":"590d662d","k":1,"diff":"Hard","type":"spr","img":"bank/590d662d_q.png","e":"At x = 0 Mary had walked 150 m, and at x = 10 she had walked 650 m. In those 10 minutes she walked 650 − 150 = 500 m.","ad":"500","a":500.0},{"id":"fc4a0d2a","k":1,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":"bank/fc4a0d2a_q.png","e":"g(0) = 3(−15) = −45, so y = g(0) − 2 = −47.","cimg":["bank/fc4a0d2a_A.png","bank/fc4a0d2a_B.png","bank/fc4a0d2a_C.png","bank/fc4a0d2a_D.png"],"a":0},{"id":"5e9b6079","k":3,"diff":"Hard","type":"mc","img":"bank/5e9b6079_q.png","e":"No solution requires the same slope (7) with a different intercept. −7x + y = 21 is y = 7x + 21.","cimg":["bank/5e9b6079_A.png","bank/5e9b6079_B.png","bank/5e9b6079_C.png","bank/5e9b6079_D.png"],"a":2},{"id":"18ac8354","k":3,"diff":"Hard","type":"spr","img":"bank/18ac8354_q.png","e":"Line g passes through (−10, 12) and (0, 1), so its slope is −11/10 and y = −1.1x + 1. In standard form, 11x + 10y = 10; multiplying by 15 gives 165x + 150y = 150. So p = 150, w = 150, and p + w = 300.","ad":"300","a":300.0},{"id":"0e926898","k":3,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":"bank/0e926898_q.png","e":"s + c = 83 and 8.5s + 12c = 730. Substituting c = 83 − s gives 996 − 3.5s = 730, so s = 76.","cimg":["bank/0e926898_A.png","bank/0e926898_B.png","bank/0e926898_C.png","bank/0e926898_D.png"],"a":2},{"id":"2493c767","k":1,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":"bank/2493c767_q.png","e":"s(3) = 121 means that at x = 3 minutes, 121 spoons remained.","cimg":["bank/2493c767_A.png","bank/2493c767_B.png","bank/2493c767_C.png","bank/2493c767_D.png"],"a":2},{"id":"340afb12","k":3,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":"bank/340afb12_q.png","e":"Cost: 11x + 9y = 497. Bags: 24x + 16y = 968.","cimg":["bank/340afb12_A.png","bank/340afb12_B.png","bank/340afb12_C.png","bank/340afb12_D.png"],"a":2},{"id":"e8fd6d99","k":4,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":"bank/e8fd6d99_q.png","e":"Terry's total is 4 + x, which must be at least 16: 4 + x ≥ 16.","cimg":["bank/e8fd6d99_A.png","bank/e8fd6d99_B.png","bank/e8fd6d99_C.png","bank/e8fd6d99_D.png"],"a":3},{"id":"5eb4918d","k":0,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":"bank/5eb4918d_q.png","e":"90x + 40 = 10(9x + 4) = 10(67) = 670.","cimg":["bank/5eb4918d_A.png","bank/5eb4918d_B.png","bank/5eb4918d_C.png","bank/5eb4918d_D.png"],"a":3},{"id":"080e75c2","k":3,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":"bank/080e75c2_q.png","e":"One line starts at (0, 13) and falls to about (11, 11), a slope of −2/11. The other starts at (0, 7) and rises to (11, 11), a slope of 4/11.","cimg":["bank/080e75c2_A.png","bank/080e75c2_B.png","bank/080e75c2_C.png","bank/080e75c2_D.png"],"a":2},{"id":"935f3403","k":0,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":"bank/935f3403_q.png","e":"200 is multiplied by t, the number of monthly payments, so it is the amount of each payment. (2,800 is the down payment.)","cimg":["bank/935f3403_A.png","bank/935f3403_B.png","bank/935f3403_C.png","bank/935f3403_D.png"],"a":1},{"id":"0c490cd5","k":1,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":"bank/0c490cd5_q.png","e":"The flag starts at 110 in² and gains 64 in² per piece: y = 110 + 64x.","cimg":["bank/0c490cd5_A.png","bank/0c490cd5_B.png","bank/0c490cd5_C.png","bank/0c490cd5_D.png"],"a":2},{"id":"4722abd2","k":2,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":"bank/4722abd2_q.png","e":"Line p is y = −4x + 11/2, with slope −4. The perpendicular slope is the negative reciprocal, 1/4.","cimg":["bank/4722abd2_A.png","bank/4722abd2_B.png","bank/4722abd2_C.png","bank/4722abd2_D.png"],"a":2},{"id":"e10d8313","k":16,"diff":"Hard","type":"spr","img":"bank/e10d8313_q.png","e":"In triangle QXS, ∠QSX = 180 − 48 − 86 = 46°. ∠RWS = 180 − 85 = 95°, so in triangle RWS, ∠SRW = 180 − 46 − 95 = 39°. ∠RTU = 180 − 162 = 18°. In triangle RTU, ∠TUR = 180 − 39 − 18 = 123°.","ad":"123","a":123.0},{"id":"3e4e2ab0","k":16,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":"bank/3e4e2ab0_q.png","e":"y = 2(63) − 47 = 79. In triangle ABC, ∠B = 180 − 63 − 79 = 38°. AB ∥ DE makes ∠D and ∠B alternate interior angles, so z = 38.","cimg":["bank/3e4e2ab0_A.png","bank/3e4e2ab0_B.png","bank/3e4e2ab0_C.png","bank/3e4e2ab0_D.png"],"a":0},{"id":"f88f27e5","k":16,"diff":"Medium","type":"spr","img":"bank/f88f27e5_q.png","e":"The three lines form a triangle with interior angles 106° and 23°, so the third interior angle (where r and s meet) is 180 − 106 − 23 = 51°. The angle x forms a linear pair with it: x = 180 − 51 = 129.","ad":"129","a":129.0},{"id":"5207e508","k":16,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":"bank/5207e508_q.png","e":"m ∥ n, so the 170° angle and w° are corresponding angles (both below their line, left of t). w = 170.","cimg":["bank/5207e508_A.png","bank/5207e508_B.png","bank/5207e508_C.png","bank/5207e508_D.png"],"a":3},{"id":"f67e4efc","k":15,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":"bank/f67e4efc_q.png","e":"V = πr²h, so 45π = πr²(5), r² = 9, and r = 3.","cimg":["bank/f67e4efc_A.png","bank/f67e4efc_B.png","bank/f67e4efc_C.png","bank/f67e4efc_D.png"],"a":0},{"id":"bb560789","k":15,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":"bank/bb560789_q.png","e":"Square S has area 4² = 16. Total = 80 + 16 = 96.","cimg":["bank/bb560789_A.png","bank/bb560789_B.png","bank/bb560789_C.png","bank/bb560789_D.png"],"a":3},{"id":"5afbdc8e","k":15,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":"bank/5afbdc8e_q.png","e":"The circle's area is π(2)² = 4π, so the square's side is √(4π) = 2√π.","cimg":["bank/5afbdc8e_A.png","bank/5afbdc8e_B.png","bank/5afbdc8e_C.png","bank/5afbdc8e_D.png"],"a":2},{"id":"6d99b141","k":16,"diff":"Hard","type":"spr","img":["bank/6d99b141_stem.png"],"e":"Since AC = CD, triangle ACD is isosceles, so angles D and A are each (180° − 104°)/2 = 38°. In triangle DBE, angle DEB = 180° − 38° − 45° = 97°, so x = 180° − 97° = 83°.","ad":"83","a":83.0},{"id":"9912e19f","k":16,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/9912e19f_stem.png"],"e":"In congruent triangles, corresponding angles are equal. Angle J corresponds to angle E, so angle J = 45°.","cimg":[["bank/9912e19f_A.png"],["bank/9912e19f_B.png"],["bank/9912e19f_C.png"],["bank/9912e19f_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"4b7bb316","k":15,"diff":"Medium","type":"spr","img":["bank/4b7bb316_stem.png"],"e":"A box without a lid has 5 square faces. Each face has area 29² = 841, so the surface area is 5 × 841 = 4205 square inches.","ad":"4205","a":4205.0},{"id":"bcb66188","k":17,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/bcb66188_stem.png"],"e":"Similar triangles have equal corresponding angles, and angle J corresponds to angle F. So sin(J) = sin(F) = 308/317.","cimg":[["bank/bcb66188_A.png"],["bank/bcb66188_B.png"],["bank/bcb66188_C.png"],["bank/bcb66188_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"5ad6bc97","k":1,"diff":"Easy","type":"spr","img":["bank/5ad6bc97_stem.png"],"e":"Substitute x = 7: f(7) = 7 × 7 + 1 = 49 + 1 = 50.","ad":"50","a":50.0},{"id":"a8e6bd75","k":2,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/a8e6bd75_stem.png"],"e":"The line y = 2x − 5 has y-intercept −5 and a positive slope of 2. Only graph D crosses the y-axis at −5 and rises 2 units for every 1 unit to the right.","cimg":[["bank/a8e6bd75_A.png"],["bank/a8e6bd75_B.png"],["bank/a8e6bd75_C.png"],["bank/a8e6bd75_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"948087f2","k":4,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/948087f2_stem.png"],"e":"Test (2, −1): −1 ≤ 3(2) + 1 = 7 is true, and 2 − (−1) = 3 > 1 is true. The other pairs fail x − y > 1.","cimg":[["bank/948087f2_A.png"],["bank/948087f2_B.png"],["bank/948087f2_C.png"],["bank/948087f2_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"00b9bd37","k":2,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/00b9bd37_stem.png"],"e":"The graph has intercepts (90, 0) and (0, 35). In 7x + 18y = 630, x = 90 gives 630 when y = 0 and y = 35 gives 630 when x = 0, so it matches.","cimg":[["bank/00b9bd37_A.png"],["bank/00b9bd37_B.png"],["bank/00b9bd37_C.png"],["bank/00b9bd37_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"73b3b7d8","k":3,"diff":"Medium","type":"spr","img":["bank/73b3b7d8_stem.png"],"e":"Add the equations to eliminate y: 0 = 15x − 10, so x = 2/3. Then 30x = 30 × 2/3 = 20.","ad":"20","a":20.0},{"id":"e5c57163","k":15,"diff":"Hard","type":"spr","img":["bank/e5c57163_stem.png"],"e":"When side lengths are multiplied by 166, area is multiplied by 166². So k = 166² = 27556.","ad":"27556","a":27556.0},{"id":"33e29881","k":17,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/33e29881_stem.png"],"e":"Angles R and S are complementary, and the cosine of an angle equals the sine of its complement. So cos(S) = sin(R) = √15/4.","cimg":[["bank/33e29881_A.png"],["bank/33e29881_B.png"],["bank/33e29881_C.png"],["bank/33e29881_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"93f48423","k":15,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/93f48423_stem.png"],"e":"Area of a rectangle is length × width = 7 × 6 = 42 square inches.","cimg":[["bank/93f48423_A.png"],["bank/93f48423_B.png"],["bank/93f48423_C.png"],["bank/93f48423_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"5252e606","k":15,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/5252e606_stem.png"],"e":"Area of a square is side² = 55² = 3,025 cm². Don't confuse this with perimeter (220) or 2 × 55 (110).","cimg":[["bank/5252e606_A.png"],["bank/5252e606_B.png"],["bank/5252e606_C.png"],["bank/5252e606_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"9342ca50","k":16,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/9342ca50_stem.png"],"e":"BC is parallel to AD and line t is a transversal, so angles x and y are alternate interior angles and are equal. So y = 22.","cimg":[["bank/9342ca50_A.png"],["bank/9342ca50_B.png"],["bank/9342ca50_C.png"],["bank/9342ca50_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"983412ea","k":15,"diff":"Medium","type":"spr","img":["bank/983412ea_stem.png"],"e":"Volume = base area × height, so base area = 2016 ÷ 14 = 144. The base is a square, so its edge is √144 = 12.","ad":"12","a":12.0},{"id":"a4c0547f","k":17,"diff":"Hard","type":"mc","img":["bank/a4c0547f_stem.png"],"e":"tan X = opposite/adjacent = YZ/XZ = 12/35, and YZ = 24, so XZ = 70. The hypotenuse is √(24² + 70²) = 74, so the perimeter is 24 + 70 + 74 = 168.","cimg":[["bank/a4c0547f_A.png"],["bank/a4c0547f_B.png"],["bank/a4c0547f_C.png"],["bank/a4c0547f_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"659cb706","k":17,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/659cb706_stem.png"],"e":"sin X = opposite/hypotenuse = ZY/XY = 35/XY. cos Y = adjacent/hypotenuse = ZY/XY = 35/XY, so cos Y equals sin X.","cimg":[["bank/659cb706_A.png"],["bank/659cb706_B.png"],["bank/659cb706_C.png"],["bank/659cb706_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"c8d60e48","k":16,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/c8d60e48_stem.png"],"e":"Since AB = AC, the base angles are equal: angle ACB = angle ABC = 67°. So x = 180 − 67 − 67 = 46.","cimg":[["bank/c8d60e48_A.png"],["bank/c8d60e48_B.png"],["bank/c8d60e48_C.png"],["bank/c8d60e48_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"947a3cde","k":16,"diff":"Hard","type":"spr","img":["bank/947a3cde_stem.png"],"e":"The 60° angle is angle QPR, so its supplement angle MPR = 180° − 60° = 120°. Triangle MPR is isosceles with MP = PR, so angle PMR = (180° − 120°)/2 = 30°, and angle QMR is that same angle.","ad":"30","a":30.0},{"id":"1f0b582e","k":15,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/1f0b582e_stem.png"],"e":"The perimeter of square X is 4 × 12 = 48, so square Y has perimeter 2 × 48 = 96. Each side of Y is 96 ÷ 4 = 24 cm.","cimg":[["bank/1f0b582e_A.png"],["bank/1f0b582e_B.png"],["bank/1f0b582e_C.png"],["bank/1f0b582e_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"deff8a2f","k":15,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/deff8a2f_stem.png"],"e":"Circumference 2πr = 20π gives r = 10. Volume = πr²h = π(10²)(6) = 600π cubic meters.","cimg":[["bank/deff8a2f_A.png"],["bank/deff8a2f_B.png"],["bank/deff8a2f_C.png"],["bank/deff8a2f_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"d5f349b7","k":16,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/d5f349b7_stem.png"],"e":"In right triangle PQR, angle P = 90° − 18° = 72°. Since P corresponds to S, angle S = 72°.","cimg":[["bank/d5f349b7_A.png"],["bank/d5f349b7_B.png"],["bank/d5f349b7_C.png"],["bank/d5f349b7_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"babd7461","k":16,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/babd7461_stem.png"],"e":"The scale factor is RS/JK = 135/15 = 9. Perimeters scale by the same factor, so the perimeter of RST is 9 × 36 = 324.","cimg":[["bank/babd7461_A.png"],["bank/babd7461_B.png"],["bank/babd7461_C.png"],["bank/babd7461_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"686b5212","k":16,"diff":"Medium","type":"spr","img":["bank/686b5212_stem.png"],"e":"The 58° angle and the angle above line r to the right of s are corresponding angles, so that angle is 58°, and y is its supplement: y = 180 − 58 = 122. Then 2x + 8 = 122, so x = 57.","ad":"57","a":57.0},{"id":"a6dbad6b","k":16,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/a6dbad6b_stem.png"],"e":"The angle where the left line meets ℓ inside the small triangle corresponds to y, so it is 20°. The small triangle above ℓ has angles 20°, z = 60°, and x, so x = 180 − 20 − 60 = 100.","cimg":[["bank/a6dbad6b_A.png"],["bank/a6dbad6b_B.png"],["bank/a6dbad6b_C.png"],["bank/a6dbad6b_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"27d075d8","k":17,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/27d075d8_stem.png"],"e":"cos(Q) = sin(R) for acute angles means Q and R are complementary: (x + 52) + (4x + 13) = 90. So 5x + 65 = 90 and x = 5.","cimg":[["bank/27d075d8_A.png"],["bank/27d075d8_B.png"],["bank/27d075d8_C.png"],["bank/27d075d8_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"81b664bc","k":16,"diff":"Hard","type":"mc","img":["bank/81b664bc_stem.png"],"e":"Parallel lines cut the two transversals proportionally, so AB/BC = FE/ED: 9/18.5 = 8.5/ED. Then ED = 8.5 × 18.5 ÷ 9 ≈ 17.47, which rounds to 17.5.","cimg":[["bank/81b664bc_A.png"],["bank/81b664bc_B.png"],["bank/81b664bc_C.png"],["bank/81b664bc_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"59cb654c","k":15,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/59cb654c_stem.png"],"e":"The side length of a square is the square root of its area: √64 = 8 inches.","cimg":[["bank/59cb654c_A.png"],["bank/59cb654c_B.png"],["bank/59cb654c_C.png"],["bank/59cb654c_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"902dc959","k":17,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/902dc959_q.png"],"e":"tan A = opposite/adjacent = BC/AC = 20/21.","cimg":[["bank/902dc959_A.png"],["bank/902dc959_B.png"],["bank/902dc959_C.png"],["bank/902dc959_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"e86f0651","k":18,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/e86f0651_stem.png"],"e":"Area of a circle is πr² = π(43²) = 1,849π square meters.","cimg":[["bank/e86f0651_A.png"],["bank/e86f0651_B.png"],["bank/e86f0651_C.png"],["bank/e86f0651_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"96467fea","k":18,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/96467fea_stem.png"],"e":"Circle N has area π(7²) = 49π. Adding circle M's area gives 49π + 64π = 113π mm².","cimg":[["bank/96467fea_A.png"],["bank/96467fea_B.png"],["bank/96467fea_C.png"],["bank/96467fea_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"858fd1cf","k":18,"diff":"Hard","type":"mc","img":["bank/858fd1cf_stem.png"],"e":"The radius to (5, −4) has slope (−4 − 1)/(5 − (−1)) = −5/6, so the tangent line has the perpendicular slope 6/5: y + 4 = (6/5)(x − 5). Checking (10, 2): (6/5)(5) = 6 = 2 + 4, so it lies on t.","cimg":[["bank/858fd1cf_A.png"],["bank/858fd1cf_B.png"],["bank/858fd1cf_C.png"],["bank/858fd1cf_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"9adb86ed","k":18,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/9adb86ed_stem.png"],"e":"PQ and PR are both radii, so each is 9 inches. Then QR = 31 − 9 − 9 = 13 inches.","cimg":[["bank/9adb86ed_A.png"],["bank/9adb86ed_B.png"],["bank/9adb86ed_C.png"],["bank/9adb86ed_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"096c7ef5","k":18,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/096c7ef5_stem.png"],"e":"The points are (4, 8), (7, 11), and (7, 5). Each is 3 units from (7, 8), so the circle has center (7, 8) and radius 3, giving circumference 2π(3) = 6π. So k = 6.","cimg":[["bank/096c7ef5_A.png"],["bank/096c7ef5_B.png"],["bank/096c7ef5_C.png"],["bank/096c7ef5_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"ec5d4823","k":15,"diff":"Easy","type":"spr","img":["bank/ec5d4823_stem.png"],"e":"Volume of a rectangular prism is length × width × height = 4 × 9 × 10 = 360 cubic centimeters.","ad":"360","a":360.0},{"id":"9966235e","k":15,"diff":"Hard","type":"mc","img":["bank/9966235e_stem.png"],"e":"Cube volume is 68³ = 314,432. Sphere volume is (4/3)π(34³) ≈ 164,636. The leftover space is 314,432 − 164,636 ≈ 149,796 cubic inches.","cimg":[["bank/9966235e_A.png"],["bank/9966235e_B.png"],["bank/9966235e_C.png"],["bank/9966235e_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"2b41a4c4","k":15,"diff":"Easy","type":"spr","img":["bank/2b41a4c4_stem.png"],"e":"Volume of a rectangular prism is length × width × height = 11 × 8 × 10 = 880 cubic meters.","ad":"880","a":880.0},{"id":"a0369739","k":16,"diff":"Hard","type":"mc","img":["bank/a0369739_stem.png"],"e":"AC = 15 + 23 = 38. The altitude BD creates triangle BDC similar to triangle ABC (angle C is shared and both have a right angle), with BC matching AC and BD matching AB. So BC/BD = AC/AB = 38/15.","cimg":[["bank/a0369739_A.png"],["bank/a0369739_B.png"],["bank/a0369739_C.png"],["bank/a0369739_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"a07ed090","k":15,"diff":"Hard","type":"mc","img":["bank/a07ed090_stem.png"],"e":"Volume πR²H must be 392 times πr²h. With R = 7r and H = 8h, the volume factor is 7² × 8 = 49 × 8 = 392. Remember the radius factor gets squared.","cimg":[["bank/a07ed090_A.png"],["bank/a07ed090_B.png"],["bank/a07ed090_C.png"],["bank/a07ed090_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"cbe8ca31","k":16,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/cbe8ca31_stem.png"],"e":"The angles of a triangle add to 180°, so angle Z = 180° − 24° − 98° = 58°.","cimg":[["bank/cbe8ca31_A.png"],["bank/cbe8ca31_B.png"],["bank/cbe8ca31_C.png"],["bank/cbe8ca31_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"3b931fb0","k":15,"diff":"Easy","type":"spr","img":["bank/3b931fb0_stem.png"],"e":"Volume of a cylinder = base area × height, so height = 377 ÷ 13 = 29 centimeters.","ad":"29","a":29.0},{"id":"94364a79","k":8,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/94364a79_stem.png"],"e":"At the same time, height and shadow are proportional: 10/5 = h/2. So h = 2 × 2 = 4 feet.","cimg":[["bank/94364a79_A.png"],["bank/94364a79_B.png"],["bank/94364a79_C.png"],["bank/94364a79_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"51f26ce8","k":16,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/51f26ce8_stem.png"],"e":"In similar triangles QPR and STR, QR corresponds to SR and QP corresponds to ST. So SR/25 = 14/15, giving SR = 25 × 14/15 = 350/15.","cimg":[["bank/51f26ce8_A.png"],["bank/51f26ce8_B.png"],["bank/51f26ce8_C.png"],["bank/51f26ce8_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"c24e1bda","k":16,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/c24e1bda_stem.png"],"e":"The 134° angle (below m, left of t) and w (below n, left of t) are corresponding angles on parallel lines, so w = 134.","cimg":[["bank/c24e1bda_A.png"],["bank/c24e1bda_B.png"],["bank/c24e1bda_C.png"],["bank/c24e1bda_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"055aafe7","k":16,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/055aafe7_stem.png"],"e":"The scale factor from ABC to XYZ is YZ/BC = 60/850. So XY = 170 × 60/850 = 12.","cimg":[["bank/055aafe7_A.png"],["bank/055aafe7_B.png"],["bank/055aafe7_C.png"],["bank/055aafe7_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"2d2cb85e","k":16,"diff":"Hard","type":"spr","img":["bank/2d2cb85e_stem.png"],"e":"Angle SVU = 180° − 41° = 139°, so in triangle SUV angle U = 180° − 29° − 139° = 12°. Since RT = TU, angle TRU also equals 12°, so x = 180 − 12 − 12 = 156.","ad":"156","a":156.0},{"id":"345cc36a","k":16,"diff":"Hard","type":"spr","img":["bank/345cc36a_stem.png"],"e":"Angles WQX and YQZ are vertical angles and angles W and Y both measure a°, so triangle WQX is similar to triangle YQZ. Then YZ/WX = YQ/WQ, so YZ = 60 × 63/70 = 54.","ad":"54","a":54.0},{"id":"c8345903","k":18,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/c8345903_q.png"],"e":"Arc ADC has central angle 100° and length 5π, so the whole circle (360°) has length 5π × 360/100 = 18π. Arc ABC is the rest: 18π − 5π = 13π.","cimg":[["bank/c8345903_A.png"],["bank/c8345903_B.png"],["bank/c8345903_C.png"],["bank/c8345903_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"901c3215","k":16,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/901c3215_stem.png"],"e":"The triangles already have two pairs of equal angles, so they are similar. Knowing BC and EF (the sides between the known angles) lets you check ASA: if BC = EF they are congruent, otherwise not. One side length of a single triangle is not enough.","cimg":[["bank/901c3215_A.png"],["bank/901c3215_B.png"],["bank/901c3215_C.png"],["bank/901c3215_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"2bddbc1b","k":17,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/2bddbc1b_stem.png"],"e":"cos A = adjacent/hypotenuse = AC/AB = 41/42.","cimg":[["bank/2bddbc1b_A.png"],["bank/2bddbc1b_B.png"],["bank/2bddbc1b_C.png"],["bank/2bddbc1b_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"85f1892d","k":17,"diff":"Hard","type":"spr","img":["bank/85f1892d_stem.png"],"e":"YZ = 26 is adjacent to angle Z and XY is opposite it, so XY = 26 tan 33°. The legs are YZ and XY, so the area is (1/2)(26)(26 tan 33°) = 338 tan 33°, giving k = 338.","ad":"338","a":338.0},{"id":"bd87bc09","k":17,"diff":"Medium","type":"spr","img":["bank/bd87bc09_stem.png"],"e":"sin(B) = AC/AB = 5/13 and AB = 26, so AC = 10. By the Pythagorean theorem, BC = √(26² − 10²) = √576 = 24.","ad":"24","a":24.0},{"id":"f7dbde16","k":16,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/f7dbde16_stem.png"],"e":"If M = 70° and T = 50°, then N = 180 − 60 − 70 = 50° and S = 180 − 60 − 50 = 70°. Both triangles have angles 60°, 70°, 50°, so they are similar by AA. Choice C gives angles that don't match, and side choices A and B don't give an included angle.","cimg":[["bank/f7dbde16_A.png"],["bank/f7dbde16_B.png"],["bank/f7dbde16_C.png"],["bank/f7dbde16_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"a4ed5285","k":15,"diff":"Easy","type":"spr","img":["bank/a4ed5285_stem.png"],"e":"The legs 3 and 5 are perpendicular, so they are base and height. Area = (1/2)(3)(5) = 7.5 square inches (7.5 is also correct).","ad":"15/2","tol":0.0011,"a":7.5},{"id":"87a9a2d4","k":17,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/87a9a2d4_stem.png"],"e":"sin A = opposite/hypotenuse = BC/AB = 35/171.","cimg":[["bank/87a9a2d4_A.png"],["bank/87a9a2d4_B.png"],["bank/87a9a2d4_C.png"],["bank/87a9a2d4_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"e6f2ace7","k":17,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/e6f2ace7_stem.png"],"e":"By the Pythagorean theorem, the hypotenuse is √(3² + 7²) = √58 ≈ 7.6.","cimg":[["bank/e6f2ace7_A.png"],["bank/e6f2ace7_B.png"],["bank/e6f2ace7_C.png"],["bank/e6f2ace7_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"b0c5ece5","k":17,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/b0c5ece5_stem.png"],"e":"In a right triangle, leg² + leg² = hypotenuse². The legs are 4 and b and the hypotenuse is 19, so 4² + b² = 19².","cimg":[["bank/b0c5ece5_A.png"],["bank/b0c5ece5_B.png"],["bank/b0c5ece5_C.png"],["bank/b0c5ece5_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"76c73dbf","k":18,"diff":"Hard","type":"spr","img":["bank/76c73dbf_stem.png"],"e":"Complete the square: (x + 1/2)² + (y + 1/2)² = 199/2 + 1/4 + 1/4 = 100. So r² = 100 and the radius is 10.","ad":"10","a":10.0},{"id":"58c26db8","k":17,"diff":"Hard","type":"mc","img":["bank/58c26db8_stem.png"],"e":"If each leg is s, the hypotenuse is s√2 and the perimeter is 2s + s√2. Setting s = 9√2 gives 18√2 + 18, which matches, so the hypotenuse is 9√2 × √2 = 18.","cimg":[["bank/58c26db8_A.png"],["bank/58c26db8_B.png"],["bank/58c26db8_C.png"],["bank/58c26db8_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"e336a1d2","k":15,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/e336a1d2_stem.png"],"e":"Volume of a cube is edge³ = 41³ = 68,921 cubic inches.","cimg":[["bank/e336a1d2_A.png"],["bank/e336a1d2_B.png"],["bank/e336a1d2_C.png"],["bank/e336a1d2_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"e4b4e9ea","k":15,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/e4b4e9ea_stem.png"],"e":"The base area is 6² = 36. Volume = base area × height, so height = 2,880 ÷ 36 = 80 units.","cimg":[["bank/e4b4e9ea_A.png"],["bank/e4b4e9ea_B.png"],["bank/e4b4e9ea_C.png"],["bank/e4b4e9ea_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"c0586eb5","k":15,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/c0586eb5_stem.png"],"e":"The radius is half the diameter, 4 inches. Volume = πr²h = π(4²)(12) = 192π cubic inches.","cimg":[["bank/c0586eb5_A.png"],["bank/c0586eb5_B.png"],["bank/c0586eb5_C.png"],["bank/c0586eb5_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"2a549721","k":15,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/2a549721_stem.png"],"e":"Area = length × width, so width = 280 ÷ 10 = 28 centimeters.","cimg":[["bank/2a549721_A.png"],["bank/2a549721_B.png"],["bank/2a549721_C.png"],["bank/2a549721_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"52f7b898","k":17,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/52f7b898_stem.png"],"e":"Angle A = 180° − 90° − 30° = 60°, and tan 60° = √3. The hypotenuse length 54 doesn't change the ratio.","cimg":[["bank/52f7b898_A.png"],["bank/52f7b898_B.png"],["bank/52f7b898_C.png"],["bank/52f7b898_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"03c6994f","k":15,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/03c6994f_stem.png"],"e":"Scaling side lengths by 246 scales area by 246². So k = 246² = 60,516.","cimg":[["bank/03c6994f_A.png"],["bank/03c6994f_B.png"],["bank/03c6994f_C.png"],["bank/03c6994f_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"151eda3c","k":15,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/151eda3c_stem.png"],"e":"Container B's radius is 16 × 1.25 = 20 cm. Volume = πr²h = π(20²)(50) = 20,000π cubic centimeters.","cimg":[["bank/151eda3c_A.png"],["bank/151eda3c_B.png"],["bank/151eda3c_C.png"],["bank/151eda3c_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"35d37640","k":17,"diff":"Hard","type":"mc","img":["bank/35d37640_stem.png"],"e":"Since H = (−1, y) is on the unit circle, y = 0, so H = (−1, 0) and angle FGH is π radians plus any whole number of full turns (2π). Only 25π = π + 12(2π) is an odd multiple of π.","cimg":[["bank/35d37640_A.png"],["bank/35d37640_B.png"],["bank/35d37640_C.png"],["bank/35d37640_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"e50afdd3","k":18,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/e50afdd3_stem.png"],"e":"The circle has center (−4, 19) and radius √121 = 11, so x-values on it run from −4 − 11 = −15 to −4 + 11 = 7. Only −14 is in that range.","cimg":[["bank/e50afdd3_A.png"],["bank/e50afdd3_B.png"],["bank/e50afdd3_C.png"],["bank/e50afdd3_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"167aff9e","k":15,"diff":"Hard","type":"spr","img":["bank/167aff9e_stem.png"],"e":"The surface area ratio is 1450/58 = 25, so the length scale factor is 5 and the volume ratio is 5³ = 125. Prism X has volume 1250 ÷ 125 = 10, so the sum is 1250 + 10 = 1260.","ad":"1260","a":1260.0},{"id":"2266984b","k":18,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/2266984b_stem.png"],"e":"Complete the square: (x + 10)² + (y + 8)² = −20 + 100 + 64 = 144. The center is (−10, −8); watch the signs.","cimg":[["bank/2266984b_A.png"],["bank/2266984b_B.png"],["bank/2266984b_C.png"],["bank/2266984b_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"d0b6d927","k":15,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/d0b6d927_stem.png"],"e":"Area = length × width, so width = 63 ÷ 9 = 7 meters.","cimg":[["bank/d0b6d927_A.png"],["bank/d0b6d927_B.png"],["bank/d0b6d927_C.png"],["bank/d0b6d927_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"d621cffb","k":15,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/d621cffb_stem.png"],"e":"Volume of a sphere is (4/3)πr³ = (4/3)π(17/5)³ = (4/3)π(4913/125) = 19,652π/375 cubic feet.","cimg":[["bank/d621cffb_A.png"],["bank/d621cffb_B.png"],["bank/d621cffb_C.png"],["bank/d621cffb_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"1429dcdf","k":17,"diff":"Easy","type":"spr","img":["bank/1429dcdf_stem.png"],"e":"sin x° = opposite/hypotenuse. The side opposite angle x is 16 and the hypotenuse is 23, so sin x° = 16/23.","ad":"16/23","tol":0.0011,"a":0.6956521739130435},{"id":"69b0d79d","k":18,"diff":"Hard","type":"mc","img":["bank/69b0d79d_stem.png"],"e":"OA = OB are radii, so triangle OAB is isosceles and angle AOB = 180° − 30° − 30° = 120°. The radius is OC = 18, so arc AB = (120/360) × 2π(18) = 12π.","cimg":[["bank/69b0d79d_A.png"],["bank/69b0d79d_B.png"],["bank/69b0d79d_C.png"],["bank/69b0d79d_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"5a7e3b46","k":17,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/5a7e3b46_stem.png"],"e":"cos A = AB/AC = 3/5, so the sides are in a 3-4-5 ratio with BC (opposite A) matching 4. Since BC = 136 = 4 × 34, AB = 3 × 34 = 102.","cimg":[["bank/5a7e3b46_A.png"],["bank/5a7e3b46_B.png"],["bank/5a7e3b46_C.png"],["bank/5a7e3b46_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"ebbf23ae","k":18,"diff":"Easy","type":"spr","img":["bank/ebbf23ae_stem.png"],"e":"The diameter runs from (2, 4) to (2, 14), so its length is 14 − 4 = 10. The radius is half of that, so r = 5.","ad":"5","a":5.0},{"id":"d7a8aa9c","k":16,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/d7a8aa9c_stem.png"],"e":"For triangle T's sides to be longer than S's, the scale factor must be greater than 1. Only 29/28 is greater than 1.","cimg":[["bank/d7a8aa9c_A.png"],["bank/d7a8aa9c_B.png"],["bank/d7a8aa9c_C.png"],["bank/d7a8aa9c_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"a2659088","k":15,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/a2659088_stem.png"],"e":"Volume = πr²h = π(12²)(8) = π(144)(8) = 1,152π cubic meters.","cimg":[["bank/a2659088_A.png"],["bank/a2659088_B.png"],["bank/a2659088_C.png"],["bank/a2659088_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"32f99025","k":15,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/32f99025_stem.png"],"e":"Area of a triangle = (1/2) × base × height = (1/2)(8)(12) = 48 square inches.","cimg":[["bank/32f99025_A.png"],["bank/32f99025_B.png"],["bank/32f99025_C.png"],["bank/32f99025_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"502d9690","k":16,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/502d9690_stem.png"],"e":"The area ratio is 648/72 = 9, so the length ratio is √9 = 3. The longest side of EFGH is 36 ÷ 3 = 12 inches.","cimg":[["bank/502d9690_A.png"],["bank/502d9690_B.png"],["bank/502d9690_C.png"],["bank/502d9690_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"6b4707aa","k":18,"diff":"Medium","type":"spr","img":["bank/6b4707aa_stem.png"],"e":"Circle A has r² = 25, so r = 5. Circle B has radius 2 × 5 = 10, so k = 10² = 100. Doubling the radius multiplies r² by 4, not 2.","ad":"100","a":100.0},{"id":"4c95c7d4","k":15,"diff":"Hard","type":"mc","img":["bank/4c95c7d4_q.png"],"e":"The trapezoid's perimeter is made of 5 triangle sides (2 on the bottom, 1 on top, 2 slanted), so each side is 20 ÷ 5 = 4. Each equilateral triangle has area (√3/4)(4²) = 4√3, and the two shaded ones total 8√3.","cimg":[["bank/4c95c7d4_A.png"],["bank/4c95c7d4_B.png"],["bank/4c95c7d4_C.png"],["bank/4c95c7d4_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"b8a225ff","k":18,"diff":"Medium","type":"spr","img":["bank/b8a225ff_stem.png"],"e":"Circle A has r² = 4, so r = 2. Circle B has radius 2 × 2 = 4, so k = 4² = 16.","ad":"16","a":16.0},{"id":"b0a72bdc","k":18,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/b0a72bdc_stem.png"],"e":"The right side, 16, is r², so r = 4 and the diameter is 2 × 4 = 8.","cimg":[["bank/b0a72bdc_A.png"],["bank/b0a72bdc_B.png"],["bank/b0a72bdc_C.png"],["bank/b0a72bdc_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"933fee1a","k":17,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/933fee1a_q.png"],"e":"BC/AB = sin 32°. In triangle DEF, angle E = 90° − 58° = 32°, and sin E = DF/DE.","cimg":[["bank/933fee1a_A.png"],["bank/933fee1a_B.png"],["bank/933fee1a_C.png"],["bank/933fee1a_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"64c1f044","k":17,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/64c1f044_stem.png"],"e":"tan x° = opposite/adjacent. The side opposite angle x is 26 and the adjacent leg is 7, so tan x° = 26/7.","cimg":[["bank/64c1f044_A.png"],["bank/64c1f044_B.png"],["bank/64c1f044_C.png"],["bank/64c1f044_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"2f7c92ad","k":16,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/2f7c92ad_stem.png"],"e":"In similar triangles, corresponding angles are equal, and angle CAE corresponds to angle CBD. So angle CAE = 57°; the side ratio 26 does not change angles.","cimg":[["bank/2f7c92ad_A.png"],["bank/2f7c92ad_B.png"],["bank/2f7c92ad_C.png"],["bank/2f7c92ad_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"c447367f","k":18,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/c447367f_stem.png"],"e":"A circle with center (h, k) and radius r is (x − h)² + (y − k)² = r². Here r = 9k, so r² = (9k)² = 81k².","cimg":[["bank/c447367f_A.png"],["bank/c447367f_B.png"],["bank/c447367f_C.png"],["bank/c447367f_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"b2528e6b","k":18,"diff":"Medium","type":"spr","img":["bank/b2528e6b_stem.png"],"e":"The points are (2, 6), (6, 10), and (6, 2). Each is 4 units from (6, 6), so the radius is 4 and the circumference is 2π(4) = 8π. So k = 8.","ad":"8","a":8.0},{"id":"9fec9d49","k":15,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/9fec9d49_stem.png"],"e":"Scaling lengths by 1/10 scales area by (1/10)² = 1/100. So the model's area is 600 ÷ 100 = 6 square meters.","cimg":[["bank/9fec9d49_A.png"],["bank/9fec9d49_B.png"],["bank/9fec9d49_C.png"],["bank/9fec9d49_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"ba8ca563","k":15,"diff":"Hard","type":"spr","img":["bank/ba8ca563_stem.png"],"e":"The edge length is the cube root of 474,552, which is 78. Each face has area 78² = 6,084, so the surface area is 6 × 6,084 = 36,504.","ad":"36504","a":36504.0},{"id":"5011b039","k":18,"diff":"Easy","type":"spr","img":["bank/5011b039_stem.png"],"e":"In (x − h)² + (y − k)² = r², the right side is r². So r² = 169 and r = 13.","ad":"13","a":13.0},{"id":"9d078710","k":16,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/9d078710_stem.png"],"e":"The 40° angle is above k and right of ℓ; w is in the matching position at j, so w = 40 means corresponding angles are equal and j ∥ k. y = 40 and z = 140 are always true (vertical and supplementary angles), and x = 140 would mean the lines are not parallel.","cimg":[["bank/9d078710_A.png"],["bank/9d078710_B.png"],["bank/9d078710_C.png"],["bank/9d078710_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"b1e1c2f5","k":16,"diff":"Hard","type":"spr","img":["bank/b1e1c2f5_stem.png"],"e":"Since DE ∥ BC, triangle ADE is similar to triangle ABC. CE = 2AE means AC = 3AE, so the scale factor is 1/3 and DE = 162 ÷ 3 = 54.","ad":"54","a":54.0},{"id":"0d43db90","k":16,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/0d43db90_stem.png"],"e":"The perimeter is the sum of the sides: BC = 17 − 4 − 7 = 6 inches.","cimg":[["bank/0d43db90_A.png"],["bank/0d43db90_B.png"],["bank/0d43db90_C.png"],["bank/0d43db90_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"62d39eb8","k":18,"diff":"Easy","type":"spr","img":["bank/62d39eb8_stem.png"],"e":"In (x − h)² + (y − k)² = r², the right side is r². So r² = 289 and r = 17.","ad":"17","a":17.0},{"id":"94f7c9e2","k":17,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/94f7c9e2_stem.png"],"e":"RS = 18 is the side opposite angle Q and QS is the hypotenuse, so sin Q = 18/QS. Solving gives QS = 18/sin Q.","cimg":[["bank/94f7c9e2_A.png"],["bank/94f7c9e2_B.png"],["bank/94f7c9e2_C.png"],["bank/94f7c9e2_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"e0874bc2","k":16,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/e0874bc2_stem.png"],"e":"The perimeter ratio is 333/37 = 9, and corresponding sides have the same ratio. So XY = 9 × 18 = 162.","cimg":[["bank/e0874bc2_A.png"],["bank/e0874bc2_B.png"],["bank/e0874bc2_C.png"],["bank/e0874bc2_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"a4bd60a3","k":17,"diff":"Hard","type":"spr","img":["bank/a4bd60a3_stem.png"],"e":"Each side is 624 ÷ 3 = 208. The height of an equilateral triangle is (side/2)√3 (from a 30-60-90 triangle), so the height is 104√3 and k = 104.","ad":"104","a":104.0},{"id":"899c6042","k":15,"diff":"Medium","type":"spr","img":["bank/899c6042_stem.png"],"e":"The radius is half the diameter, 3 cm. Cone volume = (1/3)πr²h = (1/3)π(9)(22) = 66π, so n = 66.","ad":"66","a":66.0},{"id":"498d6795","k":17,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/498d6795_stem.png"],"e":"By the Pythagorean theorem, AC² = (10√37)² + (24√37)² = 37(100 + 576) = 37 × 676. So AC = 26√37 (a 10-24-26 right triangle scaled by √37).","cimg":[["bank/498d6795_A.png"],["bank/498d6795_B.png"],["bank/498d6795_C.png"],["bank/498d6795_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"740bf79f","k":17,"diff":"Hard","type":"mc","img":["bank/740bf79f_stem.png"],"e":"Angle MNP is a right angle, so MP = 5 (3-4-5 triangle). The area is (1/2)(3)(4) = 6, and it also equals (1/2)(MP)(NQ) = (1/2)(5)(NQ), so NQ = 12/5 = 2.4.","cimg":[["bank/740bf79f_A.png"],["bank/740bf79f_B.png"],["bank/740bf79f_C.png"],["bank/740bf79f_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"0e40dfb0","k":15,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/0e40dfb0_stem.png"],"e":"Area of a rectangle is length × width, so the area is 3 · 39. Choice A is the perimeter, not the area.","cimg":[["bank/0e40dfb0_A.png"],["bank/0e40dfb0_B.png"],["bank/0e40dfb0_C.png"],["bank/0e40dfb0_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"3b225698","k":16,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/3b225698_stem.png"],"e":"In similar triangles, corresponding angles are equal. Z corresponds to T, so ∠T = ∠Z = 20°; the side scale factor does not change angles.","cimg":[["bank/3b225698_A.png"],["bank/3b225698_B.png"],["bank/3b225698_C.png"],["bank/3b225698_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"249d3f80","k":18,"diff":"Easy","type":"spr","img":["bank/249d3f80_stem.png"],"e":"A central angle has the same measure as the arc it intercepts. ∠ROS is the central angle for arc RS, so it measures 100°.","ad":"100","a":100.0},{"id":"fc5ef8d3","k":16,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/fc5ef8d3_stem.png"],"e":"The perimeter ratio 150/50 = 3 equals the side scale factor. So XY = 3 × TU = 3 × 6 = 18.","cimg":[["bank/fc5ef8d3_A.png"],["bank/fc5ef8d3_B.png"],["bank/fc5ef8d3_C.png"],["bank/fc5ef8d3_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"a4c05a1b","k":16,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/a4c05a1b_stem.png"],"e":"Because r ∥ s, the angles x and y are supplementary, so x = 180 − y. If y < 65, then x > 180 − 65 = 115.","cimg":[["bank/a4c05a1b_A.png"],["bank/a4c05a1b_B.png"],["bank/a4c05a1b_C.png"],["bank/a4c05a1b_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"38517165","k":18,"diff":"Easy","type":"spr","img":["bank/38517165_stem.png"],"e":"Circumference = π × diameter, so π d = 31π gives d = 31.","ad":"31","a":31.0},{"id":"ab176ad6","k":18,"diff":"Easy","type":"spr","img":["bank/ab176ad6_stem.png"],"e":"In (x − h)² + (y − k)² = r², the right side is r². Here r² = 121, so r = √121 = 11.","ad":"11","a":11.0},{"id":"ebf3a962","k":15,"diff":"Easy","type":"spr","img":["bank/ebf3a962_stem.png"],"e":"V = πr²h, so πr²(16) = 3,136π. Then r² = 3,136/16 = 196 and r = 14.","ad":"14","a":14.0},{"id":"98c12e38","k":18,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/98c12e38_stem.png"],"e":"Circle K has area π(4)² = 16π. Adding circle L's 100π gives 116π mm².","cimg":[["bank/98c12e38_A.png"],["bank/98c12e38_B.png"],["bank/98c12e38_C.png"],["bank/98c12e38_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"aa2d36fe","k":18,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/aa2d36fe_stem.png"],"e":"In (x − h)² + (y − k)² = r², the center is (h, k) and the radius is √(r²). So the center is (13, k) and the radius is √64 = 8.","cimg":[["bank/aa2d36fe_A.png"],["bank/aa2d36fe_B.png"],["bank/aa2d36fe_C.png"],["bank/aa2d36fe_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"d3fe472f","k":16,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/d3fe472f_stem.png"],"e":"Each side of XYZ is 2 times its corresponding side in ABC, and XY corresponds to AB. So XY = 2 × 16 = 32.","cimg":[["bank/d3fe472f_A.png"],["bank/d3fe472f_B.png"],["bank/d3fe472f_C.png"],["bank/d3fe472f_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"f9d40000","k":16,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/f9d40000_stem.png"],"e":"The angles of a triangle sum to 180°. So ∠Z = 180° − 23° − 66° = 91°.","cimg":[["bank/f9d40000_A.png"],["bank/f9d40000_B.png"],["bank/f9d40000_C.png"],["bank/f9d40000_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"0d3f51dc","k":16,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/0d3f51dc_stem.png"],"e":"The 33° angle at line n and the angle x at line m are on opposite sides of t and of the parallel lines, so they are supplementary. x = 180 − 33 = 147.","cimg":[["bank/0d3f51dc_A.png"],["bank/0d3f51dc_B.png"],["bank/0d3f51dc_C.png"],["bank/0d3f51dc_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"fd8745fc","k":16,"diff":"Easy","type":"spr","img":["bank/fd8745fc_stem.png"],"e":"The angles of a triangle sum to 180°. So ∠J = 180 − 48 − 48 = 84.","ad":"84","a":84.0},{"id":"b434e103","k":16,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/b434e103_stem.png"],"e":"∠S + ∠T = 180 − 63 = 117, and ∠T must be greater than 0. So ∠S must be less than 117, and only 116 works.","cimg":[["bank/b434e103_A.png"],["bank/b434e103_B.png"],["bank/b434e103_C.png"],["bank/b434e103_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"3e577e4a","k":18,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/3e577e4a_stem.png"],"e":"The radius to (−7, −7) has slope (−7 − (−6))/(−7 − (−4)) = (−1)/(−3) = 1/3. A tangent line is perpendicular to that radius, so its slope is the negative reciprocal, −3.","cimg":[["bank/3e577e4a_A.png"],["bank/3e577e4a_B.png"],["bank/3e577e4a_C.png"],["bank/3e577e4a_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"62ec6574","k":15,"diff":"Hard","type":"mc","img":["bank/62ec6574_stem.png"],"e":"Width = 24t ÷ (8/3) = 9t. Surface area = 2(24t) + 2(15)(8/3) + 2(15)(9t) = 48t + 80 + 270t = 318t + 80.","cimg":[["bank/62ec6574_A.png"],["bank/62ec6574_B.png"],["bank/62ec6574_C.png"],["bank/62ec6574_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"b0dc920d","k":15,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/b0dc920d_stem.png"],"e":"The height is h = r + 4, and V = πr²h = πr²(r + 4). Expanding gives πr³ + 4πr².","cimg":[["bank/b0dc920d_A.png"],["bank/b0dc920d_B.png"],["bank/b0dc920d_C.png"],["bank/b0dc920d_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"2085e10e","k":16,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/2085e10e_stem.png"],"e":"Two angles of DEF (47° and 97°) equal two angles of RST, so the third angles must also match (36° each). By angle-angle similarity, the triangles are similar, so no more information is needed.","cimg":[["bank/2085e10e_A.png"],["bank/2085e10e_B.png"],["bank/2085e10e_C.png"],["bank/2085e10e_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"689abc2a","k":15,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/689abc2a_stem.png"],"e":"Removing a piece subtracts its area: 72 − 20 = 52 square inches.","cimg":[["bank/689abc2a_A.png"],["bank/689abc2a_B.png"],["bank/689abc2a_C.png"],["bank/689abc2a_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"fa2771d5","k":18,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/fa2771d5_stem.png"],"e":"Moving right 4 units adds 4 to the x-coordinate of the center, so (7, −3) becomes (11, −3). The radius stays 1, so the equation is (x − 11)² + (y + 3)² = 1.","cimg":[["bank/fa2771d5_A.png"],["bank/fa2771d5_B.png"],["bank/fa2771d5_C.png"],["bank/fa2771d5_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"bbaac300","k":17,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/bbaac300_stem.png"],"e":"Angle B corresponds to angle E (A↔D and C↔F, so B↔E). Corresponding angles in similar triangles are equal, so cos E = cos B = 1/22.","cimg":[["bank/bbaac300_A.png"],["bank/bbaac300_B.png"],["bank/bbaac300_C.png"],["bank/bbaac300_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"55bb437a","k":17,"diff":"Medium","type":"spr","img":["bank/55bb437a_stem.png"],"e":"In right triangle ABC, tan B = AC/AB = 3/4 and BC = 15, so AB = 12 and AC = 9. Then BD = 12 − 4 = 8, and in similar triangle DBE, DE = BD × tan B = 8 × 3/4 = 6.","ad":"6","a":6.0},{"id":"c7bed21d","k":16,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/c7bed21d_stem.png"],"e":"Corresponding angles of similar figures are equal; the factor of 3 changes only side lengths. So ∠P' = ∠P = 30°.","cimg":[["bank/c7bed21d_A.png"],["bank/c7bed21d_B.png"],["bank/c7bed21d_C.png"],["bank/c7bed21d_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"fecc446d","k":16,"diff":"Hard","type":"mc","img":["bank/fecc446d_stem.png"],"e":"Each angle is either (7x − 250) or its supplement (430 − 7x). Sums of four angles can be 28x − 1000, 14x − 320, 360, −14x + 1040, or −28x + 1720. −14x + 1,540 is not one of these.","cimg":[["bank/fecc446d_A.png"],["bank/fecc446d_B.png"],["bank/fecc446d_C.png"],["bank/fecc446d_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"8e7689e0","k":17,"diff":"Easy","type":"spr","img":["bank/8e7689e0_stem.png"],"e":"180° = π radians, so 720° = 720 × π/180 = 4π. Thus a = 4.","ad":"4","a":4.0},{"id":"69f4bbdc","k":16,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/69f4bbdc_stem.png"],"e":"The angles of a triangle sum to 180°, and one angle is 90°. So a = 180 − 90 − 13 = 77.","cimg":[["bank/69f4bbdc_A.png"],["bank/69f4bbdc_B.png"],["bank/69f4bbdc_C.png"],["bank/69f4bbdc_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"3563d76d","k":8,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/3563d76d_stem.png"],"e":"At the same time, height and shadow length are proportional: h/16 = 555/300. Then h = 16 × 555/300 = 29.6, which is closest to 30.","cimg":[["bank/3563d76d_A.png"],["bank/3563d76d_B.png"],["bank/3563d76d_C.png"],["bank/3563d76d_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"c41eb616","k":16,"diff":"Hard","type":"mc","img":["bank/c41eb616_stem.png"],"e":"The angles are (9x − 140) and its supplement (320 − 9x). Possible sums of two angles are 18x − 280, 640 − 18x, and 180. So (−18x + 280) is not possible.","cimg":[["bank/c41eb616_A.png"],["bank/c41eb616_B.png"],["bank/c41eb616_C.png"],["bank/c41eb616_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"dfc420b2","k":16,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/dfc420b2_stem.png"],"e":"In triangle ABC, ∠ACB = 180 − 20 − 100 = 60. Vertical angles are equal, so ∠DCE = 60, and in triangle DCE, y = 180 − 60 − 40 = 80.","cimg":[["bank/dfc420b2_A.png"],["bank/dfc420b2_B.png"],["bank/dfc420b2_C.png"],["bank/dfc420b2_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"de550be0","k":17,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/de550be0_q.png"],"e":"By the Pythagorean theorem, a² + 6² = 21². So a² = 21² − 6², and a = √(21² − 6²).","cimg":[["bank/de550be0_A.png"],["bank/de550be0_B.png"],["bank/de550be0_C.png"],["bank/de550be0_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"f2495de4","k":17,"diff":"Hard","type":"mc","img":["bank/f2495de4_stem.png"],"e":"565π/6 = 94π + π/6, and 94π is 47 full rotations, so cos(565π/6) = cos(π/6). Since cos(π/6) = √3/2, the answer is √3/2.","cimg":[["bank/f2495de4_A.png"],["bank/f2495de4_B.png"],["bank/f2495de4_C.png"],["bank/f2495de4_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"800e71b8","k":18,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/800e71b8_stem.png"],"e":"The minor arc MN and the major arc MPN together make the whole circle. So the circumference is 39 + 195 = 234 cm.","cimg":[["bank/800e71b8_A.png"],["bank/800e71b8_B.png"],["bank/800e71b8_C.png"],["bank/800e71b8_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"901e3285","k":16,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/901e3285_stem.png"],"e":"If B = A, then B = 50°; if B = C, then B = (180 − 50)/2 = 65°; if A = C, then B = 180 − 100 = 80°. A 100° angle B would make C = 30°, so no two angles would be equal.","cimg":[["bank/901e3285_A.png"],["bank/901e3285_B.png"],["bank/901e3285_C.png"],["bank/901e3285_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"bd7f6e30","k":16,"diff":"Hard","type":"mc","img":["bank/bd7f6e30_stem.png"],"e":"Since RT = TU, the base angles are equal: ∠TRU = ∠TUR = (180 − 114)/2 = 33°. In triangle SVU, ∠SVU = 180 − 31 − 33 = 116°, so x = 180 − 116 = 64.","cimg":[["bank/bd7f6e30_A.png"],["bank/bd7f6e30_B.png"],["bank/bd7f6e30_C.png"],["bank/bd7f6e30_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"2adbf1b1","k":16,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/2adbf1b1_stem.png"],"e":"x and y are vertical angles, so 6k + 13 = 8k − 29, which gives k = 21 and x = 139. z is supplementary to x (because m ∥ n), so z = 180 − 139 = 41.","cimg":[["bank/2adbf1b1_A.png"],["bank/2adbf1b1_B.png"],["bank/2adbf1b1_C.png"],["bank/2adbf1b1_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"6708546e","k":15,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/6708546e_stem.png"],"e":"When side lengths are multiplied by 2, area is multiplied by 2² = 4. So the area of PQRS is 5 × 4 = 20 square centimeters.","cimg":[["bank/6708546e_A.png"],["bank/6708546e_B.png"],["bank/6708546e_C.png"],["bank/6708546e_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"ffe862a3","k":17,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/ffe862a3_stem.png"],"e":"In a 45-45-90 triangle, each leg is the hypotenuse ÷ √2: 58/√2 = 29√2. The perimeter is 29√2 + 29√2 + 58 = 58 + 58√2.","cimg":[["bank/ffe862a3_A.png"],["bank/ffe862a3_B.png"],["bank/ffe862a3_C.png"],["bank/ffe862a3_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"24cec8d1","k":18,"diff":"Medium","type":"spr","img":["bank/24cec8d1_stem.png"],"e":"OR and OS are both radii, so triangle ORS is isosceles and ∠RSO = ∠SRO. Each of these angles is (180 − 88)/2 = 46.","ad":"46","a":46.0},{"id":"8c1aa743","k":15,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/8c1aa743_stem.png"],"e":"Area scales by the square of the side ratio, which is 6² = 36. So the area of EFGH is 54 × 36 = 1,944.","cimg":[["bank/8c1aa743_A.png"],["bank/8c1aa743_B.png"],["bank/8c1aa743_C.png"],["bank/8c1aa743_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"7268586c","k":16,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/7268586c_stem.png"],"e":"Since PQ = QR, the angles opposite those sides are equal, so ∠R = ∠P = 24°. Check: 24 + 24 + 132 = 180.","cimg":[["bank/7268586c_A.png"],["bank/7268586c_B.png"],["bank/7268586c_C.png"],["bank/7268586c_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"44b2b894","k":18,"diff":"Hard","type":"spr","img":["bank/44b2b894_stem.png"],"e":"Let the short side be s. The diagonal is 2s, so the long side is √(4s² − s²) = s√3 and the area is s²√3 = 1,089√3, which gives s = 33. The rectangle's diagonal is a diameter of the circle, so the diameter is 2(33) = 66.","ad":"66","a":66.0},{"id":"7700d098","k":17,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/7700d098_stem.png"],"e":"By the Pythagorean theorem, the other leg is √(196.8² − 43.2²) = √36,864 = 192.","cimg":[["bank/7700d098_A.png"],["bank/7700d098_B.png"],["bank/7700d098_C.png"],["bank/7700d098_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"0837c3b9","k":16,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/0837c3b9_stem.png"],"e":"The perimeters of similar triangles scale by the same factor as the sides, which is 2. So the perimeter of DEF is 2 × 20 = 40.","cimg":[["bank/0837c3b9_A.png"],["bank/0837c3b9_B.png"],["bank/0837c3b9_C.png"],["bank/0837c3b9_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"9e44284b","k":18,"diff":"Hard","type":"mc","img":["bank/9e44284b_stem.png"],"e":"Divide by 2: x² − 3x + y² + y = 22.5. Complete the square: (x − 1.5)² + (y + 0.5)² = 22.5 + 2.25 + 0.25 = 25, so r = 5.","cimg":[["bank/9e44284b_A.png"],["bank/9e44284b_B.png"],["bank/9e44284b_C.png"],["bank/9e44284b_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"4ddfa209","k":16,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/4ddfa209_stem.png"],"e":"All three sides of an equilateral triangle are equal, so the perimeter is 3 × 28 = 84 inches.","cimg":[["bank/4ddfa209_A.png"],["bank/4ddfa209_B.png"],["bank/4ddfa209_C.png"],["bank/4ddfa209_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"58687a66","k":16,"diff":"Easy","type":"spr","img":["bank/58687a66_stem.png"],"e":"The 175° angle at line h and angle x at line g sit in the same position (below the parallel line, to the right of the transversal), so they are corresponding angles. Since g ∥ h, x = 175.","ad":"175","a":175.0},{"id":"54df8076","k":18,"diff":"Hard","type":"spr","img":["bank/54df8076_stem.png"],"e":"Each side is 852/3 = 284. For an equilateral triangle, the circumscribed radius is side/√3 = 284/√3 = (284/3)√3. So w = 284/3.","ad":"284/3","tol":0.0011,"a":94.66666666666667},{"id":"014edcb7","k":16,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/014edcb7_stem.png"],"e":"The exterior angle PRS equals the sum of the two remote interior angles: 163 = 132 + ∠QPR. So ∠QPR = 31°.","cimg":[["bank/014edcb7_A.png"],["bank/014edcb7_B.png"],["bank/014edcb7_C.png"],["bank/014edcb7_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"568d66a7","k":17,"diff":"Hard","type":"mc","img":["bank/568d66a7_stem.png"],"e":"With leg a, the hypotenuse is a√2, so the perimeter is a(2 + √2) = 94 + 94√2 = 47√2(√2 + 2). So a = 47√2.","cimg":[["bank/568d66a7_A.png"],["bank/568d66a7_B.png"],["bank/568d66a7_C.png"],["bank/568d66a7_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"322a6dfe","k":16,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/322a6dfe_stem.png"],"e":"S corresponds to Z, and corresponding angles of similar figures are equal. So ∠Z = 135°; the side lengths only tell you the scale factor.","cimg":[["bank/322a6dfe_A.png"],["bank/322a6dfe_B.png"],["bank/322a6dfe_C.png"],["bank/322a6dfe_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"0e709a29","k":17,"diff":"Hard","type":"mc","img":["bank/0e709a29_stem.png"],"e":"TR = 584 is the longest side, so the right angle is at S. Then tan T = opposite/adjacent = RS/ST = 440/384 = 55/48. W corresponds to T, so tan W = 55/48.","cimg":[["bank/0e709a29_A.png"],["bank/0e709a29_B.png"],["bank/0e709a29_C.png"],["bank/0e709a29_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"a6097ec2","k":17,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/a6097ec2_stem.png"],"e":"The side opposite angle x is 63, and the hypotenuse is 73. So sin x° = 63/73.","cimg":[["bank/a6097ec2_A.png"],["bank/a6097ec2_B.png"],["bank/a6097ec2_C.png"],["bank/a6097ec2_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"e570a99c","k":16,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/e570a99c_stem.png"],"e":"J and K are equal, so 2J + 118 = 180. Then 2J = 62 and J = 31°.","cimg":[["bank/e570a99c_A.png"],["bank/e570a99c_B.png"],["bank/e570a99c_C.png"],["bank/e570a99c_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"eeb4143c","k":16,"diff":"Hard","type":"spr","img":["bank/eeb4143c_stem.png"],"e":"AC = 12, so the area of ABC is 6y, and 48 ≤ 6y ≤ 60 gives y = 8, 9, or 10. The small triangle is similar to ABC, so x/5 = y/12 and x = 5y/12, which is 10/3, 15/4, or 25/6.","ad":"10/3 or 15/4 or 25/6","tol":0.0011,"a":3.3333333333333335,"alts":[3.3333333333333335,3.75,4.166666666666667]},{"id":"5b2b8866","k":15,"diff":"Medium","type":"spr","img":["bank/5b2b8866_stem.png"],"e":"Each dimension is multiplied by 1.2, so the area is multiplied by 1.2² = 1.44. The new area is 360 × 1.44 = 518.4.","ad":"518.4","a":518.4},{"id":"fc8aa563","k":18,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/fc8aa563_stem.png"],"e":"In (x − h)² + (y − k)² = r², the center is (h, k). Since y + 7 = y − (−7), the center is (1, −7).","cimg":[["bank/fc8aa563_A.png"],["bank/fc8aa563_B.png"],["bank/fc8aa563_C.png"],["bank/fc8aa563_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"9f934297","k":15,"diff":"Medium","type":"spr","img":["bank/9f934297_stem.png"],"e":"SA = 2(lw + lh + wh) = 2(28×15 + 28×16 + 15×16) = 2(420 + 448 + 240) = 2,216.","ad":"2216","a":2216.0},{"id":"2855cb58","k":18,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/2855cb58_stem.png"],"e":"The right side of a circle's equation is r². Here r² = (7k)² = 49k², so the equation is (x − 16)² + (y − 17)² = 49k².","cimg":[["bank/2855cb58_A.png"],["bank/2855cb58_B.png"],["bank/2855cb58_C.png"],["bank/2855cb58_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"575f1e12","k":15,"diff":"Easy","type":"spr","img":["bank/575f1e12_stem.png"],"e":"The area of a rectangle is length × width: 34 × 29 = 986 cm².","ad":"986","a":986.0},{"id":"74d8b897","k":17,"diff":"Easy","type":"spr","img":["bank/74d8b897_stem.png"],"e":"To convert radians to degrees, multiply by 180/π: (9π/20)(180/π) = 9 × 9 = 81°.","ad":"81","a":81.0},{"id":"b4767bef","k":16,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/b4767bef_stem.png"],"e":"The perimeter is the sum of all three sides, so the third side is 18 − 4 − 6 = 8 cm.","cimg":[["bank/b4767bef_A.png"],["bank/b4767bef_B.png"],["bank/b4767bef_C.png"],["bank/b4767bef_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"ee540927","k":18,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/ee540927_stem.png"],"e":"Complete the square: x² + 58x + 841 + y² = 841, so (x + 29)² + y² = 841. The center is (−29, 0).","cimg":[["bank/ee540927_A.png"],["bank/ee540927_B.png"],["bank/ee540927_C.png"],["bank/ee540927_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"dc71597b","k":15,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/dc71597b_q.png"],"e":"V = (1/3)πr²(9) = 3πr² = (1/3)π, so r² = 1/9 and r = 1/3.","cimg":[["bank/dc71597b_A.png"],["bank/dc71597b_B.png"],["bank/dc71597b_C.png"],["bank/dc71597b_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"410bdbe6","k":16,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/410bdbe6_stem.png"],"e":"The angles of a triangle sum to 180°: 31 + 2b + 45 = 180. So 2b = 104 and b = 52.","cimg":[["bank/410bdbe6_A.png"],["bank/410bdbe6_B.png"],["bank/410bdbe6_C.png"],["bank/410bdbe6_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"a0cacec1","k":17,"diff":"Easy","type":"spr","img":["bank/a0cacec1_stem.png"],"e":"To convert radians to degrees, multiply by 180/π: (16π/15)(180/π) = 16 × 12 = 192°.","ad":"192","a":192.0},{"id":"1b2b20b9","k":18,"diff":"Medium","type":"spr","img":["bank/1b2b20b9_stem.png"],"e":"Moving the circle does not change its radius, so r² stays 7 and a = 7. Then 4a = 28.","ad":"28","a":28.0},{"id":"f811d345","k":17,"diff":"Medium","type":"spr","img":["bank/f811d345_stem.png"],"e":"Hypotenuse² = 24² + 21² = 576 + 441 = 1,017 = 9 × 113. So the hypotenuse is √1,017 = 3√113, and d = 113.","ad":"113","a":113.0},{"id":"c9931030","k":17,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/c9931030_stem.png"],"e":"TR = 52 is the hypotenuse, so the right angle is at S. Then tan T = RS/ST = 20/48 = 5/12. W corresponds to T, so tan W = 5/12.","cimg":[["bank/c9931030_A.png"],["bank/c9931030_B.png"],["bank/c9931030_C.png"],["bank/c9931030_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"a456f28c","k":16,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/a456f28c_stem.png"],"e":"Vertical angles are equal, so angle 2 = angle 1 = 72°.","cimg":[["bank/a456f28c_A.png"],["bank/a456f28c_B.png"],["bank/a456f28c_C.png"],["bank/a456f28c_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"9823f279","k":17,"diff":"Easy","type":"spr","img":["bank/9823f279_stem.png"],"e":"The two legs are equal (15 and 15), so this is an isosceles right triangle. Its two acute angles are equal, so x = 90/2 = 45.","ad":"45","a":45.0},{"id":"087cdcfd","k":16,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/087cdcfd_stem.png"],"e":"The angle above the horizontal line between x and z is vertical to y, so it also measures 75°. The angles along the straight line add to 180: x + y + z = 180, so z = 180 − 65 − 75 = 40.","cimg":[["bank/087cdcfd_A.png"],["bank/087cdcfd_B.png"],["bank/087cdcfd_C.png"],["bank/087cdcfd_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"6ae1360d","k":18,"diff":"Easy","type":"spr","img":["bank/6ae1360d_stem.png"],"e":"Area = πr² = π(2.1)² = 4.41π, so b = 4.41.","ad":"4.41","a":4.41},{"id":"c88183f7","k":15,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/c88183f7_stem.png"],"e":"Perimeter = 2(length + width) = 2(13 + 6) = 38.","cimg":[["bank/c88183f7_A.png"],["bank/c88183f7_B.png"],["bank/c88183f7_C.png"],["bank/c88183f7_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"6933b3d9","k":17,"diff":"Hard","type":"spr","img":["bank/6933b3d9_stem.png"],"e":"Angle RSW and angle WST together make the 90° angle at S, so they are complementary. The cosine of an angle equals the sine of its complement, so the difference is 0.","ad":"0","a":0.0},{"id":"afa3c48b","k":16,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/afa3c48b_stem.png"],"e":"The angle x and the 26° angle are on the same side of line ℓ, between the parallel lines (same-side interior angles), so they are supplementary. x = 180 − 26 = 154.","cimg":[["bank/afa3c48b_A.png"],["bank/afa3c48b_B.png"],["bank/afa3c48b_C.png"],["bank/afa3c48b_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"9ec76b54","k":17,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/9ec76b54_stem.png"],"e":"By the Pythagorean theorem, c² = 28² + 20² = 784 + 400 = 1,184 = 16 × 74. So c = 4√74.","cimg":[["bank/9ec76b54_A.png"],["bank/9ec76b54_B.png"],["bank/9ec76b54_C.png"],["bank/9ec76b54_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"992f4e93","k":16,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/992f4e93_stem.png"],"e":"The 64° angle (above k, right of j) and angle a (above ℓ, left of j) together form a straight angle once matched up through the parallel lines, so they are supplementary. a = 180 − 64 = 116.","cimg":[["bank/992f4e93_A.png"],["bank/992f4e93_B.png"],["bank/992f4e93_C.png"],["bank/992f4e93_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"f1747a6a","k":16,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/f1747a6a_stem.png"],"e":"The angles of a triangle sum to 180°, so ∠A = 180 − 52 − 17 = 111°.","cimg":[["bank/f1747a6a_A.png"],["bank/f1747a6a_B.png"],["bank/f1747a6a_C.png"],["bank/f1747a6a_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"23c5fcce","k":18,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/23c5fcce_stem.png"],"e":"The central angle AOC is a right angle, 90°, which is 90/360 = 1/4 of the circle. So arc AC = 36/4 = 9.","cimg":[["bank/23c5fcce_A.png"],["bank/23c5fcce_B.png"],["bank/23c5fcce_C.png"],["bank/23c5fcce_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"f1c1e971","k":17,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/f1c1e971_stem.png"],"e":"2π/3 radians = 120° and 5π/12 radians = 75°. So angle T = 120 + 75 = 195°.","cimg":[["bank/f1c1e971_A.png"],["bank/f1c1e971_B.png"],["bank/f1c1e971_C.png"],["bank/f1c1e971_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"6ab30ce3","k":17,"diff":"Hard","type":"mc","img":["bank/6ab30ce3_stem.png"],"e":"tan D = tan A = √3, so angle D = 60°. In right triangle DEF with the right angle at F, DF is adjacent to D and DE is the hypotenuse, so DE = DF/cos 60° = 125/(1/2) = 250.","cimg":[["bank/6ab30ce3_A.png"],["bank/6ab30ce3_B.png"],["bank/6ab30ce3_C.png"],["bank/6ab30ce3_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"1c3d613c","k":16,"diff":"Easy","type":"spr","img":["bank/1c3d613c_stem.png"],"e":"The side ratios are all equal, so the triangles are similar with A↔D, B↔E, C↔F. Corresponding angles are equal, so ∠EDF = ∠BAC = 20.","ad":"20","a":20.0},{"id":"2d521ca9","k":17,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/2d521ca9_stem.png"],"e":"180° = π radians, so 60° = 60 × π/180 = π/3, which is (1/3)π.","cimg":[["bank/2d521ca9_A.png"],["bank/2d521ca9_B.png"],["bank/2d521ca9_C.png"],["bank/2d521ca9_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"9acd101f","k":18,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/9acd101f_stem.png"],"e":"Circle A has center (0, 1). Moving it down 2 gives center (0, −1), and the radius is unchanged. So the equation is x² + (y + 1)² = 49.","cimg":[["bank/9acd101f_A.png"],["bank/9acd101f_B.png"],["bank/9acd101f_C.png"],["bank/9acd101f_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"e9c5bfb2","k":16,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/e9c5bfb2_stem.png"],"e":"AB corresponds to QR and AD corresponds to QT, so AD/10 = 12/5. Then AD = 24 inches.","cimg":[["bank/e9c5bfb2_A.png"],["bank/e9c5bfb2_B.png"],["bank/e9c5bfb2_C.png"],["bank/e9c5bfb2_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"48fb6483","k":16,"diff":"Hard","type":"spr","img":["bank/48fb6483_stem.png"],"e":"∠X = 180 − 90 − 63 = 27°. Since PQ ∥ XY, ∠QPZ = ∠YXZ = 27°, and ∠XPQ is supplementary to ∠QPZ, so ∠XPQ = 180 − 27 = 153.","ad":"153","a":153.0},{"id":"244ff6c4","k":17,"diff":"Hard","type":"mc","img":["bank/244ff6c4_stem.png"],"e":"92π/3 = 30π + 2π/3, and tangent repeats every π, so tan(92π/3) = tan(2π/3). The angle 2π/3 is in quadrant II, where tangent is negative, so tan(2π/3) = −√3.","cimg":[["bank/244ff6c4_A.png"],["bank/244ff6c4_B.png"],["bank/244ff6c4_C.png"],["bank/244ff6c4_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"010243e6","k":16,"diff":"Hard","type":"mc","img":["bank/010243e6_stem.png"],"e":"Both triangles have a right angle at P and L, and their legs are equal (2 and 2; 2 + k and 2 + k). So both are 45-45-90 triangles, giving t = 45 and ∠N = 45 = 90 − t.","cimg":[["bank/010243e6_A.png"],["bank/010243e6_B.png"],["bank/010243e6_C.png"],["bank/010243e6_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"08b7a3f5","k":15,"diff":"Easy","type":"spr","img":["bank/08b7a3f5_stem.png"],"e":"V = Bh, so 216 = B × 8 and B = 27 cm².","ad":"27","a":27.0},{"id":"1318dfea","k":16,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/1318dfea_stem.png"],"e":"Triangles WQX and YQZ are similar by angle-angle: the a° angles are equal and the angles at Q are vertical. The scale factor is WQ/YQ = 70/21 = 10/3, so YZ = WX × 3/10 = 60 × 3/10 = 18.","cimg":[["bank/1318dfea_A.png"],["bank/1318dfea_B.png"],["bank/1318dfea_C.png"],["bank/1318dfea_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"5733ce30","k":16,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/5733ce30_stem.png"],"e":"∠BCA = 180 − 110 = 70°, so ∠BAC = 70° too. Then x = 180 − 70 − 70 = 40.","cimg":[["bank/5733ce30_A.png"],["bank/5733ce30_B.png"],["bank/5733ce30_C.png"],["bank/5733ce30_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"0acfddb5","k":18,"diff":"Hard","type":"mc","img":["bank/0acfddb5_stem.png"],"e":"The perimeter is 2(168) + 2(MH) = 3,856, so MH = 1,760. A tangent is perpendicular to the radius, so GMH is a right triangle and GH = √(168² + 1,760²) = 1,768.","cimg":[["bank/0acfddb5_A.png"],["bank/0acfddb5_B.png"],["bank/0acfddb5_C.png"],["bank/0acfddb5_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"7a8ad237","k":16,"diff":"Medium","type":"spr","img":["bank/7a8ad237_stem.png"],"e":"Congruent triangles have equal corresponding angles: D = A = 69° and E = B = 90°. So F = 180 − 90 − 69 = 21.","ad":"21","a":21.0},{"id":"50774285","k":15,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/50774285_stem.png"],"e":"V = lwh, so 2,736 = 19 × 8 × h = 152h. Then h = 18 inches.","cimg":[["bank/50774285_A.png"],["bank/50774285_B.png"],["bank/50774285_C.png"],["bank/50774285_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"3b4b5b1e","k":16,"diff":"Easy","type":"spr","img":["bank/3b4b5b1e_stem.png"],"e":"Angle x and the 133° angle are next to each other along line j, so they form a straight angle. x = 180 − 133 = 47.","ad":"47","a":47.0},{"id":"29e9b28c","k":16,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/29e9b28c_stem.png"],"e":"The perimeter is x + y + z = 22, so z = 22 − 9 − 7 = 6.","cimg":[["bank/29e9b28c_A.png"],["bank/29e9b28c_B.png"],["bank/29e9b28c_C.png"],["bank/29e9b28c_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"5b4757df","k":16,"diff":"Hard","type":"spr","img":["bank/5b4757df_stem.png"],"e":"The area is (1/2)(RT)(ST) = (1/2)(72)(ST) = 792, so ST = 22. Since LK ∥ RT, triangle SLK is similar to triangle SRT with ratio 24/72 = 1/3, so SK = 22/3 and KT = 22 − 22/3 = 44/3.","ad":"44/3","tol":0.0011,"a":14.666666666666666},{"id":"ca2235f6","k":18,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/ca2235f6_stem.png"],"e":"A 45° arc is 45/360 = 1/8 of the circle. So the circumference is 8 × 3 = 24 inches.","cimg":[["bank/ca2235f6_A.png"],["bank/ca2235f6_B.png"],["bank/ca2235f6_C.png"],["bank/ca2235f6_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"856372ca","k":18,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/856372ca_q.png"],"e":"Center (h, k) = (−8, 6) and r = 5 give (x + 8)² + (y − 6)² = 25. Remember the right side is r², not r.","cimg":[["bank/856372ca_A.png"],["bank/856372ca_B.png"],["bank/856372ca_C.png"],["bank/856372ca_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"cf0d3050","k":16,"diff":"Easy","type":"spr","img":["bank/cf0d3050_stem.png"],"e":"The 110° angle at t (above t, left of c) corresponds to the angle above s and left of c, which is also 110°. Angle x is next to it along s, so x = 180 − 110 = 70.","ad":"70","a":70.0},{"id":"0bb39de4","k":16,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/0bb39de4_stem.png"],"e":"Congruent triangles have equal corresponding angles, so D = 18° and E = 90°. Then F = 180 − 90 − 18 = 72°.","cimg":[["bank/0bb39de4_A.png"],["bank/0bb39de4_B.png"],["bank/0bb39de4_C.png"],["bank/0bb39de4_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"1be8b6b2","k":15,"diff":"Hard","type":"mc","img":["bank/1be8b6b2_stem.png"],"e":"πr² = 5,929π, so r = 77. V = (1/3)(5,929π)h = 71,148π gives h = 36, and the slant height is √(77² + 36²) = √7,225 = 85.","cimg":[["bank/1be8b6b2_A.png"],["bank/1be8b6b2_B.png"],["bank/1be8b6b2_C.png"],["bank/1be8b6b2_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"9c0a0eca","k":15,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/9c0a0eca_stem.png"],"e":"The area of a triangle is (1/2) × base × height = (1/2)(10)(70) = 350 cm².","cimg":[["bank/9c0a0eca_A.png"],["bank/9c0a0eca_B.png"],["bank/9c0a0eca_C.png"],["bank/9c0a0eca_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"9d159400","k":18,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/9d159400_stem.png"],"e":"A circle touches the y-axis at exactly one point when the distance from its center to the y-axis (the absolute value of the center’s x-coordinate) equals the radius. All radii are 4, and only (x − 4)² + (y − 9)² = 16 has center x-coordinate 4.","cimg":[["bank/9d159400_A.png"],["bank/9d159400_B.png"],["bank/9d159400_C.png"],["bank/9d159400_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"379ffefb","k":17,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/379ffefb_stem.png"],"e":"By the Pythagorean theorem, hypotenuse² = 11² + 9² = 121 + 81 = 202, so the hypotenuse is √202.","cimg":[["bank/379ffefb_A.png"],["bank/379ffefb_B.png"],["bank/379ffefb_C.png"],["bank/379ffefb_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"bf8d843e","k":17,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/bf8d843e_stem.png"],"e":"In right triangle BDC with angle C = 60° and BC = 12, BD = 12·sin 60° = 6√3. In right triangle ABD with angle ABD = 30°, AD = BD·tan 30° = 6√3 · (1/√3) = 6.","cimg":[["bank/bf8d843e_A.png"],["bank/bf8d843e_B.png"],["bank/bf8d843e_C.png"],["bank/bf8d843e_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"3453aafc","k":15,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/3453aafc_stem.png"],"e":"Area of a rectangle is length × width = 36 × 34 = 1,224 square centimeters.","cimg":[["bank/3453aafc_A.png"],["bank/3453aafc_B.png"],["bank/3453aafc_C.png"],["bank/3453aafc_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"aef4fd8a","k":15,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/aef4fd8a_stem.png"],"e":"The area of a square is side × side, so the area is 94 · 94 cm². Note 4 · 94 would be the perimeter.","cimg":[["bank/aef4fd8a_A.png"],["bank/aef4fd8a_B.png"],["bank/aef4fd8a_C.png"],["bank/aef4fd8a_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"43236565","k":16,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/43236565_stem.png"],"e":"The angle x° (above line n, left of k) and the 145° angle (below n, right of k) are vertical angles formed by lines n and k, so they are equal: x = 145.","cimg":[["bank/43236565_A.png"],["bank/43236565_B.png"],["bank/43236565_C.png"],["bank/43236565_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"981275d2","k":18,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/981275d2_stem.png"],"e":"The center is (6, −5), which is the midpoint of diameter PQ. So Q = (2·6 − 10, 2·(−5) − (−5)) = (2, −5).","cimg":[["bank/981275d2_A.png"],["bank/981275d2_B.png"],["bank/981275d2_C.png"],["bank/981275d2_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"d71550d0","k":16,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/d71550d0_stem.png"],"e":"The angles r° and s° are on opposite sides of the intersection point, so they are vertical angles and are equal. Therefore s = 53.","cimg":[["bank/d71550d0_A.png"],["bank/d71550d0_B.png"],["bank/d71550d0_C.png"],["bank/d71550d0_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"89661424","k":18,"diff":"Hard","type":"spr","img":["bank/89661424_stem.png"],"e":"The equation is (x + 5)² + (y − 2)² = 81. Expanding gives x² + 10x + 25 + y² − 4y + 4 = 81, so x² + y² + 10x − 4y − 52 = 0 and c = −52.","ad":"-52","a":-52.0},{"id":"196e8e6e","k":18,"diff":"Hard","type":"mc","img":["bank/196e8e6e_stem.png"],"e":"The radius is CA = √(1² + (√102)²) = √103. Since angle ACB is a right angle and CA = CB = √103, AB = √(103 + 103) = √206.","cimg":[["bank/196e8e6e_A.png"],["bank/196e8e6e_B.png"],["bank/196e8e6e_C.png"],["bank/196e8e6e_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"d03e29f1","k":18,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/d03e29f1_stem.png"],"e":"A circle (x − h)² + (y − k)² = r² has radius r. Here r² = 81, so r = 9, not 81.","cimg":[["bank/d03e29f1_A.png"],["bank/d03e29f1_B.png"],["bank/d03e29f1_C.png"],["bank/d03e29f1_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"7c25b0dc","k":17,"diff":"Medium","type":"spr","img":["bank/7c25b0dc_stem.png"],"e":"The diagonal and the two sides form a right triangle: (3√17)² = 3² + L², so 153 = 9 + L², L² = 144, and L = 12.","ad":"12","a":12.0},{"id":"36661021","k":17,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/36661021_stem.png"],"e":"By the Pythagorean theorem, c² = 9² + 6² = 81 + 36 = 117, so c = √117 ≈ 10.8.","cimg":[["bank/36661021_A.png"],["bank/36661021_B.png"],["bank/36661021_C.png"],["bank/36661021_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"e80d62c6","k":18,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/e80d62c6_stem.png"],"e":"Circle A has center (0, 2). Shifting down 4 units moves the center to (0, −2), so circle B is x² + (y + 2)² = 36.","cimg":[["bank/e80d62c6_A.png"],["bank/e80d62c6_B.png"],["bank/e80d62c6_C.png"],["bank/e80d62c6_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"f243c383","k":15,"diff":"Hard","type":"mc","img":["bank/f243c383_stem.png"],"e":"Each prism has surface area K = 2s² + 4·90s = 2s² + 360s. Gluing hides two bases, so 2K − 2s² = (92/47)K, which gives (2/47)K = 2s², so K = 47s². Then 2s² + 360s = 47s², so 45s = 360 and s = 8.","cimg":[["bank/f243c383_A.png"],["bank/f243c383_B.png"],["bank/f243c383_C.png"],["bank/f243c383_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"95ba2d09","k":18,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/95ba2d09_q.png"],"e":"Angle QOR = 180° − 30° − 30° = 120°, and 120° × π/180° = 2π/3 radians.","cimg":[["bank/95ba2d09_A.png"],["bank/95ba2d09_B.png"],["bank/95ba2d09_C.png"],["bank/95ba2d09_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"adae6543","k":16,"diff":"Hard","type":"mc","img":["bank/adae6543_stem.png"],"e":"Since LM ∥ PQ, triangles LMR and QPR are similar, so MR/RP = LR/RQ: 6/11 = 7/RQ, giving RQ = 77/6. Then LQ = LR + RQ = 7 + 77/6 = 119/6.","cimg":[["bank/adae6543_A.png"],["bank/adae6543_B.png"],["bank/adae6543_C.png"],["bank/adae6543_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"6dd463ca","k":16,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/6dd463ca_stem.png"],"e":"Because BD ∥ AE, angle CEA equals angle CDB = 58° (corresponding angles). In triangle ACE, angle CAE = 180° − 62° − 58° = 60°.","cimg":[["bank/6dd463ca_A.png"],["bank/6dd463ca_B.png"],["bank/6dd463ca_C.png"],["bank/6dd463ca_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"0815a5af","k":18,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/0815a5af_stem.png"],"e":"Half the circumference is 72π, and arcs PQ and PS together make a semicircle, so PQ + 2·PQ = 72π gives PQ = 24π and PS = 48π. Arc QR is cut off by the angle vertical to angle POS, so arc QR = 48π.","cimg":[["bank/0815a5af_A.png"],["bank/0815a5af_B.png"],["bank/0815a5af_C.png"],["bank/0815a5af_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"f731d88b","k":16,"diff":"Hard","type":"spr","img":["bank/f731d88b_stem.png"],"e":"Walking around the convex pentagon, the direction turns from AB to DE by 180° because the sides are parallel and traversed in opposite directions. The exterior angles at B and D are 180 − 139 = 41 and 180 − 174 = 6, so the exterior angle at C is 180 − 41 − 6 = 133, and angle C = 180 − 133 = 47 degrees.","ad":"47","a":47.0},{"id":"93de3f84","k":15,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/93de3f84_stem.png"],"e":"Volume is V = πr²h. Doubling the radius multiplies V by 2² = 4, and halving the height multiplies it by 1/2, so the new volume is 22 × 4 × 1/2 = 44.","cimg":[["bank/93de3f84_A.png"],["bank/93de3f84_B.png"],["bank/93de3f84_C.png"],["bank/93de3f84_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"16d66178","k":17,"diff":"Hard","type":"mc","img":["bank/16d66178_stem.png"],"e":"Since 24° and 66° are complementary, sin 24° = cos 66° and sin 66° = cos 24°. Substituting gives (cos 66°)(cos 66°) + (cos 24°)(cos 24°) = (cos 66°)² + (cos 24°)².","cimg":[["bank/16d66178_A.png"],["bank/16d66178_B.png"],["bank/16d66178_C.png"],["bank/16d66178_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"f1251f35","k":17,"diff":"Easy","type":"spr","img":["bank/f1251f35_stem.png"],"e":"Cosine is adjacent over hypotenuse. For angle Z, the adjacent side is ZY = 560 and the hypotenuse is XZ = 565, so cos Z = 560/565 and c = 565.","ad":"565","a":565.0},{"id":"5b918ebb","k":16,"diff":"Easy","type":"spr","img":["bank/5b918ebb_stem.png"],"e":"The 162° angle (above r, left of n) and x° (above s, left of n) are corresponding angles formed by the transversal n and parallel lines r and s, so x = 162.","ad":"162","a":162.0},{"id":"c9f8d1e9","k":17,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/c9f8d1e9_stem.png"],"e":"By the Pythagorean theorem, c² = a² + b², so c = √(4² + 5²). Adding the legs or multiplying them does not give the hypotenuse.","cimg":[["bank/c9f8d1e9_A.png"],["bank/c9f8d1e9_B.png"],["bank/c9f8d1e9_C.png"],["bank/c9f8d1e9_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"f60bb551","k":15,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/f60bb551_stem.png"],"e":"Area = length × width, so 630 = 70 × w and w = 630 ÷ 70 = 9 inches.","cimg":[["bank/f60bb551_A.png"],["bank/f60bb551_B.png"],["bank/f60bb551_C.png"],["bank/f60bb551_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"d2047497","k":15,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/d2047497_stem.png"],"e":"Area of a rectangle = length × width = 17 × 7 = 119 cm². Adding the sides (24) gives half the perimeter, not the area.","cimg":[["bank/d2047497_A.png"],["bank/d2047497_B.png"],["bank/d2047497_C.png"],["bank/d2047497_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"a71617d3","k":17,"diff":"Easy","type":"spr","img":["bank/a71617d3_stem.png"],"e":"The two legs are equal (32 and 32), so the right triangle is isosceles and its two acute angles are equal: x = (180 − 90)/2 = 45.","ad":"45","a":45.0},{"id":"a5aee181","k":17,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/a5aee181_stem.png"],"e":"The diagonal is the hypotenuse of a right triangle with the sides as legs: (5√17)² = 5² + L², so 425 = 25 + L², L² = 400, and L = 20.","cimg":[["bank/a5aee181_A.png"],["bank/a5aee181_B.png"],["bank/a5aee181_C.png"],["bank/a5aee181_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"4efea6a3","k":15,"diff":"Easy","type":"spr","img":["bank/4efea6a3_stem.png"],"e":"Area = longer side × shorter side, so 57 = 19 × w, giving w = 57 ÷ 19 = 3 inches.","ad":"3","a":3.0},{"id":"fb58c0db","k":18,"diff":"Medium","type":"spr","img":["bank/fb58c0db_stem.png"],"e":"The circumference is 2π(1) = 2π. The fraction is (π/3) ÷ (2π) = 1/6.","ad":"1/6","tol":0.0011,"a":0.16666666666666666},{"id":"ae041e52","k":18,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/ae041e52_stem.png"],"e":"The diagonal of an inscribed square is a diameter: 2 × (20√2/2) = 20√2. A square's diagonal is side × √2, so side = 20√2 ÷ √2 = 20.","cimg":[["bank/ae041e52_A.png"],["bank/ae041e52_B.png"],["bank/ae041e52_C.png"],["bank/ae041e52_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"c6dff223","k":17,"diff":"Hard","type":"spr","img":["bank/c6dff223_stem.png"],"e":"Similar triangles have equal corresponding angles, so sin D = sin A. With tan A = 21/20, take legs 21 and 20; the hypotenuse is √(21² + 20²) = 29, so sin A = 21/29 = sin D. The 2.9 scale factor does not affect trig ratios.","ad":"21/29","tol":0.0011,"a":0.7241379310344828},{"id":"eb70d2d0","k":15,"diff":"Hard","type":"spr","img":["bank/eb70d2d0_stem.png"],"e":"The points are (−3, 4), (5, 3), and (4, −3). Enclose them in an 8 by 7 rectangle (area 56) and subtract the three outside right triangles with areas 4, 3, and 24.5: 56 − 31.5 = 24.5 (also 49/2).","ad":"24.5","a":24.5},{"id":"64d1f49f","k":16,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/64d1f49f_stem.png"],"e":"The angles w° and z° are on opposite sides of the intersection point, so they are vertical angles and are equal: z = 136.","cimg":[["bank/64d1f49f_A.png"],["bank/64d1f49f_B.png"],["bank/64d1f49f_C.png"],["bank/64d1f49f_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"f329442c","k":15,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/f329442c_stem.png"],"e":"Area scales with the square of the radius. The radius ratio is 129n/3n = 43, so the area ratio is 43² = 1,849, not 43.","cimg":[["bank/f329442c_A.png"],["bank/f329442c_B.png"],["bank/f329442c_C.png"],["bank/f329442c_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"f39f88b7","k":15,"diff":"Easy","type":"spr","img":["bank/f39f88b7_stem.png"],"e":"Area of a triangle = (1/2) × base × height = (1/2)(40)(90) = 1,800 square centimeters.","ad":"1800","a":1800.0},{"id":"92eb236a","k":17,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/92eb236a_q.png"],"e":"The acute angles are complementary, so the tangent of one is the reciprocal of the other's: 1 ÷ (√3/3) = 3/√3.","cimg":[["bank/92eb236a_A.png"],["bank/92eb236a_B.png"],["bank/92eb236a_C.png"],["bank/92eb236a_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"ae33e0a1","k":15,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/ae33e0a1_stem.png"],"e":"The radius is half the diameter, 11 cm. Volume = πr²h = π(11²)(6) = 726π cubic centimeters.","cimg":[["bank/ae33e0a1_A.png"],["bank/ae33e0a1_B.png"],["bank/ae33e0a1_C.png"],["bank/ae33e0a1_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"13d9a1c3","k":17,"diff":"Easy","type":"spr","img":["bank/13d9a1c3_stem.png"],"e":"PQ is the side opposite the 30° angle and QR = 8 is the hypotenuse. In a 30-60-90 triangle the side opposite 30° is half the hypotenuse, so PQ = 8 × sin 30° = 4.","ad":"4","a":4.0},{"id":"76670c80","k":15,"diff":"Easy","type":"spr","img":["bank/76670c80_stem.png"],"e":"A square has 4 equal sides, so its perimeter is 4 × 45 = 180.","ad":"180","a":180.0},{"id":"17912810","k":16,"diff":"Hard","type":"spr","img":["bank/17912810_stem.png"],"e":"At the s–q intersection, the angle inside the triangle formed by q, r, and s is 180 − 122 = 58; the angle at the r–s intersection is 43 (vertical to a), so the angle between r and q is 180 − 58 − 43 = 79. At line t, the angle below t between t and r is 180 − 79 = 101 (since q ∥ t), and it is split into two angles of w°, so 2w = 101 and w = 50.5.","ad":"101/2","tol":0.0011,"a":50.5},{"id":"4420e500","k":15,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/4420e500_stem.png"],"e":"Area of a rectangle = length × width = 4 × 2 = 8 cm². Adding the sides gives 6, which is half the perimeter, not the area.","cimg":[["bank/4420e500_A.png"],["bank/4420e500_B.png"],["bank/4420e500_C.png"],["bank/4420e500_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"099526fc","k":17,"diff":"Hard","type":"mc","img":["bank/099526fc_stem.png"],"e":"The segment runs from (−6, 4) to (3, 10), so its length is √(9² + 6²) = √117 = 3√13. The area of a right triangle is (1/2)(leg)(leg), so 36√13 = (1/2)(3√13)(L), giving L = 24.","cimg":[["bank/099526fc_A.png"],["bank/099526fc_B.png"],["bank/099526fc_C.png"],["bank/099526fc_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"c4e5e23c","k":15,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/c4e5e23c_stem.png"],"e":"Square N has side √49 = 7 ft, so square M has side 6 × 7 = 42 ft and area 42² = 1,764 square feet. Equivalently, the area scales by 6² = 36: 36 × 49 = 1,764.","cimg":[["bank/c4e5e23c_A.png"],["bank/c4e5e23c_B.png"],["bank/c4e5e23c_C.png"],["bank/c4e5e23c_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"a67b9f88","k":17,"diff":"Medium","type":"spr","img":["bank/a67b9f88_stem.png"],"e":"The hypotenuse is TR = 53, so TS = √(53² − 105) = √(2809 − 105) = √2704 = 52. Sin R = opposite/hypotenuse = TS/TR = 52/53.","ad":"52/53","tol":0.0011,"a":0.9811320754716981},{"id":"165c30c4","k":15,"diff":"Easy","type":"spr","img":["bank/165c30c4_stem.png"],"e":"Area of a rectangle = length × width = 64 × 32 = 2,048 square inches.","ad":"2048","a":2048.0},{"id":"694b7fce","k":16,"diff":"Hard","type":"spr","img":["bank/694b7fce_stem.png"],"e":"In right triangle ABC, BC = √(34 − 9) = 5. Triangles ABC and ADE are similar, with AE = 3 + 21 = 24, which is 8 times AC, so DE = 8 × 5 = 40. Area of ADE = (1/2)(24)(40) = 480.","ad":"480","a":480.0},{"id":"f7e626b2","k":15,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/f7e626b2_stem.png"],"e":"Surface area = 2(lw + lh + wh) = 2(4·5 + 4·6 + 5·6) = 2(20 + 24 + 30) = 148. Note 120 is the volume.","cimg":[["bank/f7e626b2_A.png"],["bank/f7e626b2_B.png"],["bank/f7e626b2_C.png"],["bank/f7e626b2_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"585a9138","k":16,"diff":"Medium","type":"spr","img":["bank/585a9138_stem.png"],"e":"Since the triangles are congruent, angle D = angle A = 27° and angle E = 90°. In triangle DEF, angle F = 180° − 90° − 27° = 63°.","ad":"63","a":63.0},{"id":"2be01bd9","k":17,"diff":"Hard","type":"spr","img":["bank/2be01bd9_stem.png"],"e":"In right triangle ABC (right angle at C), tan A = BC/AC = 50/7, so tan B = AC/BC = 7/50. Angle E corresponds to angle B, and similar triangles have equal angles, so tan E = 7/50.","ad":"7/50","tol":0.0011,"a":0.14},{"id":"3828f53d","k":16,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/3828f53d_stem.png"],"e":"At line n, the 130° angle means line k makes a 50° angle with the parallel lines, so the a° angle at line m is 50° (and the other a° is also 50°). Line ℓ is perpendicular to m, so in the triangle formed by m, ℓ, and the line through b, b = 180 − 90 − 50 = 40.","cimg":[["bank/3828f53d_A.png"],["bank/3828f53d_B.png"],["bank/3828f53d_C.png"],["bank/3828f53d_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"a38c0183","k":18,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/a38c0183_stem.png"],"e":"Circle A has center (−2, 0) and radius 3. Shifting down 6 gives center (−2, −6), and doubling the radius gives r = 6, so r² = 36 = (4)(9). The equation is (x + 2)² + (y + 6)² = (4)(9).","cimg":[["bank/a38c0183_A.png"],["bank/a38c0183_B.png"],["bank/a38c0183_C.png"],["bank/a38c0183_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"739f1bbc","k":16,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/739f1bbc_stem.png"],"e":"An equilateral triangle has all three sides equal. Since AB = BC = 4,680 mm, AC must also be 4,680 mm.","cimg":[["bank/739f1bbc_A.png"],["bank/739f1bbc_B.png"],["bank/739f1bbc_C.png"],["bank/739f1bbc_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"dba6a25a","k":16,"diff":"Medium","type":"spr","img":["bank/dba6a25a_stem.png"],"e":"In right triangle CBD, CD = √(8² + 6²) = 10. Since BD ∥ AE, triangle CBD is similar to triangle CAE with scale factor 18/6 = 3, so CE = 3 × 10 = 30.","ad":"30","a":30.0},{"id":"c984f1a5","k":15,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/c984f1a5_stem.png"],"e":"A hemisphere's volume is half of (4/3)πr³, which is (2/3)πr³ = (2/3)π(27³) ≈ 41,224 cubic inches, closest to 41,200.","cimg":[["bank/c984f1a5_A.png"],["bank/c984f1a5_B.png"],["bank/c984f1a5_C.png"],["bank/c984f1a5_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"acd30391","k":18,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/acd30391_stem.png"],"e":"A point is inside the circle if (x + 3)² + (y − 1)² < 25. For (3, 2): 6² + 1² = 37 > 25, so it is outside; the other points give 20, 0, and 10, all less than 25.","cimg":[["bank/acd30391_A.png"],["bank/acd30391_B.png"],["bank/acd30391_C.png"],["bank/acd30391_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"4ff7b652","k":16,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/4ff7b652_stem.png"],"e":"Corresponding angles of similar triangles are equal. Since M corresponds to Q, angle Q = angle M = 53°.","cimg":[["bank/4ff7b652_A.png"],["bank/4ff7b652_B.png"],["bank/4ff7b652_C.png"],["bank/4ff7b652_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"053e5e9f","k":17,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/053e5e9f_stem.png"],"e":"Side RS = 25 is opposite angle Q, and QS is the hypotenuse, so sin Q = 25/QS. Solving gives QS = 25/sin Q.","cimg":[["bank/053e5e9f_A.png"],["bank/053e5e9f_B.png"],["bank/053e5e9f_C.png"],["bank/053e5e9f_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"8027db3f","k":17,"diff":"Medium","type":"spr","img":["bank/8027db3f_stem.png"],"e":"With the right angle at J, cos K = JK/KL = 24/51, so take JK = 24 and KL = 51. Then JL = √(51² − 24²) = 45, and cos L = JL/KL = 45/51 = 15/17.","ad":"15/17","tol":0.0011,"a":0.8823529411764706},{"id":"e0d2e21a","k":16,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/e0d2e21a_stem.png"],"e":"A dilation keeps angle measures the same; only side lengths are multiplied by 3. Angle X corresponds to angle A, so angle X = 60°.","cimg":[["bank/e0d2e21a_A.png"],["bank/e0d2e21a_B.png"],["bank/e0d2e21a_C.png"],["bank/e0d2e21a_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"cecbdeba","k":15,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/cecbdeba_stem.png"],"e":"Volume of a cylinder = base area × height, so 432 = 24 × h and h = 432 ÷ 24 = 18 cm.","cimg":[["bank/cecbdeba_A.png"],["bank/cecbdeba_B.png"],["bank/cecbdeba_C.png"],["bank/cecbdeba_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"42b4493b","k":16,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/42b4493b_stem.png"],"e":"The two acute angles of a right triangle add to 90°, so the other angle is 90° − 51° = 39°.","cimg":[["bank/42b4493b_A.png"],["bank/42b4493b_B.png"],["bank/42b4493b_C.png"],["bank/42b4493b_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"d683a9cc","k":15,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/d683a9cc_stem.png"],"e":"V = lwh = 6 × 2 × 3 = 36 cubic centimeters. Adding the edges (11) does not give volume.","cimg":[["bank/d683a9cc_A.png"],["bank/d683a9cc_B.png"],["bank/d683a9cc_C.png"],["bank/d683a9cc_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"1bf809b5","k":17,"diff":"Easy","type":"spr","img":["bank/1bf809b5_stem.png"],"e":"Cosine is adjacent over hypotenuse. For angle x, the adjacent leg is 11 and the hypotenuse is 28, so cos x° = 11/28.","ad":"11/28","tol":0.0011,"a":0.39285714285714285},{"id":"14e7c1f4","k":17,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/14e7c1f4_stem.png"],"e":"cos Q = sin R means Q and R are complementary, so (x + 61) + (4x + 4) = 90. Then 5x + 65 = 90 and x = 5.","cimg":[["bank/14e7c1f4_A.png"],["bank/14e7c1f4_B.png"],["bank/14e7c1f4_C.png"],["bank/14e7c1f4_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"a2e76b60","k":15,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/a2e76b60_stem.png"],"e":"The can's volume is base area × height = 75 × 10 = 750 cm³. The fruit fills what the syrup does not: 750 − 110 = 640 cm³.","cimg":[["bank/a2e76b60_A.png"],["bank/a2e76b60_B.png"],["bank/a2e76b60_C.png"],["bank/a2e76b60_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"468613c0","k":15,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/468613c0_stem.png"],"e":"Area of a triangle = (1/2) × base × height = (1/2)(56)(112) = 3,136 square centimeters.","cimg":[["bank/468613c0_A.png"],["bank/468613c0_B.png"],["bank/468613c0_C.png"],["bank/468613c0_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"145337bc","k":17,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/145337bc_stem.png"],"e":"A right triangle with two 45° angles is isosceles, so its legs are equal: x = 24. The hypotenuse would be 24√2.","cimg":[["bank/145337bc_A.png"],["bank/145337bc_B.png"],["bank/145337bc_C.png"],["bank/145337bc_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"36200a38","k":16,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/36200a38_stem.png"],"e":"The third angle of the triangle is 180° − 70° − 50° = 60°. The angle x° lies beside this vertex angle on a straight line where the extended sides cross, so x = 180 − 60 = 120.","cimg":[["bank/36200a38_A.png"],["bank/36200a38_B.png"],["bank/36200a38_C.png"],["bank/36200a38_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"a490003a","k":15,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/a490003a_stem.png"],"e":"The length is 7 + 40 = 47 cm, so the area is 47 × 7 = 329 square centimeters. Don't use 40 as the length.","cimg":[["bank/a490003a_A.png"],["bank/a490003a_B.png"],["bank/a490003a_C.png"],["bank/a490003a_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"95ca2683","k":16,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/95ca2683_stem.png"],"e":"The angles of a triangle sum to 180°, so angle C = 180° − 54° − 90° = 36°. Since k/2 = 36, k = 72. Don't stop at 36, which is the angle itself.","cimg":[["bank/95ca2683_A.png"],["bank/95ca2683_B.png"],["bank/95ca2683_C.png"],["bank/95ca2683_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"306264ab","k":17,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/306264ab_stem.png"],"e":"The longest side, √80, is the hypotenuse, so the legs are 2√2 and 6√2. Area = (1/2)(2√2)(6√2) = (1/2)(12 × 2) = 12.","cimg":[["bank/306264ab_A.png"],["bank/306264ab_B.png"],["bank/306264ab_C.png"],["bank/306264ab_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"6a3fbec3","k":16,"diff":"Hard","type":"spr","img":["bank/6a3fbec3_stem.png"],"e":"Angle ABC is a right angle (marked in the figure) and BD is the altitude to the hypotenuse, so triangles ADB and BDC are similar: AD/BD = BD/DC. Then 8/6 = 6/DC, so DC = 36/8 = 4.5.","ad":"9/2","tol":0.0011,"a":4.5},{"id":"37dde49f","k":15,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/37dde49f_stem.png"],"e":"Set 7πk³/48 = 473, so k³ = 473 × 48/(7π) ≈ 1032.4, and k ≈ 10.11 cm.","cimg":[["bank/37dde49f_A.png"],["bank/37dde49f_B.png"],["bank/37dde49f_C.png"],["bank/37dde49f_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"f67255ea","k":16,"diff":"Hard","type":"spr","img":["bank/f67255ea_stem.png"],"e":"Each obtuse angle is supplementary to an acute angle: 180 − (9x − 560) = 740 − 9x. Then (9x − 560) + 3(740 − 9x) = 9x − 560 + 2220 − 27x = −18x + 1660, so w = 1660.","ad":"1660","a":1660.0},{"id":"02b02213","k":15,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/02b02213_stem.png"],"e":"Perimeter = 2(length + width) = 2(4 + 9) = 26 inches. Note 13 is only half the perimeter and 36 would be the area.","cimg":[["bank/02b02213_A.png"],["bank/02b02213_B.png"],["bank/02b02213_C.png"],["bank/02b02213_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"82c8325f","k":18,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/82c8325f_stem.png"],"e":"With center (−4, 5) the equation is (x + 4)² + (y − 5)² = r². Plugging in (−8, 8): (−4)² + 3² = 16 + 9 = 25, so r² = 25.","cimg":[["bank/82c8325f_A.png"],["bank/82c8325f_B.png"],["bank/82c8325f_C.png"],["bank/82c8325f_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"c0b53183","k":18,"diff":"Hard","type":"spr","img":["bank/c0b53183_stem.png"],"e":"A tangent is perpendicular to the radius, so triangles OAE and OUE are right triangles with hypotenuse OE = 510 and leg 78 (OA = OU = 78). The tangent length is √(510² − 78²) = 504. The area is 2 × (1/2)(78)(504) = 39,312.","ad":"39312","a":39312.0},{"id":"459dd6c5","k":15,"diff":"Medium","type":"spr","img":["bank/459dd6c5_stem.png"],"e":"When lengths are scaled by 4, areas are scaled by 4² = 16. So the area of DEF is 270 ÷ 16 = 16.875 (135/8) square inches.","ad":"135/8","tol":0.0011,"a":16.875},{"id":"603c18ad","k":17,"diff":"Hard","type":"mc","img":["bank/603c18ad_stem.png"],"e":"In right triangle XWY, tan Y = WX/WY = 429/572 = 3/4. Since angle X = 90°, angles Y and Z are complementary, so tan Z = 1/tan Y = 4/3.","cimg":[["bank/603c18ad_A.png"],["bank/603c18ad_B.png"],["bank/603c18ad_C.png"],["bank/603c18ad_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"6585d841","k":18,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/6585d841_stem.png"],"e":"Rewrite as x² + 14x + y² − 6y = 109 and complete the square: (x + 7)² + (y − 3)² = 109 + 49 + 9 = 167. The radius is √167.","cimg":[["bank/6585d841_A.png"],["bank/6585d841_B.png"],["bank/6585d841_C.png"],["bank/6585d841_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"3b44439b","k":16,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/3b44439b_stem.png"],"e":"The angles x° and 142° lie on the same side of line q on either side of t, so together they form a straight angle: x + 142 = 180.","cimg":[["bank/3b44439b_A.png"],["bank/3b44439b_B.png"],["bank/3b44439b_C.png"],["bank/3b44439b_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"1efd7ef3","k":17,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/1efd7ef3_stem.png"],"e":"42π is 21 full rotations of 2π, so it ends at the same spot as angle 0 on the unit circle. Therefore sin 42π = sin 0 = 0.","cimg":[["bank/1efd7ef3_A.png"],["bank/1efd7ef3_B.png"],["bank/1efd7ef3_C.png"],["bank/1efd7ef3_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"9d2e7037","k":15,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/9d2e7037_stem.png"],"e":"Area of a rectangle = length × width = 56 × 28 = 1,568 square inches.","cimg":[["bank/9d2e7037_A.png"],["bank/9d2e7037_B.png"],["bank/9d2e7037_C.png"],["bank/9d2e7037_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"25da87f8","k":17,"diff":"Hard","type":"spr","img":["bank/25da87f8_stem.png"],"e":"A 30-60-90 triangle has sides s, s√3, and 2s, so its perimeter is s(3 + √3). Since 18 + 6√3 = 6(3 + √3), s = 6 and the longest side (hypotenuse) is 2s = 12.","ad":"12","a":12.0},{"id":"310c87fe","k":15,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/310c87fe_stem.png"],"e":"A cube has 6 equal square faces, so each face has area 54 ÷ 6 = 9 and the edge is 3 m. The volume is 3³ = 27 cubic meters.","cimg":[["bank/310c87fe_A.png"],["bank/310c87fe_B.png"],["bank/310c87fe_C.png"],["bank/310c87fe_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"cf53cb56","k":15,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/cf53cb56_stem.png"],"e":"The vertices are (0, 5), (−5, 0), (0, −5), and (5, 0), so each diagonal is 10. A square's area is (diagonal²)/2 = 100/2 = 50. Equivalently, the side is 5√2 and (5√2)² = 50.","cimg":[["bank/cf53cb56_A.png"],["bank/cf53cb56_B.png"],["bank/cf53cb56_C.png"],["bank/cf53cb56_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"b96ff36e","k":18,"diff":"Medium","type":"spr","img":["bank/b96ff36e_stem.png"],"e":"Substitute x = 6: (6 − 3)² + (c − 5)² = 9, so 9 + (c − 5)² = 9, (c − 5)² = 0, and c = 5. The point (6, 5) is the rightmost point of the circle.","ad":"5","a":5.0},{"id":"85939da5","k":13,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/85939da5_stem.png"],"e":"The margin of error gives a plausible range of 30% ± 3%, or 27% to 33%, for all US teens. 35% is outside that range, so it is doubtful; values outside the interval are not impossible, and 33% is not certain.","cimg":[["bank/85939da5_A.png"],["bank/85939da5_B.png"],["bank/85939da5_C.png"],["bank/85939da5_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"3c8fdc40","k":8,"diff":"Easy","type":"spr","img":["bank/3c8fdc40_stem.png"],"e":"There are 60 minutes in an hour, so 42 posters per minute × 60 minutes per hour = 2,520 posters per hour.","ad":"2520","a":2520.0},{"id":"eccbf957","k":12,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/eccbf957_stem.png"],"e":"There are 14 equally likely outcomes and only one face shows a 2, so the probability is 1/14.","cimg":[["bank/eccbf957_A.png"],["bank/eccbf957_B.png"],["bank/eccbf957_C.png"],["bank/eccbf957_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"affb2315","k":13,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/affb2315_stem.png"],"e":"Apply the sample percentage to the whole club: 20% of 55 = 0.20 × 55 = 11 students.","cimg":[["bank/affb2315_A.png"],["bank/affb2315_B.png"],["bank/affb2315_C.png"],["bank/affb2315_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"954943a4","k":9,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/954943a4_stem.png"],"e":"Each serving provides 5% of the daily potassium allowance, so x servings provide 5x percent, giving p = 5x. The percent adds up linearly, not exponentially.","cimg":[["bank/954943a4_A.png"],["bank/954943a4_B.png"],["bank/954943a4_C.png"],["bank/954943a4_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"1baffbcf","k":9,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/1baffbcf_stem.png"],"e":"0.35x means 35% of x remains, so x was decreased by 100% − 35% = 65%. 35% would be the amount kept, not the decrease.","cimg":[["bank/1baffbcf_A.png"],["bank/1baffbcf_B.png"],["bank/1baffbcf_C.png"],["bank/1baffbcf_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"a5b069b4","k":10,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/a5b069b4_stem.png"],"e":"Order the 8 values: 4, 4, 4, 5, 5, 6, 10, 18. With an even count, the median is the average of the 4th and 5th values: (5 + 5)/2 = 5.","cimg":[["bank/a5b069b4_A.png"],["bank/a5b069b4_B.png"],["bank/a5b069b4_C.png"],["bank/a5b069b4_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"b1b5300b","k":12,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/b1b5300b_q.png"],"e":"2 hybrid cars cost no more than $25,000, out of 14 cars: 2/14 = 1/7.","cimg":[["bank/b1b5300b_A.png"],["bank/b1b5300b_B.png"],["bank/b1b5300b_C.png"],["bank/b1b5300b_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"d28c29e1","k":8,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/d28c29e1_stem.png"],"e":"There are 3,600 seconds in an hour, so 4.76 miles per second × 3,600 = 17,136 miles per hour.","cimg":[["bank/d28c29e1_A.png"],["bank/d28c29e1_B.png"],["bank/d28c29e1_C.png"],["bank/d28c29e1_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"1adb39f0","k":11,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/1adb39f0_stem.png"],"e":"At x = 1 the data point is at about y = 12, while the line of best fit gives about y = 11. The difference is 12 − 11 = 1.","cimg":[["bank/1adb39f0_A.png"],["bank/1adb39f0_B.png"],["bank/1adb39f0_C.png"],["bank/1adb39f0_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"555939d2","k":13,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/555939d2_stem.png"],"e":"The sample proportion is 8/300. Applying it to all customers: (8/300) × 30,000 = 800.","cimg":[["bank/555939d2_A.png"],["bank/555939d2_B.png"],["bank/555939d2_C.png"],["bank/555939d2_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"3f5398a6","k":8,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/3f5398a6_stem.png"],"e":"The ratio m : k = 1 : 5 means m = k/5. With k = 25 seconds, m = 25/5 = 5 miles.","cimg":[["bank/3f5398a6_A.png"],["bank/3f5398a6_B.png"],["bank/3f5398a6_C.png"],["bank/3f5398a6_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"b4912cc5","k":8,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/b4912cc5_stem.png"],"e":"Population = density × area. The density increased by 3.3 − 2.5 = 0.8 people per square kilometer, so the population increased by 0.8 × 100,250 = 80,200.","cimg":[["bank/b4912cc5_A.png"],["bank/b4912cc5_B.png"],["bank/b4912cc5_C.png"],["bank/b4912cc5_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"f890dc20","k":10,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/f890dc20_stem.png"],"e":"The 7 values are already in order: 2, 2, 2, 3, 4, 4, 11. The median is the middle (4th) value, which is 3.","cimg":[["bank/f890dc20_A.png"],["bank/f890dc20_B.png"],["bank/f890dc20_C.png"],["bank/f890dc20_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"d3b9c8d8","k":10,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/d3b9c8d8_stem.png"],"e":"The median is the line inside each box: group 1's median is 25 kg and group 2's median is 24 kg, so group 1's median is greater. Box plots don't show means, so A and B can't be determined.","cimg":[["bank/d3b9c8d8_A.png"],["bank/d3b9c8d8_B.png"],["bank/d3b9c8d8_C.png"],["bank/d3b9c8d8_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"65c49824","k":9,"diff":"Medium","type":"spr","img":["bank/65c49824_stem.png"],"e":"Students make up 100% − 15% − 45% − 25% = 15%, so 6 = 0.15 × total and the total is 40. Teachers = 0.45 × 40 = 18 and administrators = 0.25 × 40 = 10, so there are 18 − 10 = 8 more teachers.","ad":"8","a":8.0},{"id":"825b7490","k":8,"diff":"Easy","type":"spr","img":["bank/825b7490_stem.png"],"e":"Set 140/m = 4/28. Since 4 × 35 = 140, multiply 28 by 35 too: m = 980.","ad":"980","a":980.0},{"id":"86636d8f","k":8,"diff":"Easy","type":"spr","img":["bank/86636d8f_stem.png"],"e":"Pounds = total cost ÷ price per pound = 27 ÷ 3 = 9 pounds.","ad":"9","a":9.0},{"id":"608cf8e2","k":10,"diff":"Hard","type":"mc","img":["bank/608cf8e2_stem.png"],"e":"Every value in set A is at least 30, so adding 18 must lower the mean. The median might not change: if the 25th and 26th values are equal (both are in the 50–60 bin), the new median equals the old one, so I is not guaranteed.","cimg":[["bank/608cf8e2_A.png"],["bank/608cf8e2_B.png"],["bank/608cf8e2_C.png"],["bank/608cf8e2_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"fe4c1c9e","k":8,"diff":"Easy","type":"spr","img":["bank/fe4c1c9e_stem.png"],"e":"At 60 items per hour for 3 hours, the device makes 60 × 3 = 180 items.","ad":"180","a":180.0},{"id":"1ea09200","k":13,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/1ea09200_stem.png"],"e":"The sample was chosen at random from the fourth graders at this one school, so results can be applied only to all fourth-grade students at that school, not other grades or other schools.","cimg":[["bank/1ea09200_A.png"],["bank/1ea09200_B.png"],["bank/1ea09200_C.png"],["bank/1ea09200_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"82aaa0a1","k":11,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/82aaa0a1_stem.png"],"e":"The data open upward with a minimum near x ≈ 2.75 and y ≈ 5, and y is positive near x = 0. y = 2x² − 11x + 20 has its vertex at x = 11/4 = 2.75 with y ≈ 4.9 and y-intercept 20, which matches; the other options have negative minimums or a vertex near x = 1.25.","cimg":[["bank/82aaa0a1_A.png"],["bank/82aaa0a1_B.png"],["bank/82aaa0a1_C.png"],["bank/82aaa0a1_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"37930b2a","k":13,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/37930b2a_stem.png"],"e":"A sample estimate is not guaranteed to equal the population value, and a different random sample will usually give a somewhat different percentage. So neither statement must be true.","cimg":[["bank/37930b2a_A.png"],["bank/37930b2a_B.png"],["bank/37930b2a_C.png"],["bank/37930b2a_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"83272c51","k":11,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/83272c51_stem.png"],"e":"The graph drops fastest at the start: from about 200°F at 0 minutes to about 150°F at 10 minutes, a 50° drop. Later intervals show much smaller drops as the curve levels off.","cimg":[["bank/83272c51_A.png"],["bank/83272c51_B.png"],["bank/83272c51_C.png"],["bank/83272c51_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"3310c2ab","k":8,"diff":"Easy","type":"spr","img":["bank/3310c2ab_stem.png"],"e":"1 quart = 4 cups = 4 × 8 = 32 fluid ounces, so 76 quarts = 76 × 32 = 2,432 fluid ounces.","ad":"2432","a":2432.0},{"id":"4c774b00","k":10,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/4c774b00_stem.png"],"e":"The mode is 18 (most frequent). The median of 20 values is the average of the 10th and 11th, both 19. The mean is 400 ÷ 20 = 20, pulled up by the 30. So mode < median < mean.","cimg":[["bank/4c774b00_A.png"],["bank/4c774b00_B.png"],["bank/4c774b00_C.png"],["bank/4c774b00_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"1353b86e","k":12,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/1353b86e_q.png"],"e":"There are 10 blue marbles out of 40 total, so the probability is 10/40.","cimg":[["bank/1353b86e_A.png"],["bank/1353b86e_B.png"],["bank/1353b86e_C.png"],["bank/1353b86e_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"29fa7970","k":10,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/29fa7970_stem.png"],"e":"The bar above 0 kWh reaches a height of 6, so the battery received 0 kWh on 6 days.","cimg":[["bank/29fa7970_A.png"],["bank/29fa7970_B.png"],["bank/29fa7970_C.png"],["bank/29fa7970_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"d89c1513","k":12,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/d89c1513_q.png"],"e":"50 of the 135 customers did not purchase gasoline, so the probability is 50/135.","cimg":[["bank/d89c1513_A.png"],["bank/d89c1513_B.png"],["bank/d89c1513_C.png"],["bank/d89c1513_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"52f9a246","k":10,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/52f9a246_stem.png"],"e":"Count each value: 4 appears 4 times, 8 appears 3 times, and 13 appears 2 times. The table that pairs each number with its count is A.","cimg":[["bank/52f9a246_A.png"],["bank/52f9a246_B.png"],["bank/52f9a246_C.png"],["bank/52f9a246_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"000259aa","k":8,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/000259aa_stem.png"],"e":"Average rate = distance ÷ time = 2,100 miles ÷ 120 days = 17.5 miles per day.","cimg":[["bank/000259aa_A.png"],["bank/000259aa_B.png"],["bank/000259aa_C.png"],["bank/000259aa_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"a456cfd2","k":10,"diff":"Easy","type":"spr","img":["bank/a456cfd2_stem.png"],"e":"The largest data value with a nonzero frequency is 14, which appears 6 times. 13 has frequency 0, so it does not occur, but 14 does.","ad":"14","a":14.0},{"id":"e1ad3d41","k":12,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/e1ad3d41_q.png"],"e":"Use only the Chocolate row: 12 of the 16 chocolate kittens have deep blue eyes, so the fraction is 12/16.","cimg":[["bank/e1ad3d41_A.png"],["bank/e1ad3d41_B.png"],["bank/e1ad3d41_C.png"],["bank/e1ad3d41_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"3726e079","k":5,"diff":"Medium","type":"spr","img":["bank/3726e079_stem.png"],"e":"Rewrite 24x/(ny) as (24/n)(x/y). Since x/y = 4, this is 96/n = 4, so n = 24.","ad":"24","a":24.0},{"id":"8baf2118","k":11,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/8baf2118_stem.png"],"e":"The line slopes downward, so the slope is negative. It crosses the y-axis at about 13.5, which is positive. That gives y = 13.5 − 0.8x.","cimg":[["bank/8baf2118_A.png"],["bank/8baf2118_B.png"],["bank/8baf2118_C.png"],["bank/8baf2118_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"05195d8a","k":9,"diff":"Easy","type":"spr","img":["bank/05195d8a_stem.png"],"e":"0.80 × total = 88, so total = 88 ÷ 0.8 = 110 items.","ad":"110","a":110.0},{"id":"ac5b6558","k":11,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/ac5b6558_stem.png"],"e":"Find 8,500 on the horizontal axis and go up to the line; the line is at about 39°F there. Use the line's value, not a nearby data point.","cimg":[["bank/ac5b6558_A.png"],["bank/ac5b6558_B.png"],["bank/ac5b6558_C.png"],["bank/ac5b6558_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"46545dd6","k":12,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/46545dd6_q.png"],"e":"In 2010, 140 students completed internships and 65 were from Valley, so the fraction is 65/140.","cimg":[["bank/46545dd6_A.png"],["bank/46545dd6_B.png"],["bank/46545dd6_C.png"],["bank/46545dd6_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"58a71e06","k":9,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/58a71e06_stem.png"],"e":"234,000 ÷ 300,000 = 0.78, which is 78%.","cimg":[["bank/58a71e06_A.png"],["bank/58a71e06_B.png"],["bank/58a71e06_C.png"],["bank/58a71e06_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"4aaa9c42","k":9,"diff":"Hard","type":"mc","img":["bank/4aaa9c42_stem.png"],"e":"Let c = 1, so b = 0.83 and a = 22.41 × (0.83 + 1) = 41.01. The question asks what percent of b a is, so a ÷ b = 41.01 ÷ 0.83 ≈ 49.41, which is 4,941%.","cimg":[["bank/4aaa9c42_A.png"],["bank/4aaa9c42_B.png"],["bank/4aaa9c42_C.png"],["bank/4aaa9c42_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"16cea46c","k":12,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/16cea46c_stem.png"],"e":"10 of the 25 singers are baritones, so the probability is 10 ÷ 25 = 0.40.","cimg":[["bank/16cea46c_A.png"],["bank/16cea46c_B.png"],["bank/16cea46c_C.png"],["bank/16cea46c_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"fb866265","k":11,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/fb866265_stem.png"],"e":"The curve decreases, so b must be between 0 and 1. Check it: the curve goes from about 126 at x = 0 to about 67 at x = 3.5, and 0.83^3.5 ≈ 0.52 matches that drop.","cimg":[["bank/fb866265_A.png"],["bank/fb866265_B.png"],["bank/fb866265_C.png"],["bank/fb866265_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"bd90f87e","k":9,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/bd90f87e_stem.png"],"e":"Percent increase = (1.60 − 1.00) ÷ 1.00 × 100% = 60%.","cimg":[["bank/bd90f87e_A.png"],["bank/bd90f87e_B.png"],["bank/bd90f87e_C.png"],["bank/bd90f87e_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"15d87c0f","k":10,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/15d87c0f_stem.png"],"e":"The drama bar is at 40 and the chess bar is at 30, so drama has 40 − 30 = 10 more students.","cimg":[["bank/15d87c0f_A.png"],["bank/15d87c0f_B.png"],["bank/15d87c0f_C.png"],["bank/15d87c0f_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"312ba47c","k":8,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/312ba47c_stem.png"],"e":"Black : red = 8 : 1, so the number of red pens is 40 ÷ 8 = 5.","cimg":[["bank/312ba47c_A.png"],["bank/312ba47c_B.png"],["bank/312ba47c_C.png"],["bank/312ba47c_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"0ea56bb2","k":9,"diff":"Hard","type":"mc","img":["bank/0ea56bb2_stem.png"],"e":"The 2012–2013 increase is 280 ÷ 5,600 = 5%, so the expected 2013–2014 increase is half of that, 2.5%. Then 5,880 × 1.025 = 6,027.","cimg":[["bank/0ea56bb2_A.png"],["bank/0ea56bb2_B.png"],["bank/0ea56bb2_C.png"],["bank/0ea56bb2_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"90eed2e5","k":13,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/90eed2e5_stem.png"],"e":"In the sample, 6 of 20 = 30% support the bill. Apply that to all 50 members: 0.30 × 50 = 15.","cimg":[["bank/90eed2e5_A.png"],["bank/90eed2e5_B.png"],["bank/90eed2e5_C.png"],["bank/90eed2e5_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"8e528129","k":8,"diff":"Medium","type":"spr","img":["bank/8e528129_stem.png"],"e":"One cubic inch weighs 0.555 ounce, and each ounce costs $8.00, so one cubic inch costs 0.555 × 8 = $4.44.","ad":"4.44","a":4.44},{"id":"15617f62","k":8,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/15617f62_stem.png"],"e":"Area = population ÷ density = 92,800 ÷ 290 = 320 square miles.","cimg":[["bank/15617f62_A.png"],["bank/15617f62_B.png"],["bank/15617f62_C.png"],["bank/15617f62_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"8736334b","k":10,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/8736334b_stem.png"],"e":"Both sets have 5 numbers, so equal means require equal sums. Set A sums to 370, and set B's known values sum to 284, so x = 370 − 284 = 86.","cimg":[["bank/8736334b_A.png"],["bank/8736334b_B.png"],["bank/8736334b_C.png"],["bank/8736334b_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"0231050d","k":9,"diff":"Easy","type":"spr","img":["bank/0231050d_stem.png"],"e":"Snowfall fell from 40 to 10 inches, a drop of 30. Percent decrease = 30 ÷ 40 × 100% = 75%, so p = 75.","ad":"75","a":75.0},{"id":"be35c117","k":8,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/be35c117_stem.png"],"e":"Revolutions per minute = 900 ÷ 50 = 18.","cimg":[["bank/be35c117_A.png"],["bank/be35c117_B.png"],["bank/be35c117_C.png"],["bank/be35c117_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"4a2264b3","k":10,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/4a2264b3_stem.png"],"e":"The lowest point on the graph is at model year 2014, at about 4%.","cimg":[["bank/4a2264b3_A.png"],["bank/4a2264b3_B.png"],["bank/4a2264b3_C.png"],["bank/4a2264b3_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"e3d49511","k":8,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/e3d49511_stem.png"],"e":"Density = number ÷ area = 2,358 ÷ 131 = 18 raccoons per square mile.","cimg":[["bank/e3d49511_A.png"],["bank/e3d49511_B.png"],["bank/e3d49511_C.png"],["bank/e3d49511_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"b680e76d","k":10,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/b680e76d_stem.png"],"e":"All four cells add to 1,000, so the missing value is 1,000 − 312 − 220 − 216 = 252.","cimg":[["bank/b680e76d_A.png"],["bank/b680e76d_B.png"],["bank/b680e76d_C.png"],["bank/b680e76d_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"53d97af5","k":13,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/53d97af5_stem.png"],"e":"The sample contained only largemouth bass, so it supports a conclusion only about largemouth bass: about 30% of them weigh more than 2 pounds. It says nothing about other kinds of fish.","cimg":[["bank/53d97af5_A.png"],["bank/53d97af5_B.png"],["bank/53d97af5_C.png"],["bank/53d97af5_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"15ce8207","k":11,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/15ce8207_stem.png"],"e":"The points rise slowly and then very steeply, which is exponential growth. Only the curve in D passes close to the points; B's curve sits well above most of them, and the lines in A and C miss the curved pattern.","cimg":[["bank/15ce8207_A.png"],["bank/15ce8207_B.png"],["bank/15ce8207_C.png"],["bank/15ce8207_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"d4413871","k":12,"diff":"Medium","type":"spr","img":["bank/d4413871_stem.png"],"e":"Rhesus-negative people total 7 + 2 + 1 + x = 10 + x, and 2 of them are type B. Set 2/(10 + x) = 1/9, so 10 + x = 18 and x = 8.","ad":"8","a":8.0},{"id":"0301c5dc","k":12,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/0301c5dc_q.png"],"e":"Parks with camping but no bicycle paths: 5. Total parks: 20 + 5 + 8 + 4 = 37. Probability = 5/37.","cimg":[["bank/0301c5dc_A.png"],["bank/0301c5dc_B.png"],["bank/0301c5dc_C.png"],["bank/0301c5dc_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"0ae37ff3","k":12,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/0ae37ff3_stem.png"],"e":"There are 7 + 4 + 33 + 33 = 77 cubes. Cubes that are neither blue nor yellow are red or white: 7 + 4 = 11. The probability is 11/77 = 1/7.","cimg":[["bank/0ae37ff3_A.png"],["bank/0ae37ff3_B.png"],["bank/0ae37ff3_C.png"],["bank/0ae37ff3_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"c88e0663","k":10,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/c88e0663_stem.png"],"e":"The average is the total ÷ the count = 90 ÷ 10 = 9 boxes. The median, the greatest, and the least all need the individual students' sales, which are not given.","cimg":[["bank/c88e0663_A.png"],["bank/c88e0663_B.png"],["bank/c88e0663_C.png"],["bank/c88e0663_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"9bb4107c","k":7,"diff":"Medium","type":"spr","img":["bank/9bb4107c_stem.png"],"e":"Read y = 6 at x = 2 and y = 8 at x = 6 from the graph. Average rate of change = (8 − 6) ÷ (6 − 2) = 2/4 = 0.5.","ad":"1/2","tol":0.0011,"a":0.5},{"id":"3f2ee20a","k":10,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/3f2ee20a_stem.png"],"e":"Standard deviation measures spread. Group B's standard deviation (19.1) is larger than Group A's (12.5), so Group B's heights are more spread out. The table gives no information about medians or maximums.","cimg":[["bank/3f2ee20a_A.png"],["bank/3f2ee20a_B.png"],["bank/3f2ee20a_C.png"],["bank/3f2ee20a_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"993000da","k":9,"diff":"Hard","type":"mc","img":["bank/993000da_stem.png"],"e":"a = 2.3b and a = 0.6c, so c = 2.3b ÷ 0.6 ≈ 3.83b. That makes c about 383% of b, so p ≈ 383.","cimg":[["bank/993000da_A.png"],["bank/993000da_B.png"],["bank/993000da_C.png"],["bank/993000da_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"fe6a49d6","k":10,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/fe6a49d6_stem.png"],"e":"The bar above 78 walnuts reaches 7, so 7 containers hold exactly 78 walnuts.","cimg":[["bank/fe6a49d6_A.png"],["bank/fe6a49d6_B.png"],["bank/fe6a49d6_C.png"],["bank/fe6a49d6_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"632cf8f9","k":7,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/632cf8f9_stem.png"],"e":"The graph rises from left to right and curves upward more and more steeply, flattening toward 0 on the left. That shape is an increasing exponential.","cimg":[["bank/632cf8f9_A.png"],["bank/632cf8f9_B.png"],["bank/632cf8f9_C.png"],["bank/632cf8f9_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"d0efc1dd","k":10,"diff":"Hard","type":"mc","img":["bank/d0efc1dd_stem.png"],"e":"The mean is (64 + x)/5. If x ≤ 15 the median is 15, giving x = 11. If 15 ≤ x ≤ 17 the median is x, giving x = 16. If x ≥ 17 the median is 17, giving x = 21. So 6 is not possible: then the median is 15 but the mean is 14.","cimg":[["bank/d0efc1dd_A.png"],["bank/d0efc1dd_B.png"],["bank/d0efc1dd_C.png"],["bank/d0efc1dd_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"80f1f3a9","k":10,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/80f1f3a9_stem.png"],"e":"The green bar reaches 70 on the frequency axis; the other bars are near 27, 33, and 43.","cimg":[["bank/80f1f3a9_A.png"],["bank/80f1f3a9_B.png"],["bank/80f1f3a9_C.png"],["bank/80f1f3a9_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"e9fb7774","k":9,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/e9fb7774_stem.png"],"e":"75 ÷ 300 = 0.25, which is 25%.","cimg":[["bank/e9fb7774_A.png"],["bank/e9fb7774_B.png"],["bank/e9fb7774_C.png"],["bank/e9fb7774_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"190be2fc","k":10,"diff":"Hard","type":"spr","img":["bank/190be2fc_stem.png"],"e":"The 9 integers sum to 9 × 42 = 378. The 10th integer x is less than 60, so the total 378 + x must be a multiple of 10 that is greater than 420 and less than 438. The only option is 430, so x = 52, which is the largest value.","ad":"52","a":52.0},{"id":"3f236a64","k":8,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/3f236a64_stem.png"],"e":"y/x = 4 for every pair, so k = 4 × 40 = 160.","cimg":[["bank/3f236a64_A.png"],["bank/3f236a64_B.png"],["bank/3f236a64_C.png"],["bank/3f236a64_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"8705ecba","k":9,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/8705ecba_stem.png"],"e":"Tax = 5% of $20 = $1.00, so the total is $20 + $1 = $21.00.","cimg":[["bank/8705ecba_A.png"],["bank/8705ecba_B.png"],["bank/8705ecba_C.png"],["bank/8705ecba_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"2e74e403","k":11,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/2e74e403_stem.png"],"e":"The line goes from about (0, 8) to about (10, 1), so the slope ≈ (1 − 8) ÷ 10 = −0.7. It is negative because the line falls.","cimg":[["bank/2e74e403_A.png"],["bank/2e74e403_B.png"],["bank/2e74e403_C.png"],["bank/2e74e403_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"f8f79e11","k":13,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/f8f79e11_stem.png"],"e":"A margin of error describes uncertainty in the estimate of the population mean, not individual visitors. So it is plausible that the true mean is between 4.5 − 0.5 = 4 and 4.5 + 0.5 = 5 miles.","cimg":[["bank/f8f79e11_A.png"],["bank/f8f79e11_B.png"],["bank/f8f79e11_C.png"],["bank/f8f79e11_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"da9ffcf6","k":8,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/da9ffcf6_stem.png"],"e":"XY : ZV = 6 : 1, so ZV = 102 ÷ 6 = 17 inches.","cimg":[["bank/da9ffcf6_A.png"],["bank/da9ffcf6_B.png"],["bank/da9ffcf6_C.png"],["bank/da9ffcf6_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"db88a933","k":10,"diff":"Hard","type":"mc","img":["bank/db88a933_stem.png"],"e":"Let b = a + 1 and c = a + 2. Mean of Q = (110a + 30b)/140 = a + 3/14. Mean of R = (3b + 11c)/14 = a + 25/14. R's mean is larger by 22/14 = 2(11)/14.","cimg":[["bank/db88a933_A.png"],["bank/db88a933_B.png"],["bank/db88a933_C.png"],["bank/db88a933_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"2e8027b0","k":11,"diff":"Hard","type":"mc","img":["bank/2e8027b0_stem.png"],"e":"Set E's line has a y-intercept of about 12 and a slope of about (42.7 − 12)/20 ≈ 1.5. Multiplying every y by 3.9 multiplies both: 12 × 3.9 = 46.8 and 1.5 × 3.9 ≈ 5.9, so y = 46.8 + 5.9x.","cimg":[["bank/2e8027b0_A.png"],["bank/2e8027b0_B.png"],["bank/2e8027b0_C.png"],["bank/2e8027b0_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"c178d4da","k":10,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/c178d4da_stem.png"],"e":"Both sets use the same values, but set A has more values at the high end (42 and 46) and set B has more at the low end (30 and 34). So A's mean is greater.","cimg":[["bank/c178d4da_A.png"],["bank/c178d4da_B.png"],["bank/c178d4da_C.png"],["bank/c178d4da_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"2c76bcce","k":13,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/2c76bcce_stem.png"],"e":"The margin of error applies to the estimate of the population mean, so it is plausible that the true mean is between 27.8 − 0.02 = 27.78 and 27.8 + 0.02 = 27.82 oz. It does not describe individual handbag weights.","cimg":[["bank/2c76bcce_A.png"],["bank/2c76bcce_B.png"],["bank/2c76bcce_C.png"],["bank/2c76bcce_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"9fa781f8","k":8,"diff":"Easy","type":"spr","img":["bank/9fa781f8_stem.png"],"e":"x/y = 9/5. Since 162 = 9 × 18, y = 5 × 18 = 90.","ad":"90","a":90.0},{"id":"9a144a01","k":7,"diff":"Hard","type":"mc","img":["bank/9a144a01_stem.png"],"e":"Test values: at x = 1, 2¹ = 2 < 4. At x = 3, 2³ = 8 = 2(3) + 2. At x = 4, 16 > 10. So with c = 3, 2^x < 2x + 2 for 0 < x < 3 and 2^x > 2x + 2 for x > 3.","cimg":[["bank/9a144a01_A.png"],["bank/9a144a01_B.png"],["bank/9a144a01_C.png"],["bank/9a144a01_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"022e9894","k":9,"diff":"Medium","type":"spr","img":["bank/022e9894_stem.png"],"e":"Second session: 0.72 × 1,250 = 900 people. Third session: 0.36 × 900 = 324 people.","ad":"324","a":324.0},{"id":"457d2f2c","k":10,"diff":"Hard","type":"mc","img":["bank/457d2f2c_stem.png"],"e":"There are 13 numbers above the median and 13 below. Adding 7 to the 13 high values and subtracting 7 from the 13 low values leaves the sum, mean, and median unchanged. The values move farther from the center, so the standard deviation increases.","cimg":[["bank/457d2f2c_A.png"],["bank/457d2f2c_B.png"],["bank/457d2f2c_C.png"],["bank/457d2f2c_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"e24765e6","k":11,"diff":"Easy","type":"spr","img":["bank/e24765e6_stem.png"],"e":"Read y = 14 at x = 5 and y = 24 at x = 7. Average rate of change = (24 − 14) ÷ (7 − 5) = 5 °C per minute.","ad":"5","a":5.0},{"id":"47624288","k":12,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/47624288_stem.png"],"e":"20 of the 80 students voted for lion, so the probability is 20/80 = 1/4.","cimg":[["bank/47624288_A.png"],["bank/47624288_B.png"],["bank/47624288_C.png"],["bank/47624288_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"6310adbc","k":8,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/6310adbc_stem.png"],"e":"t : u = 1 : 2, so u is twice t: u = 2 × 10 = 20.","cimg":[["bank/6310adbc_A.png"],["bank/6310adbc_B.png"],["bank/6310adbc_C.png"],["bank/6310adbc_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"e438ec3f","k":12,"diff":"Hard","type":"mc","img":["bank/e438ec3f_stem.png"],"e":"Trees 20 feet or taller: birch 6 × 8 = 48 and maple 5 × 9 = 45, so 93 in all. Given the tree is tall, P(maple) = 45/93 = 15/31.","cimg":[["bank/e438ec3f_A.png"],["bank/e438ec3f_B.png"],["bank/e438ec3f_C.png"],["bank/e438ec3f_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"63573fea","k":9,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/63573fea_stem.png"],"e":"Each month 0.15 × 1,300,000 = 195,000 units are returned. Over 6 months (the first month plus 5 more), that is 6 × 195,000 = 1,170,000.","cimg":[["bank/63573fea_A.png"],["bank/63573fea_B.png"],["bank/63573fea_C.png"],["bank/63573fea_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"191d167b","k":9,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/191d167b_stem.png"],"e":"147% of 200 = 1.47 × 200 = 294 students.","cimg":[["bank/191d167b_A.png"],["bank/191d167b_B.png"],["bank/191d167b_C.png"],["bank/191d167b_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"03a16790","k":11,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/03a16790_stem.png"],"e":"The line goes from about (0, 12.8) to about (14, 1.6), so the slope ≈ (1.6 − 12.8) ÷ 14 ≈ −0.8. It is negative because the line falls.","cimg":[["bank/03a16790_A.png"],["bank/03a16790_B.png"],["bank/03a16790_C.png"],["bank/03a16790_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"60caadfd","k":12,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/60caadfd_stem.png"],"e":"10 of the 70 rocks are igneous, so the probability is 10/70. Divide by the total of all rocks, not by another category.","cimg":[["bank/60caadfd_A.png"],["bank/60caadfd_B.png"],["bank/60caadfd_C.png"],["bank/60caadfd_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"c3d65f93","k":10,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/c3d65f93_stem.png"],"e":"The original values range from 136 to 149, so the original mean is above 121. Adding a value below the mean lowers it, so the original mean is greater.","cimg":[["bank/c3d65f93_A.png"],["bank/c3d65f93_B.png"],["bank/c3d65f93_C.png"],["bank/c3d65f93_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"b4f5a7ca","k":13,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/b4f5a7ca_stem.png"],"e":"The sample was drawn at random from history professors at the California State Universities, so the results generalize only to that group, not to other professors or other schools.","cimg":[["bank/b4f5a7ca_A.png"],["bank/b4f5a7ca_B.png"],["bank/b4f5a7ca_C.png"],["bank/b4f5a7ca_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"93724cc6","k":9,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/93724cc6_stem.png"],"e":"0.21 × n = 21, so n = 21 ÷ 0.21 = 100.","cimg":[["bank/93724cc6_A.png"],["bank/93724cc6_B.png"],["bank/93724cc6_C.png"],["bank/93724cc6_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"d6af3572","k":11,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/d6af3572_stem.png"],"e":"The slope 0.096 is the predicted change in y (dollars) for each 1-unit increase in x, and x is measured in years. So the model predicts an average increase of $0.096 each year. The −0.488 is the y-intercept, not a rate.","cimg":[["bank/d6af3572_A.png"],["bank/d6af3572_B.png"],["bank/d6af3572_C.png"],["bank/d6af3572_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"2d16d62c","k":8,"diff":"Easy","type":"spr","img":["bank/2d16d62c_stem.png"],"e":"Each fathom is 6 feet, so 58 fathoms = 58 × 6 = 348 feet.","ad":"348","a":348.0},{"id":"69f6717f","k":15,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/69f6717f_stem.png"],"e":"Volume = 0.90³ = 0.729 cubic meters. Mass = density × volume = 807 × 0.729 ≈ 588.3, which rounds to 588 kg.","cimg":[["bank/69f6717f_A.png"],["bank/69f6717f_B.png"],["bank/69f6717f_C.png"],["bank/69f6717f_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"35bec412","k":10,"diff":"Easy","type":"spr","img":["bank/35bec412_stem.png"],"e":"The 9 values are already in order, so the median is the 5th value, 79.","ad":"79","a":79.0},{"id":"74dee52b","k":10,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/74dee52b_stem.png"],"e":"Of the choices, 2002 has the lowest point on the graph, at about 220 graduates. 2004, 2005, and 2007 are all higher.","cimg":[["bank/74dee52b_A.png"],["bank/74dee52b_B.png"],["bank/74dee52b_C.png"],["bank/74dee52b_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"c3d78831","k":8,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/c3d78831_stem.png"],"e":"There are 26 athletes for every coach, so x coaches means 26x athletes.","cimg":[["bank/c3d78831_A.png"],["bank/c3d78831_B.png"],["bank/c3d78831_C.png"],["bank/c3d78831_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"b5bc47d5","k":8,"diff":"Hard","type":"mc","img":["bank/b5bc47d5_stem.png"],"e":"Each model inch stands for 17/3 actual feet, so x actual feet corresponds to x ÷ (17/3) = 3x/17 model inches. No feet-to-inches conversion is needed because the scale already pairs model inches with actual feet.","cimg":[["bank/b5bc47d5_A.png"],["bank/b5bc47d5_B.png"],["bank/b5bc47d5_C.png"],["bank/b5bc47d5_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"fea831fc","k":8,"diff":"Medium","type":"spr","img":["bank/fea831fc_stem.png"],"e":"26 minutes = 26/60 hour. Speed = 11 ÷ (26/60) = 660/26 ≈ 25.38, which is about 25.4 miles per hour.","ad":"25.4","a":25.4},{"id":"aeeaec96","k":8,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/aeeaec96_stem.png"],"e":"Yards = inches ÷ 36 = 612 ÷ 36 = 17.","cimg":[["bank/aeeaec96_A.png"],["bank/aeeaec96_B.png"],["bank/aeeaec96_C.png"],["bank/aeeaec96_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"6c9444cd","k":10,"diff":"Medium","type":"spr","img":["bank/6c9444cd_stem.png"],"e":"Class A ranges from 0 to 5, so its range is 5. Class B ranges from 1 to 10, so its range is 9. The difference is 9 − 5 = 4.","ad":"4","a":4.0},{"id":"9d88a3e3","k":10,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/9d88a3e3_stem.png"],"e":"Speed increased from 0 to 5 and from 20 to 25 minutes (10 minutes total) and decreased from 10 to 20 and from 25 to 30 minutes (15 minutes total). So B is false. A, C, and D all match the graph.","cimg":[["bank/9d88a3e3_A.png"],["bank/9d88a3e3_B.png"],["bank/9d88a3e3_C.png"],["bank/9d88a3e3_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"e03f3477","k":13,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/e03f3477_stem.png"],"e":"A margin of error gives a plausible range for the population percentage: 32% − 3.41% = 28.59% to 32% + 3.41% = 35.41%.","cimg":[["bank/e03f3477_A.png"],["bank/e03f3477_B.png"],["bank/e03f3477_C.png"],["bank/e03f3477_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"d693f563","k":9,"diff":"Easy","type":"spr","img":["bank/d693f563_stem.png"],"e":"A 60% increase means multiplying by 1.60: 35 × 1.6 = 56 plants.","ad":"56","a":56.0},{"id":"f46139df","k":11,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/f46139df_stem.png"],"e":"The line runs from about (23.5, 10) to about (34.75, 0), so its slope ≈ −0.89, and it passes through (28, 6). At x = 25.5, y ≈ 6 + 2.5 × 0.89 ≈ 8.2.","cimg":[["bank/f46139df_A.png"],["bank/f46139df_B.png"],["bank/f46139df_C.png"],["bank/f46139df_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"07f2829b","k":10,"diff":"Medium","type":"spr","img":["bank/07f2829b_stem.png"],"e":"With 9 values, the median is the 5th value in order. Sorted, the 2012 median is 46.4 (Italy) and the 2013 median is 47.7 (Italy). The difference is 47.7 − 46.4 = 1.3 million.","ad":"1.3","a":1.3},{"id":"e5b5fbdd","k":12,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/e5b5fbdd_q.png"],"e":"4 of the 8 planets are rocky: 4/8 = 1/2.","cimg":[["bank/e5b5fbdd_A.png"],["bank/e5b5fbdd_B.png"],["bank/e5b5fbdd_C.png"],["bank/e5b5fbdd_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"d65b9a87","k":10,"diff":"Hard","type":"mc","img":["bank/d65b9a87_stem.png"],"e":"Each set has 17 values, and the 9th value is 13 in both, so the medians are equal. Both sets are symmetric about 13, but B has more values at 10 and 16 and fewer at 13, so it is more spread out and its standard deviation is larger. Only I is true.","cimg":[["bank/d65b9a87_A.png"],["bank/d65b9a87_B.png"],["bank/d65b9a87_C.png"],["bank/d65b9a87_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"7ac5d686","k":1,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/7ac5d686_stem.png"],"e":"The number of shirts left drops by the same amount each unit of time, so it decreases linearly. That is a linear model with a negative slope.","cimg":[["bank/7ac5d686_A.png"],["bank/7ac5d686_B.png"],["bank/7ac5d686_C.png"],["bank/7ac5d686_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"1fc4f47b","k":12,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/1fc4f47b_stem.png"],"e":"P(C) = 1 − 0.48 − 0.24 = 0.28, so theater C has 0.28 × 350 = 98 customers.","cimg":[["bank/1fc4f47b_A.png"],["bank/1fc4f47b_B.png"],["bank/1fc4f47b_C.png"],["bank/1fc4f47b_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"e7133228","k":8,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/e7133228_stem.png"],"e":"Convert both units: 1 second² = (1/60 minute)², so multiply by 3,600, and divide by 1,609 to get miles. 7.3 × 3,600 ÷ 1,609 ≈ 16.3 miles per minute squared.","cimg":[["bank/e7133228_A.png"],["bank/e7133228_B.png"],["bank/e7133228_C.png"],["bank/e7133228_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"2905ded0","k":12,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/2905ded0_stem.png"],"e":"107 of the 135 members are at least 40 years old, so the probability is 107/135.","cimg":[["bank/2905ded0_A.png"],["bank/2905ded0_B.png"],["bank/2905ded0_C.png"],["bank/2905ded0_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"bb7c8186","k":9,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/bb7c8186_stem.png"],"e":"23% of 100 = 0.23 × 100 = 23.","cimg":[["bank/bb7c8186_A.png"],["bank/bb7c8186_B.png"],["bank/bb7c8186_C.png"],["bank/bb7c8186_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"d230e963","k":11,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/d230e963_stem.png"],"e":"The line rises, so the slope is positive. It crosses the y-axis at about 2.8, which is positive. That gives y = 2.8 + 1.7x.","cimg":[["bank/d230e963_A.png"],["bank/d230e963_B.png"],["bank/d230e963_C.png"],["bank/d230e963_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"181cc4d6","k":8,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/181cc4d6_q.png"],"e":"Same ratio means 15/w = 20/x, so x = 20w/15 = (4/3)w.","cimg":[["bank/181cc4d6_A.png"],["bank/181cc4d6_B.png"],["bank/181cc4d6_C.png"],["bank/181cc4d6_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"241f1db7","k":10,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/241f1db7_stem.png"],"e":"With 71 values the median is the 36th value; cumulative counts 12, 20, 25, 32, 41 put it at 17. With 72 values the median is the average of the 36th and 37th values, both 17, so the median is unchanged, while adding 39 (far above the mean) raises the mean.","cimg":[["bank/241f1db7_A.png"],["bank/241f1db7_B.png"],["bank/241f1db7_C.png"],["bank/241f1db7_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"578e26ae","k":10,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/578e26ae_stem.png"],"e":"Adding 46 to every value shifts the whole data set up by 46, so the median increases by 46. The range is max − min, and both shift by 46, so the range stays the same.","cimg":[["bank/578e26ae_A.png"],["bank/578e26ae_B.png"],["bank/578e26ae_C.png"],["bank/578e26ae_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"e9841407","k":8,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/e9841407_stem.png"],"e":"The ratio of red to blue is 7 to 28; dividing both by 7 gives 1 to 4.","cimg":[["bank/e9841407_A.png"],["bank/e9841407_B.png"],["bank/e9841407_C.png"],["bank/e9841407_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"7fd284ac","k":11,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/7fd284ac_stem.png"],"e":"The highest point is about 91.5% at an income near 3,500 million dollars. The line of best fit there predicts about 85%, so the difference is about 6.5%, closest to 7%.","cimg":[["bank/7fd284ac_A.png"],["bank/7fd284ac_B.png"],["bank/7fd284ac_C.png"],["bank/7fd284ac_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"0d125b35","k":8,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/0d125b35_stem.png"],"e":"Since p is proportional to t, p/t = 5,130/6,840 = 0.75. Then p = 0.75 × 5,472 = 4,104.","cimg":[["bank/0d125b35_A.png"],["bank/0d125b35_B.png"],["bank/0d125b35_C.png"],["bank/0d125b35_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"1fbd3b67","k":9,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/1fbd3b67_stem.png"],"e":"b is 80% less than 24, so b = 0.20 × 24 = 4.8. a is 190% greater than b, so a = 2.90 × 4.8 = 13.92.","cimg":[["bank/1fbd3b67_A.png"],["bank/1fbd3b67_B.png"],["bank/1fbd3b67_C.png"],["bank/1fbd3b67_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"1b403590","k":8,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/1b403590_stem.png"],"e":"Density = mass ÷ volume = 168 ÷ 24 = 7 grams per cubic centimeter.","cimg":[["bank/1b403590_A.png"],["bank/1b403590_B.png"],["bank/1b403590_C.png"],["bank/1b403590_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"c81499e1","k":8,"diff":"Easy","type":"spr","img":["bank/c81499e1_stem.png"],"e":"Multiply by the conversion factor: 39 kilograms × 1,000 grams per kilogram = 39,000 grams.","ad":"39000","a":39000.0},{"id":"a2162ea1","k":13,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/a2162ea1_stem.png"],"e":"The margin of error gives a range of plausible values: 23.1 − 0.19 = 22.91 to 23.1 + 0.19 = 23.29 pounds.","cimg":[["bank/a2162ea1_A.png"],["bank/a2162ea1_B.png"],["bank/a2162ea1_C.png"],["bank/a2162ea1_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"ecbdbe84","k":10,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/ecbdbe84_stem.png"],"e":"With 17 restaurants the median is the 9th value. Cumulative counts are 2, 6, 8, 15, so the 9th value lies in the 20 to 25 interval; only 21 fits.","cimg":[["bank/ecbdbe84_A.png"],["bank/ecbdbe84_B.png"],["bank/ecbdbe84_C.png"],["bank/ecbdbe84_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"f8a322d9","k":10,"diff":"Hard","type":"mc","img":["bank/f8a322d9_stem.png"],"e":"Data set B has the same frequencies as A but every bar is shifted 10 lower. Make A as small as possible (each value at its bin's lower end) and B as large as possible (each value at its bin's upper end, which is 1 below A's lower end), so each of the 23 pairs differs by at least 1 and the means differ by at least 23 ÷ 23 = 1.","cimg":[["bank/f8a322d9_A.png"],["bank/f8a322d9_B.png"],["bank/f8a322d9_C.png"],["bank/f8a322d9_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"e7d9649f","k":13,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/e7d9649f_stem.png"],"e":"The sample proportion is 7/50 = 0.14. Applying it to the town gives 0.14 × 14,878 ≈ 2,083, which is about 2,100.","cimg":[["bank/e7d9649f_A.png"],["bank/e7d9649f_B.png"],["bank/e7d9649f_C.png"],["bank/e7d9649f_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"2df8f293","k":12,"diff":"Easy","type":"spr","img":["bank/2df8f293_stem.png"],"e":"Each of the 14 vertices is equally likely and exactly one has the letter D, so the probability is 1/14.","ad":"1/14","tol":0.0011,"a":0.07142857142857142},{"id":"7cab9fe1","k":9,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/7cab9fe1_stem.png"],"e":"Increasing by 43% means keeping 100% of w and adding 43% more: w + 0.43w = 1.43w.","cimg":[["bank/7cab9fe1_A.png"],["bank/7cab9fe1_B.png"],["bank/7cab9fe1_C.png"],["bank/7cab9fe1_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"ec7b0eb8","k":12,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/ec7b0eb8_q.png"],"e":"415 of the 799 teens talk on a cell phone daily, so the probability is 415/799.","cimg":[["bank/ec7b0eb8_A.png"],["bank/ec7b0eb8_B.png"],["bank/ec7b0eb8_C.png"],["bank/ec7b0eb8_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"0700a2d5","k":8,"diff":"Easy","type":"spr","img":["bank/0700a2d5_stem.png"],"e":"Each rod is 5.5 yards, so 77 rods = 77 × 5.5 = 423.5 yards.","ad":"423.5","a":423.5},{"id":"3638f413","k":7,"diff":"Medium","type":"spr","img":["bank/3638f413_stem.png"],"e":"From January 1, 2001 to January 1, 2005 the amount doubled 4 times, so 2⁴x = 16x = 480 and x = 30.","ad":"30","a":30.0},{"id":"e17babed","k":11,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/e17babed_stem.png"],"e":"A point's actual y-value is greater than predicted when the point lies above the line. Counting the points above the line (near x = 0.3, 1, 2, 4.2, 6.1 and 9.2) gives 6.","cimg":[["bank/e17babed_A.png"],["bank/e17babed_B.png"],["bank/e17babed_C.png"],["bank/e17babed_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"12dae628","k":10,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/12dae628_stem.png"],"e":"Mean = (2 + 9 + 14 + 23 + 32) ÷ 5 = 80 ÷ 5 = 16.","cimg":[["bank/12dae628_A.png"],["bank/12dae628_B.png"],["bank/12dae628_C.png"],["bank/12dae628_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"1142af44","k":10,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/1142af44_stem.png"],"e":"The frequencies a, 2a, 3a, 2a, a are symmetric around the value 3, so both the mean and the median equal 3. The difference is 0.","cimg":[["bank/1142af44_A.png"],["bank/1142af44_B.png"],["bank/1142af44_C.png"],["bank/1142af44_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"79201024","k":12,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/79201024_stem.png"],"e":"Probability = favorable outcomes ÷ total outcomes = 11 saxophone players ÷ 45 members = 11/45.","cimg":[["bank/79201024_A.png"],["bank/79201024_B.png"],["bank/79201024_C.png"],["bank/79201024_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"445dd032","k":1,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/445dd032_stem.png"],"e":"Earnings are 13.50 times the number of hours. Replacing z with 3z gives 13.50(3z), which equals 3(13.50z).","cimg":[["bank/445dd032_A.png"],["bank/445dd032_B.png"],["bank/445dd032_C.png"],["bank/445dd032_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"121dc44f","k":9,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/121dc44f_stem.png"],"e":"A 7% increase means the new population is 100% + 7% = 107% of the old one, so k = 1.07.","cimg":[["bank/121dc44f_A.png"],["bank/121dc44f_B.png"],["bank/121dc44f_C.png"],["bank/121dc44f_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"1e8ccffd","k":10,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/1e8ccffd_stem.png"],"e":"The total of all 8 scores is 8 × 14.5 = 116 and the total of the remaining 7 is 7 × 12 = 84. The removed highest score is 116 − 84 = 32.","cimg":[["bank/1e8ccffd_A.png"],["bank/1e8ccffd_B.png"],["bank/1e8ccffd_C.png"],["bank/1e8ccffd_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"a29e89fc","k":10,"diff":"Easy","type":"spr","img":["bank/a29e89fc_stem.png"],"e":"The sum is 4,010 + 4,010 + 3,030 + 4,050 + 3,050 = 18,150, and 18,150 ÷ 5 = 3,630 grams.","ad":"3630","a":3630.0},{"id":"9bedc4a0","k":13,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/9bedc4a0_stem.png"],"e":"A margin of error gives a plausible range around the estimate: 12% − 3.62% = 8.38% to 12% + 3.62% = 15.62%.","cimg":[["bank/9bedc4a0_A.png"],["bank/9bedc4a0_B.png"],["bank/9bedc4a0_C.png"],["bank/9bedc4a0_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"1e1027a7","k":11,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/1e1027a7_stem.png"],"e":"The line rises from about 480 at t = 12 to about 920 at t = 25, a slope of about 33, which rules out A and B. At t = 12, d = 33(12) + 84 = 480 matches the line, while 33(12) + 300 = 696 does not.","cimg":[["bank/1e1027a7_A.png"],["bank/1e1027a7_B.png"],["bank/1e1027a7_C.png"],["bank/1e1027a7_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"fe1ec415","k":8,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/fe1ec415_stem.png"],"e":"The rate is 12 ÷ 3 = 4 pounds per minute, so 96 pounds takes 96 ÷ 4 = 24 minutes.","cimg":[["bank/fe1ec415_A.png"],["bank/fe1ec415_B.png"],["bank/fe1ec415_C.png"],["bank/fe1ec415_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"f85bbf7a","k":13,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/f85bbf7a_stem.png"],"e":"The interval 24% to 40% is centered at the sample value 32%, and 32 − 24 = 8, so the margin of error is 8%.","cimg":[["bank/f85bbf7a_A.png"],["bank/f85bbf7a_B.png"],["bank/f85bbf7a_C.png"],["bank/f85bbf7a_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"ba62b0b0","k":8,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/ba62b0b0_stem.png"],"e":"Multiply by the conversion factor: 28 kilograms × 1,000 grams per kilogram = 28,000 grams.","cimg":[["bank/ba62b0b0_A.png"],["bank/ba62b0b0_B.png"],["bank/ba62b0b0_C.png"],["bank/ba62b0b0_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"939c46d1","k":8,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/939c46d1_stem.png"],"e":"One gallon is 128 fluid ounces and the glass holds 16 fluid ounces, so it can be filled 128 ÷ 16 = 8 times. The volume formula is not needed.","cimg":[["bank/939c46d1_A.png"],["bank/939c46d1_B.png"],["bank/939c46d1_C.png"],["bank/939c46d1_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"29c177e6","k":9,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/29c177e6_stem.png"],"e":"10% of 470 = 0.10 × 470 = 47.","cimg":[["bank/29c177e6_A.png"],["bank/29c177e6_B.png"],["bank/29c177e6_C.png"],["bank/29c177e6_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"13f67ddc","k":10,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/13f67ddc_stem.png"],"e":"Read across from 30 on the vertical axis: the only point at 30% is Thursday.","cimg":[["bank/13f67ddc_A.png"],["bank/13f67ddc_B.png"],["bank/13f67ddc_C.png"],["bank/13f67ddc_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"ea95087d","k":10,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/ea95087d_stem.png"],"e":"Subtract the supermarket average from the warehouse store average: 365 − 130 = 235.","cimg":[["bank/ea95087d_A.png"],["bank/ea95087d_B.png"],["bank/ea95087d_C.png"],["bank/ea95087d_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"fc46af57","k":13,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/fc46af57_stem.png"],"e":"Plausible percents are 15% ± 2%, so 13% to 17%. Of 10,000 beads that is 0.13 × 10,000 = 1,300 to 0.17 × 10,000 = 1,700.","cimg":[["bank/fc46af57_A.png"],["bank/fc46af57_B.png"],["bank/fc46af57_C.png"],["bank/fc46af57_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"e7d48c8a","k":10,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/e7d48c8a_stem.png"],"e":"The 13 values are four 1s, five 2s, two 3s, one 4 and one 5, so the median (7th value) is 2. With 14 values the median is the average of the 7th and 8th values, still 2, but adding 11 raises the mean. Only II increases.","cimg":[["bank/e7d48c8a_A.png"],["bank/e7d48c8a_B.png"],["bank/e7d48c8a_C.png"],["bank/e7d48c8a_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"7b65bb28","k":10,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/7b65bb28_stem.png"],"e":"Order the prices: 3.609, 3.679, 3.699, 3.729, 3.729. The middle (3rd) value is $3.699.","cimg":[["bank/7b65bb28_A.png"],["bank/7b65bb28_B.png"],["bank/7b65bb28_C.png"],["bank/7b65bb28_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"8a714fa1","k":9,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/8a714fa1_stem.png"],"e":"Increasing x by 9% gives x + 0.09x = 1.09x.","cimg":[["bank/8a714fa1_A.png"],["bank/8a714fa1_B.png"],["bank/8a714fa1_C.png"],["bank/8a714fa1_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"7cd1c6db","k":8,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/7cd1c6db_stem.png"],"e":"Time = distance ÷ speed = 108 ÷ 12 = 9 seconds.","cimg":[["bank/7cd1c6db_A.png"],["bank/7cd1c6db_B.png"],["bank/7cd1c6db_C.png"],["bank/7cd1c6db_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"8784bc84","k":9,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/8784bc84_stem.png"],"e":"20% of 440 = 0.20 × 440 = 88.","cimg":[["bank/8784bc84_A.png"],["bank/8784bc84_B.png"],["bank/8784bc84_C.png"],["bank/8784bc84_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"8637294f","k":6,"diff":"Hard","type":"spr","img":["bank/8637294f_stem.png"],"e":"From 4a/b = 6.7, a/b = 1.675. Since a/(bn) = (a/b) × (1/n) = 26.8, n = 1.675 ÷ 26.8 = 0.0625, which is 1/16.","ad":"0.0625","a":0.0625},{"id":"8e2e424e","k":9,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/8e2e424e_stem.png"],"e":"k = 50 × 1.36 = 68 because k is 36% greater than 50. Since k = 50r, r = 68 ÷ 50 = 1.36.","cimg":[["bank/8e2e424e_A.png"],["bank/8e2e424e_B.png"],["bank/8e2e424e_C.png"],["bank/8e2e424e_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"24ad9dcb","k":8,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/24ad9dcb_stem.png"],"e":"On Jupiter the object weighs (23/10)(100) = 230 pounds, and on Venus it weighs (9/10)(100) = 90 pounds. The difference is 230 − 90 = 140 pounds.","cimg":[["bank/24ad9dcb_A.png"],["bank/24ad9dcb_B.png"],["bank/24ad9dcb_C.png"],["bank/24ad9dcb_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"be00d896","k":10,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/be00d896_stem.png"],"e":"In set C, the large values 256 and 512 pull the mean up to 1,022 ÷ 9 ≈ 113.6, far above the median of 32. Sets A and B are symmetric (mean = median), and in D the mean is below the median.","cimg":[["bank/be00d896_A.png"],["bank/be00d896_B.png"],["bank/be00d896_C.png"],["bank/be00d896_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"3d985614","k":11,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/3d985614_stem.png"],"e":"The data rise about 3.3 feet of long jump for each foot of high jump, so the slope is about 3.30. At x = 4, y = 3.30(4) + 0.82 ≈ 14 matches the points, while 3.30(4) − 3.30 ≈ 9.9 is too low.","cimg":[["bank/3d985614_A.png"],["bank/3d985614_B.png"],["bank/3d985614_C.png"],["bank/3d985614_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"560fab82","k":10,"diff":"Easy","type":"spr","img":["bank/560fab82_stem.png"],"e":"The values in the data set are 19, 21, 23 and 25, each appearing at least once, so the smallest value is 19.","ad":"19","a":19.0},{"id":"308084c5","k":13,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/308084c5_stem.png"],"e":"With the same population and the same method, a larger margin of error comes from a smaller sample, because smaller samples give less precise estimates.","cimg":[["bank/308084c5_A.png"],["bank/308084c5_B.png"],["bank/308084c5_C.png"],["bank/308084c5_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"d94018fd","k":10,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/d94018fd_stem.png"],"e":"Both dot plots have the same shape (frequencies 1, 1, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7); class B is just class A shifted up by 13. Shifting data does not change spread, so the standard deviations are equal.","cimg":[["bank/d94018fd_A.png"],["bank/d94018fd_B.png"],["bank/d94018fd_C.png"],["bank/d94018fd_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"e635aede","k":9,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/e635aede_stem.png"],"e":"Successive percent increases multiply: 2009 earnings = 1.14 × 1.04 = 1.1856 times 2007 earnings. Do not just add 14% and 4%.","cimg":[["bank/e635aede_A.png"],["bank/e635aede_B.png"],["bank/e635aede_C.png"],["bank/e635aede_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"1f4c57d7","k":10,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/1f4c57d7_stem.png"],"e":"Mean = (8 + 7 + 9) ÷ 3 = 24 ÷ 3 = 8 piglets per litter.","cimg":[["bank/1f4c57d7_A.png"],["bank/1f4c57d7_B.png"],["bank/1f4c57d7_C.png"],["bank/1f4c57d7_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"e21d10a7","k":8,"diff":"Easy","type":"spr","img":["bank/e21d10a7_stem.png"],"e":"Each orbit of the second moon takes 287 − 252 = 35 more days, so 29 orbits take 29 × 35 = 1,015 more days.","ad":"1015","a":1015.0},{"id":"7d721177","k":15,"diff":"Hard","type":"mc","img":["bank/7d721177_stem.png"],"e":"Volume = mass ÷ density = 345 ÷ 353 ≈ 0.9773 cubic meters. The edge length is the cube root, ∛0.9773 ≈ 0.992, which rounds to 0.99 meters.","cimg":[["bank/7d721177_A.png"],["bank/7d721177_B.png"],["bank/7d721177_C.png"],["bank/7d721177_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"d0d9ede4","k":8,"diff":"Easy","type":"spr","img":["bank/d0d9ede4_stem.png"],"e":"Each yard is 3 feet, so 34 yards = 34 × 3 = 102 feet.","ad":"102","a":102.0},{"id":"1d945139","k":8,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/1d945139_stem.png"],"e":"Each object has mass t/r, so 146r objects have mass 146r × (t/r) = 146t. Multiplying the number of objects by 146 multiplies the total mass by 146.","cimg":[["bank/1d945139_A.png"],["bank/1d945139_B.png"],["bank/1d945139_C.png"],["bank/1d945139_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"4b09f783","k":10,"diff":"Easy","type":"spr","img":["bank/4b09f783_stem.png"],"e":"The sum is 6 + 8 + 16 + 4 + 17 + 26 + 8 + 5 + 5 + 5 = 100, and 100 ÷ 10 = 10.","ad":"10","a":10.0},{"id":"67c0200a","k":9,"diff":"Hard","type":"spr","img":["bank/67c0200a_stem.png"],"e":"a is 70% less than b, so a = 0.30b. c is 80% greater than a, so c = 1.80 × 0.30b = 0.54b.","ad":"0.54","a":0.54},{"id":"f04d40b2","k":13,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/f04d40b2_stem.png"],"e":"Plausible percents are 35% ± 3%, so 32% to 38% of 50,000, which is 16,000 to 19,000 people. Only 16,750 falls in that range.","cimg":[["bank/f04d40b2_A.png"],["bank/f04d40b2_B.png"],["bank/f04d40b2_C.png"],["bank/f04d40b2_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"3aa0642c","k":10,"diff":"Easy","type":"spr","img":["bank/3aa0642c_stem.png"],"e":"Read the Triangle row of the table: 14 cards.","ad":"14","a":14.0},{"id":"bfa8a85c","k":10,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/bfa8a85c_stem.png"],"e":"The original 7 values have median 8 (the 4th value). For 6, 6, 8, 8, 10, 10 the median is the average of the 3rd and 4th values, (8 + 8)/2 = 8. The other lists have medians 6, 10 and 10.","cimg":[["bank/bfa8a85c_A.png"],["bank/bfa8a85c_B.png"],["bank/bfa8a85c_C.png"],["bank/bfa8a85c_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"c9dd92b1","k":11,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/c9dd92b1_stem.png"],"e":"The points rise roughly linearly, from about 1,240 at 50% to about 1,350 at 70%. Halfway between, at 60%, the trend predicts about 1,300 kg/m³.","cimg":[["bank/c9dd92b1_A.png"],["bank/c9dd92b1_B.png"],["bank/c9dd92b1_C.png"],["bank/c9dd92b1_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"9bf4c545","k":14,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/9bf4c545_stem.png"],"e":"The council wanted the opinions of all residents but surveyed only dog owners, who are likely to favor a dog park. The sample is not representative, so it is biased.","cimg":[["bank/9bf4c545_A.png"],["bank/9bf4c545_B.png"],["bank/9bf4c545_C.png"],["bank/9bf4c545_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"fa7a0164","k":10,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/fa7a0164_stem.png"],"e":"Use the low temperatures only: (49 + 37 + 41 + 54 + 63) ÷ 5 = 244 ÷ 5 = 48.8.","cimg":[["bank/fa7a0164_A.png"],["bank/fa7a0164_B.png"],["bank/fa7a0164_C.png"],["bank/fa7a0164_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"40e7a1a9","k":9,"diff":"Medium","type":"spr","img":["bank/40e7a1a9_stem.png"],"e":"The increase is 210 − 30 = 180, and 180 ÷ 30 = 6 = 600%. Check: 30 + 6(30) = 210.","ad":"600","a":600.0},{"id":"708590d7","k":10,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/708590d7_stem.png"],"e":"Mean of A = 28 ÷ 7 = 4 and mean of B = 16 ÷ 7 ≈ 2.29, so A's mean is greater.","cimg":[["bank/708590d7_A.png"],["bank/708590d7_B.png"],["bank/708590d7_C.png"],["bank/708590d7_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"bf47ad54","k":10,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/bf47ad54_stem.png"],"e":"Tables B, C and D are symmetric about 85, so each has mean 85. Table A puts more weight on the higher values (frequency 7 at 100, 4 at 70), so its mean is above 85.","cimg":[["bank/bf47ad54_A.png"],["bank/bf47ad54_B.png"],["bank/bf47ad54_C.png"],["bank/bf47ad54_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"a6b2fcce","k":10,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/a6b2fcce_stem.png"],"e":"Compare the changes between consecutive years: 2010 to 2011 goes from about 26 to 45, an increase of about 19. That is larger than 2008 to 2009 (about 12) and 2009 to 2010 (about 6).","cimg":[["bank/a6b2fcce_A.png"],["bank/a6b2fcce_B.png"],["bank/a6b2fcce_C.png"],["bank/a6b2fcce_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"699af7b3","k":9,"diff":"Hard","type":"spr","img":["bank/699af7b3_stem.png"],"e":"A = 4.68B and A = 0.00780C, so 0.0078C = 4.68B and C = 4.68B ÷ 0.0078 = 600B. 600 times B is 60,000% of B.","ad":"60000","a":60000.0},{"id":"f52123e0","k":10,"diff":"Easy","type":"spr","img":["bank/f52123e0_stem.png"],"e":"Range = maximum − minimum = 52 − 23 = 29.","ad":"29","a":29.0},{"id":"06a152cd","k":8,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/06a152cd_stem.png"],"e":"48 muffins × 2.5 ounces = 120 ounces of chocolate, and 120 ÷ 16 = 7.5 pounds.","cimg":[["bank/06a152cd_A.png"],["bank/06a152cd_B.png"],["bank/06a152cd_C.png"],["bank/06a152cd_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"7d68096f","k":14,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/7d68096f_stem.png"],"e":"The 55 teams were chosen at random from all trivia teams in the tournament, so the results can be generalized to all teams in the tournament.","cimg":[["bank/7d68096f_A.png"],["bank/7d68096f_B.png"],["bank/7d68096f_C.png"],["bank/7d68096f_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"7760c516","k":10,"diff":"Easy","type":"spr","img":["bank/7760c516_stem.png"],"e":"The sum is 6 + 10 + 13 + 2 + 15 + 22 + 10 + 4 + 4 + 4 = 90, and 90 ÷ 10 = 9 centimeters.","ad":"9","a":9.0},{"id":"8917ce38","k":8,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/8917ce38_stem.png"],"e":"90 km/h = 90,000 meters per 3,600 seconds = 25 meters per second.","cimg":[["bank/8917ce38_A.png"],["bank/8917ce38_B.png"],["bank/8917ce38_C.png"],["bank/8917ce38_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"f4b3672a","k":13,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/f4b3672a_stem.png"],"e":"The sample mean is (51 + 59 + 45 + 52 + 73) ÷ 5 = 56 trees per acre. Then 56 × 253 = 14,168 trees, which falls between 13,500 and 14,500.","cimg":[["bank/f4b3672a_A.png"],["bank/f4b3672a_B.png"],["bank/f4b3672a_C.png"],["bank/f4b3672a_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"40f0ee70","k":10,"diff":"Easy","type":"spr","img":["bank/40f0ee70_stem.png"],"e":"Mean = (5 + 2 + 15 + 9 + 9) ÷ 5 = 40 ÷ 5 = 8 minutes.","ad":"8","a":8.0},{"id":"374b18f9","k":10,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/374b18f9_stem.png"],"e":"The median is the line inside the box, which sits just past the 7,000 tick, so 7,067 is closest.","cimg":[["bank/374b18f9_A.png"],["bank/374b18f9_B.png"],["bank/374b18f9_C.png"],["bank/374b18f9_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"585de39a","k":12,"diff":"Medium","type":"spr","img":["bank/585de39a_stem.png"],"e":"On September 30 there were 97 million subscribers and 43% of them were MTN, so p = 0.43 × 97 = 41.71, about 42. The May figure of 83 million is not needed.","ad":"42","a":42.0},{"id":"4ff597db","k":10,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/4ff597db_stem.png"],"e":"The total for 20 employees is 20 × 6.7 = 134 years and the total for the remaining 19 is 19 × 6.25 = 118.75 years. The employee who left worked 134 − 118.75 = 15.25 years.","cimg":[["bank/4ff597db_A.png"],["bank/4ff597db_B.png"],["bank/4ff597db_C.png"],["bank/4ff597db_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"ec787383","k":8,"diff":"Easy","type":"spr","img":["bank/ec787383_stem.png"],"e":"1 furlong = 220 × 3 = 660 feet, so 61 furlongs = 61 × 660 = 40,260 feet.","ad":"40260","a":40260.0},{"id":"7e6c745f","k":8,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/7e6c745f_stem.png"],"e":"For the egg, $0.36 ÷ 6 = $0.06 per gram; for the milk, $0.24 ÷ 8 = $0.03 per gram. The ratio is 0.06 : 0.03 = 2 : 1.","cimg":[["bank/7e6c745f_A.png"],["bank/7e6c745f_B.png"],["bank/7e6c745f_C.png"],["bank/7e6c745f_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"7b52985c","k":11,"diff":"Medium","type":"spr","img":["bank/7b52985c_stem.png"],"e":"January 13 is x = 2 (y = 6) and January 15 is x = 4 (y = 15). The average rate of change is (15 − 6) ÷ (4 − 2) = 9 ÷ 2 = 4.5 hours per day.","ad":"4.5","a":4.5},{"id":"7ce2830a","k":14,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/7ce2830a_stem.png"],"e":"The sample was chosen at random from the students at one school only, so the results can be generalized to all students at that school, not to the whole city.","cimg":[["bank/7ce2830a_A.png"],["bank/7ce2830a_B.png"],["bank/7ce2830a_C.png"],["bank/7ce2830a_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"12dbe3de","k":12,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/12dbe3de_stem.png"],"e":"Probability = 4 defective ÷ 1,000 total = 0.004.","cimg":[["bank/12dbe3de_A.png"],["bank/12dbe3de_B.png"],["bank/12dbe3de_C.png"],["bank/12dbe3de_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"709e04de","k":9,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/709e04de_stem.png"],"e":"z = 1.13 × 100 = 113, which is 13 more than 100. 13 out of 100 is 13%.","cimg":[["bank/709e04de_A.png"],["bank/709e04de_B.png"],["bank/709e04de_C.png"],["bank/709e04de_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"642519d7","k":13,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/642519d7_stem.png"],"e":"A single random sample is only an estimate: the true city-wide percent, another sample's percent, and a different city's percent can all differ from 78%. None of the statements must be true.","cimg":[["bank/642519d7_A.png"],["bank/642519d7_B.png"],["bank/642519d7_C.png"],["bank/642519d7_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"0108ac2d","k":13,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/0108ac2d_stem.png"],"e":"The margin of error gives a range of plausible values for the population percent: 38% − 5.5% = 32.5% to 38% + 5.5% = 43.5%.","cimg":[["bank/0108ac2d_A.png"],["bank/0108ac2d_B.png"],["bank/0108ac2d_C.png"],["bank/0108ac2d_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"949cd96b","k":9,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/949cd96b_stem.png"],"e":"89% as a decimal is 0.89, so the base is 0.89h.","cimg":[["bank/949cd96b_A.png"],["bank/949cd96b_B.png"],["bank/949cd96b_C.png"],["bank/949cd96b_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"28c6bd8c","k":9,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/28c6bd8c_stem.png"],"e":"Doctor or Internet is 63% + 13% = 76% of responses, and 0.76 × 1,200 = 912.","cimg":[["bank/28c6bd8c_A.png"],["bank/28c6bd8c_B.png"],["bank/28c6bd8c_C.png"],["bank/28c6bd8c_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"912cd125","k":12,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/912cd125_q.png"],"e":"Only the 64 no-rain days count, and 16 of them were weekend days: 16/64 = 1/4.","cimg":[["bank/912cd125_A.png"],["bank/912cd125_B.png"],["bank/912cd125_C.png"],["bank/912cd125_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"3a6ed720","k":9,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/3a6ed720_stem.png"],"e":"828,000 ÷ 900,000 = 0.92, which is 92%.","cimg":[["bank/3a6ed720_A.png"],["bank/3a6ed720_B.png"],["bank/3a6ed720_C.png"],["bank/3a6ed720_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"ad7dbb22","k":11,"diff":"Medium","type":"spr","img":["bank/ad7dbb22_stem.png"],"e":"The line predicts a greater y-value than the actual one when a point lies below the line. The points below the line are near x = 2.5, 3.3, 4.1, 4.9, 7.4 and 9, which makes 6.","ad":"6","a":6.0},{"id":"85b33aa8","k":8,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/85b33aa8_stem.png"],"e":"Divide by the number of yards in a mile: 5,104 ÷ 1,760 = 2.9 miles.","cimg":[["bank/85b33aa8_A.png"],["bank/85b33aa8_B.png"],["bank/85b33aa8_C.png"],["bank/85b33aa8_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"284303f1","k":9,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/284303f1_stem.png"],"e":"6% of 250 = 0.06 × 250 = 15 birch trees.","cimg":[["bank/284303f1_A.png"],["bank/284303f1_B.png"],["bank/284303f1_C.png"],["bank/284303f1_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"ba61d95f","k":9,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/ba61d95f_stem.png"],"e":"A 7% increase means the 2016 population is 107% of the 2015 population, so k = 1.07.","cimg":[["bank/ba61d95f_A.png"],["bank/ba61d95f_B.png"],["bank/ba61d95f_C.png"],["bank/ba61d95f_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"873d2838","k":8,"diff":"Easy","type":"spr","img":["bank/873d2838_stem.png"],"e":"Area = population ÷ density = 85,100 ÷ 230 = 370 square miles.","ad":"370","a":370.0},{"id":"16988f9c","k":11,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/16988f9c_stem.png"],"e":"The points rise from left to right, so the slope is positive, which rules out A, B and C. At x = 1, y = 0.9(1) + 2.2 = 3.1 matches the point near (1, 3).","cimg":[["bank/16988f9c_A.png"],["bank/16988f9c_B.png"],["bank/16988f9c_C.png"],["bank/16988f9c_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"2cdefcb1","k":8,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/2cdefcb1_stem.png"],"e":"There are 100 centimeters in a meter, so 51 meters = 51 × 100 = 5,100 centimeters.","cimg":[["bank/2cdefcb1_A.png"],["bank/2cdefcb1_B.png"],["bank/2cdefcb1_C.png"],["bank/2cdefcb1_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"6a715bed","k":12,"diff":"Medium","type":"spr","img":["bank/6a715bed_stem.png"],"e":"At least 10 years old means the 10−19 and 20+ columns: 30 + 30 = 60 participants. Of these, Group A has 14 + 9 = 23, so the probability is 23/60.","ad":"23/60","tol":0.0011,"a":0.38333333333333336},{"id":"8cbf1415","k":9,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/8cbf1415_stem.png"],"e":"Red with stripes is 30% of the 40% that are red: 0.30 × 0.40 = 0.12, which is 12% of all items.","cimg":[["bank/8cbf1415_A.png"],["bank/8cbf1415_B.png"],["bank/8cbf1415_C.png"],["bank/8cbf1415_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"58ba7239","k":9,"diff":"Hard","type":"spr","img":["bank/58ba7239_stem.png"],"e":"b is 320% greater than 160, so b = 4.20 × 160 = 672. a is 55% less than b, so a = 0.45 × 672 = 302.4.","ad":"302.4","a":302.4},{"id":"c7c6445f","k":8,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/c7c6445f_stem.png"],"e":"One square mile = 1,760 × 1,760 = 3,097,600 square yards. Then 4.36 × 3,097,600 = 13,505,536 square yards. Remember to square the conversion factor for area.","cimg":[["bank/c7c6445f_A.png"],["bank/c7c6445f_B.png"],["bank/c7c6445f_C.png"],["bank/c7c6445f_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"c54b92a2","k":10,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/c54b92a2_stem.png"],"e":"Range = maximum − minimum = 24 − 19 = 5.0 wheels.","cimg":[["bank/c54b92a2_A.png"],["bank/c54b92a2_B.png"],["bank/c54b92a2_C.png"],["bank/c54b92a2_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"3c5b19ef","k":11,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/3c5b19ef_stem.png"],"e":"The line starts at about 16,000 visitors when t = 0 and rises to about 70,000 by t = 12, a slope of roughly 4,500 per year. That matches n = 16,090 + 4,680t.","cimg":[["bank/3c5b19ef_A.png"],["bank/3c5b19ef_B.png"],["bank/3c5b19ef_C.png"],["bank/3c5b19ef_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"73ddfdac","k":8,"diff":"Easy","type":"spr","img":["bank/73ddfdac_stem.png"],"e":"112 furlongs × 220 yards per furlong = 24,640 yards. 24,640 yards × 3 feet per yard = 73,920 feet.","ad":"73920","a":73920.0},{"id":"96a45430","k":9,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/96a45430_stem.png"],"e":"Increasing n by 6% gives 1.06n = 318. Divide both sides by 1.06 to get n = 300.","cimg":[["bank/96a45430_A.png"],["bank/96a45430_B.png"],["bank/96a45430_C.png"],["bank/96a45430_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"589cd7a6","k":12,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/589cd7a6_stem.png"],"e":"The probability is the number of brown tokens divided by the total number of tokens: 13/104. This simplifies to 1/8.","cimg":[["bank/589cd7a6_A.png"],["bank/589cd7a6_B.png"],["bank/589cd7a6_C.png"],["bank/589cd7a6_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"5267c3c7","k":9,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/5267c3c7_stem.png"],"e":"Increasing x by 400% means adding 4x to x, so the result is 5x = 60. That gives x = 12. It is not 4x, because the original amount is kept.","cimg":[["bank/5267c3c7_A.png"],["bank/5267c3c7_B.png"],["bank/5267c3c7_C.png"],["bank/5267c3c7_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"ae32cc3c","k":11,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/ae32cc3c_stem.png"],"e":"Find the line of best fit at x = 1,200. The line passes through about y = 11 there. Read the line, not the data point at (1,200, 12).","cimg":[["bank/ae32cc3c_A.png"],["bank/ae32cc3c_B.png"],["bank/ae32cc3c_C.png"],["bank/ae32cc3c_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"82dfb646","k":13,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/82dfb646_stem.png"],"e":"The 200 people were chosen at random from people who liked the book, so the results apply only to that group. Since 95% disliked the movie, most people who like the book would probably dislike the movie.","cimg":[["bank/82dfb646_A.png"],["bank/82dfb646_B.png"],["bank/82dfb646_C.png"],["bank/82dfb646_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"5c3c2e3c","k":10,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/5c3c2e3c_stem.png"],"e":"Lowering the smallest of 15 values changes the mean, the range, and the standard deviation. The median is the 8th value, so it does not change when only the lowest value gets smaller.","cimg":[["bank/5c3c2e3c_A.png"],["bank/5c3c2e3c_B.png"],["bank/5c3c2e3c_C.png"],["bank/5c3c2e3c_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"ed6b7e5f","k":12,"diff":"Easy","type":"spr","img":["bank/ed6b7e5f_stem.png"],"e":"Look only at the pepperoni row: 20 + 30 = 50 orders. Of these, 20 have thin crust, so the probability is 20/50 = 2/5, or 0.4.","ad":"2/5","tol":0.0011,"a":0.4},{"id":"c5ee6ac0","k":11,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/c5ee6ac0_stem.png"],"e":"The line slopes upward, so the slope is positive. It crosses the y-axis at about 3.4, so the best equation is y = x + 3.4.","cimg":[["bank/c5ee6ac0_A.png"],["bank/c5ee6ac0_B.png"],["bank/c5ee6ac0_C.png"],["bank/c5ee6ac0_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"9ce8cbbe","k":12,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/9ce8cbbe_stem.png"],"e":"The even numbers from 1 to 50 are 2, 4, …, 50, which is 25 numbers. Set K has 160 numbers, so the probability is 25/160 = 5/32.","cimg":[["bank/9ce8cbbe_A.png"],["bank/9ce8cbbe_B.png"],["bank/9ce8cbbe_C.png"],["bank/9ce8cbbe_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"61b87506","k":8,"diff":"Easy","type":"spr","img":["bank/61b87506_stem.png"],"e":"To keep the ratio j:k the same, both values must be multiplied by the same number. Since j is multiplied by 17, k must also be multiplied by 17.","ad":"17","a":17.0},{"id":"30db8f77","k":12,"diff":"Medium","type":"spr","img":["bank/30db8f77_stem.png"],"e":"The probability of group C is 1 − 0.44 − 0.24 = 0.32. Then 0.32 × 275 = 88 attendees.","ad":"88","a":88.0},{"id":"43744269","k":1,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/43744269_stem.png"],"e":"The altitude drops by the same amount (400 feet) every minute. A constant rate of change means a linear function, and since the altitude is falling, it is decreasing linear.","cimg":[["bank/43744269_A.png"],["bank/43744269_B.png"],["bank/43744269_C.png"],["bank/43744269_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"3ac09984","k":9,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/3ac09984_stem.png"],"e":"First convert: 7,500 × 0.075 = $562.50. A 2% fee leaves 98%, so 562.50 × 0.98 = $551.25.","cimg":[["bank/3ac09984_A.png"],["bank/3ac09984_B.png"],["bank/3ac09984_C.png"],["bank/3ac09984_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"66f03086","k":10,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/66f03086_stem.png"],"e":"There are 9 values, already in order. The median is the 5th value, which is 77.","cimg":[["bank/66f03086_A.png"],["bank/66f03086_B.png"],["bank/66f03086_C.png"],["bank/66f03086_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"61f61789","k":15,"diff":"Easy","type":"spr","img":["bank/61f61789_stem.png"],"e":"The volume of the cube is 2³ = 8 cubic centimeters. Density = mass ÷ volume = 2.56 ÷ 8 = 0.32 grams per cubic centimeter.","ad":"0.32","a":0.32},{"id":"d0430601","k":11,"diff":"Medium","type":"spr","img":["bank/d0430601_stem.png"],"e":"A slope of 57 means about 57 more people for each 1°C increase. For a 5°C increase, that is 5 × 57 = 285 more people.","ad":"285","a":285.0},{"id":"9110c120","k":10,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/9110c120_stem.png"],"e":"Both data sets have a median of 5, because 5 is the middle value in each. The 100 in data set B raises its mean above 5, so only the means are different.","cimg":[["bank/9110c120_A.png"],["bank/9110c120_B.png"],["bank/9110c120_C.png"],["bank/9110c120_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"c74df824","k":8,"diff":"Medium","type":"spr","img":["bank/c74df824_stem.png"],"e":"For square units, square the conversion factor: 1 square nautical mile = 1.852² ≈ 3.4299 square kilometers. Then 46 × 3.4299 ≈ 157.8.","ad":"157.8","a":157.8},{"id":"9296553d","k":11,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/9296553d_stem.png"],"e":"The data goes downward, so the slope is negative. The data starts near y = 6 when x = 0, so y = −x + 6 fits best.","cimg":[["bank/9296553d_A.png"],["bank/9296553d_B.png"],["bank/9296553d_C.png"],["bank/9296553d_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"d1db8def","k":10,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/d1db8def_stem.png"],"e":"Add the two frequencies: \"almost never\" is 53 and \"never\" is 29. 53 + 29 = 82 people.","cimg":[["bank/d1db8def_A.png"],["bank/d1db8def_B.png"],["bank/d1db8def_C.png"],["bank/d1db8def_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"b2f6f17d","k":9,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/b2f6f17d_stem.png"],"e":"The increase is 79.86 − 75.74 = 4.12. Divide by the original bill: 4.12 ÷ 75.74 ≈ 0.0544, which is about 5.4%.","cimg":[["bank/b2f6f17d_A.png"],["bank/b2f6f17d_B.png"],["bank/b2f6f17d_C.png"],["bank/b2f6f17d_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"4626102e","k":10,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/4626102e_stem.png"],"e":"Adding 56 to every value moves the whole data set up by 56, so the median also goes up by 56. The distance between the largest and smallest values stays the same, so the range does not change.","cimg":[["bank/4626102e_A.png"],["bank/4626102e_B.png"],["bank/4626102e_C.png"],["bank/4626102e_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"d6121490","k":7,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/d6121490_stem.png"],"e":"From the graph, the braking distance is about 100 feet at 30 mph and about 225 feet at 50 mph. The difference is 225 − 100 = 125 feet.","cimg":[["bank/d6121490_A.png"],["bank/d6121490_B.png"],["bank/d6121490_C.png"],["bank/d6121490_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"55cfaf22","k":10,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/55cfaf22_stem.png"],"e":"The mean of X is (5 + 9 + 9 + 13)/4 = 9. The mean of Y is 63/5 = 12.6. Adding 27, which is larger than the mean, raises the mean, so X has the smaller mean.","cimg":[["bank/55cfaf22_A.png"],["bank/55cfaf22_B.png"],["bank/55cfaf22_C.png"],["bank/55cfaf22_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"b58dbf88","k":11,"diff":"Easy","type":"spr","img":["bank/b58dbf88_stem.png"],"e":"Find x = 4 on the horizontal axis and go up to the point. The point is at y = 40, so the weight was 40 pounds.","ad":"40","a":40.0},{"id":"5154615f","k":15,"diff":"Easy","type":"spr","img":["bank/5154615f_stem.png"],"e":"The volume of the cube is 3³ = 27 cubic centimeters. Mass = density × volume = 0.230 × 27 = 6.21 grams.","ad":"6.21","a":6.21},{"id":"ab7740a8","k":7,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/ab7740a8_q.png"],"e":"In D, y doubles each time x increases by 1 (6, 12, 24, 48). That's exponential, not linear. The other tables increase by a constant amount.","cimg":[["bank/ab7740a8_A.png"],["bank/ab7740a8_B.png"],["bank/ab7740a8_C.png"],["bank/ab7740a8_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"2a08d878","k":12,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/2a08d878_q.png"],"e":"There are n + 12 books in all and n are nonfiction, so the probability is n/(n + 12).","cimg":[["bank/2a08d878_A.png"],["bank/2a08d878_B.png"],["bank/2a08d878_C.png"],["bank/2a08d878_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"820d7a73","k":10,"diff":"Easy","type":"spr","img":["bank/820d7a73_stem.png"],"e":"The bar for group 6 reaches the line at 40. Check: the bar values 30, 63, 38, 50, 47, 40, 54, 60, 17, 20 add to 419, which matches the total.","ad":"40","a":40.0},{"id":"38a9ac45","k":8,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/38a9ac45_q.png"],"e":"In 5 days, 5 × 1,200 = 6,000 accounts are registered, and 6,000/60,000 = 1/10.","cimg":[["bank/38a9ac45_A.png"],["bank/38a9ac45_B.png"],["bank/38a9ac45_C.png"],["bank/38a9ac45_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"9c44f828","k":9,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/9c44f828_stem.png"],"e":"50% means half. Half of 840 is 0.5 × 840 = 420 seats.","cimg":[["bank/9c44f828_A.png"],["bank/9c44f828_B.png"],["bank/9c44f828_C.png"],["bank/9c44f828_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"b695711c","k":13,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/b695711c_stem.png"],"e":"The sample was chosen at random from second-year piano students in the region. So the results can be generalized only to all piano students in the region who were in their second year with their conservatory.","cimg":[["bank/b695711c_A.png"],["bank/b695711c_B.png"],["bank/b695711c_C.png"],["bank/b695711c_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"eb672707","k":8,"diff":"Easy","type":"spr","img":["bank/eb672707_stem.png"],"e":"Divide by 3, because 3 teaspoons make 1 tablespoon: 14 ÷ 3 = 14/3 ≈ 4.67 tablespoons.","ad":"14/3","tol":0.0011,"a":4.666666666666667},{"id":"7270d642","k":8,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/7270d642_stem.png"],"e":"Distance = rate × time = 16 meters per second × 4 seconds = 64 meters.","cimg":[["bank/7270d642_A.png"],["bank/7270d642_B.png"],["bank/7270d642_C.png"],["bank/7270d642_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"6e3ab4bf","k":10,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/6e3ab4bf_stem.png"],"e":"The bar for gift C reaches 18. Check: 14 + 8 + 18 + 3 = 43, which matches the total.","cimg":[["bank/6e3ab4bf_A.png"],["bank/6e3ab4bf_B.png"],["bank/6e3ab4bf_C.png"],["bank/6e3ab4bf_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"c256b723","k":9,"diff":"Easy","type":"spr","img":["bank/c256b723_stem.png"],"e":"20% of $50 is 0.20 × 50 = $10.","ad":"10","a":10.0},{"id":"90ba8f98","k":11,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/90ba8f98_stem.png"],"e":"The line passes near (0, 1.5) and (7, 14.5). Its slope is (14.5 − 1.5)/7 ≈ 1.9, so 2 is the closest choice.","cimg":[["bank/90ba8f98_A.png"],["bank/90ba8f98_B.png"],["bank/90ba8f98_C.png"],["bank/90ba8f98_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"881ef5f5","k":10,"diff":"Easy","type":"spr","img":["bank/881ef5f5_stem.png"],"e":"Nine consecutive integers are spread evenly around the middle number. So the mean and the median both equal the middle number, and |a − b| = 0.","ad":"0","a":0.0},{"id":"273b7f37","k":9,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/273b7f37_stem.png"],"e":"10% of 760 is 0.10 × 760 = 76 potatoes.","cimg":[["bank/273b7f37_A.png"],["bank/273b7f37_B.png"],["bank/273b7f37_C.png"],["bank/273b7f37_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"2e511919","k":10,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/2e511919_stem.png"],"e":"The highest point on the line graph is above 1994, at about 155 chipmunks. So 1994 had the greatest estimated number.","cimg":[["bank/2e511919_A.png"],["bank/2e511919_B.png"],["bank/2e511919_C.png"],["bank/2e511919_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"7ed0d098","k":9,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/7ed0d098_stem.png"],"e":"An 8-hour workday is 8 × 60 = 480 minutes. 15% of 480 is 0.15 × 480 = 72 minutes.","cimg":[["bank/7ed0d098_A.png"],["bank/7ed0d098_B.png"],["bank/7ed0d098_C.png"],["bank/7ed0d098_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"38525983","k":11,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/38525983_stem.png"],"e":"The line passes near (0, 3.2) and (10, 9.2). Its slope is (9.2 − 3.2)/10 = 0.6.","cimg":[["bank/38525983_A.png"],["bank/38525983_B.png"],["bank/38525983_C.png"],["bank/38525983_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"c141366d","k":1,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/c141366d_stem.png"],"e":"The graph is a straight line, so the function is linear. The line rises from left to right, so it is increasing.","cimg":[["bank/c141366d_A.png"],["bank/c141366d_B.png"],["bank/c141366d_C.png"],["bank/c141366d_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"20845d36","k":9,"diff":"Hard","type":"spr","img":["bank/20845d36_stem.png"],"e":"Since a is 70% less than b, a = 0.3b. Since c is 60% greater than a, c = 1.6a = 1.6 × 0.3b = 0.48b.","ad":"0.48","a":0.48},{"id":"8bf3f67a","k":8,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/8bf3f67a_stem.png"],"e":"Multiply by 6, because each fathom is 6 feet: 39 × 6 = 234 feet.","cimg":[["bank/8bf3f67a_A.png"],["bank/8bf3f67a_B.png"],["bank/8bf3f67a_C.png"],["bank/8bf3f67a_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"a478f9f5","k":12,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/a478f9f5_stem.png"],"e":"3 of the 157 gemstones are color Y, so the probability is 3/157.","cimg":[["bank/a478f9f5_A.png"],["bank/a478f9f5_B.png"],["bank/a478f9f5_C.png"],["bank/a478f9f5_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"dae79de4","k":12,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/dae79de4_stem.png"],"e":"105 of the 135 customers are at least 40 years old, so the probability is 105/135. Use the row total, not a column total.","cimg":[["bank/dae79de4_A.png"],["bank/dae79de4_B.png"],["bank/dae79de4_C.png"],["bank/dae79de4_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"4bb25495","k":10,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/4bb25495_stem.png"],"e":"The sum is 2.0 + 21 + 61 + 26 + 0.44 = 110.44. Divide by 5 to get about 22.09, which rounds to 22.","cimg":[["bank/4bb25495_A.png"],["bank/4bb25495_B.png"],["bank/4bb25495_C.png"],["bank/4bb25495_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"aa43b41f","k":14,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/aa43b41f_stem.png"],"e":"The viewers chose for themselves whether to answer the poll, so it is not a random sample. That means the results cannot be generalized to the whole US population.","cimg":[["bank/aa43b41f_A.png"],["bank/aa43b41f_B.png"],["bank/aa43b41f_C.png"],["bank/aa43b41f_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"cb4894f9","k":8,"diff":"Easy","type":"spr","img":["bank/cb4894f9_stem.png"],"e":"Multiply by 1,760, because each mile is 1,760 yards: 19.700 × 1,760 = 34,672 yards per hour.","ad":"34672","a":34672.0},{"id":"b6569d0e","k":12,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/b6569d0e_q.png"],"e":"At least 50 years old: 13 + 11 + 7 + 3 = 34. At least 60: 7 + 3 = 10. Fraction = 10/34.","cimg":[["bank/b6569d0e_A.png"],["bank/b6569d0e_B.png"],["bank/b6569d0e_C.png"],["bank/b6569d0e_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"50b99b2d","k":8,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/50b99b2d_stem.png"],"e":"R's speed is 4x/y, so S's speed is twice that, 8x/y. Time = distance ÷ speed = 24x ÷ (8x/y) = 3y seconds.","cimg":[["bank/50b99b2d_A.png"],["bank/50b99b2d_B.png"],["bank/50b99b2d_C.png"],["bank/50b99b2d_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"5dc386fb","k":12,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/5dc386fb_stem.png"],"e":"There are 39 + 6 = 45 states with a sales tax. Of these, 6 have no income tax, and 6/45 ≈ 13.3%.","cimg":[["bank/5dc386fb_A.png"],["bank/5dc386fb_B.png"],["bank/5dc386fb_C.png"],["bank/5dc386fb_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"c47256ca","k":8,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/c47256ca_stem.png"],"e":"Multiply by 3, because each yard is 3 feet: 64 × 3 = 192 feet per second.","cimg":[["bank/c47256ca_A.png"],["bank/c47256ca_B.png"],["bank/c47256ca_C.png"],["bank/c47256ca_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"86684ce9","k":9,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/86684ce9_stem.png"],"e":"Increasing x by 1,800% adds 18x to x, so the result is 19x = 684. That gives x = 684 ÷ 19 = 36.","cimg":[["bank/86684ce9_A.png"],["bank/86684ce9_B.png"],["bank/86684ce9_C.png"],["bank/86684ce9_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"551c52b9","k":8,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/551c52b9_stem.png"],"e":"39w hours is 39 groups of w hours. Tilly earns p dollars for each group, so she earns 39p dollars.","cimg":[["bank/551c52b9_A.png"],["bank/551c52b9_B.png"],["bank/551c52b9_C.png"],["bank/551c52b9_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"e97fd3f8","k":10,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/e97fd3f8_stem.png"],"e":"Five boards are between 18 and 48 cm, with prices 10, 15, 20, 30, and 40. Their mean is 115/5 = $23.00. The boards wider than 48 cm average 255/4 = $63.75, so choices A and B are wrong.","cimg":[["bank/e97fd3f8_A.png"],["bank/e97fd3f8_B.png"],["bank/e97fd3f8_C.png"],["bank/e97fd3f8_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"014c47ab","k":12,"diff":"Easy","type":"spr","img":["bank/014c47ab_stem.png"],"e":"Look only at the 50 tulips. 35 of them are at site A, so the probability is 35/50 = 0.7.","ad":"7/10","tol":0.0011,"a":0.7},{"id":"1180401d","k":8,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/1180401d_stem.png"],"e":"The land area is 92.1 − 11.3 = 80.8 square miles. The density is 621,000 ÷ 80.8 ≈ 7,686, which is closest to 7,690 people per square mile.","cimg":[["bank/1180401d_A.png"],["bank/1180401d_B.png"],["bank/1180401d_C.png"],["bank/1180401d_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"57481175","k":10,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/57481175_stem.png"],"e":"The bar graph shows 11 vervets and 5 mandrills. The difference is 11 − 5 = 6.","cimg":[["bank/57481175_A.png"],["bank/57481175_B.png"],["bank/57481175_C.png"],["bank/57481175_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"1b8e412e","k":12,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/1b8e412e_stem.png"],"e":"Only one of the three numbers, 26, is positive. So the probability is 1/3.","cimg":[["bank/1b8e412e_A.png"],["bank/1b8e412e_B.png"],["bank/1b8e412e_C.png"],["bank/1b8e412e_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"f6cbb04a","k":8,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/f6cbb04a_stem.png"],"e":"Distance is proportional to time. The time 9k is 3 times the time 3k, so the distance is 3 times as large: 55(9k) ÷ 55(3k) = 3.","cimg":[["bank/f6cbb04a_A.png"],["bank/f6cbb04a_B.png"],["bank/f6cbb04a_C.png"],["bank/f6cbb04a_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"568bc2a4","k":8,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/568bc2a4_stem.png"],"e":"Each furlong is 220 × 3 = 660 feet. So 354 × 660 = 233,640 feet.","cimg":[["bank/568bc2a4_A.png"],["bank/568bc2a4_B.png"],["bank/568bc2a4_C.png"],["bank/568bc2a4_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"96c3e32d","k":8,"diff":"Easy","type":"spr","img":["bank/96c3e32d_stem.png"],"e":"Force = pressure × area = 19 pounds per square inch × 874 square inches = 16,606 pounds.","ad":"16606","a":16606.0},{"id":"98958ae8","k":10,"diff":"Medium","type":"spr","img":["bank/98958ae8_stem.png"],"e":"First find each set's total: 75 × 25 = 1,875 and 50 × 65 = 3,250. The combined mean is (1,875 + 3,250)/125 = 5,125/125 = 41. Do not just average 25 and 65, because the sets are different sizes.","ad":"41","a":41.0},{"id":"391ae4b2","k":10,"diff":"Hard","type":"mc","img":["bank/391ae4b2_stem.png"],"e":"Adding 10, which is smaller than every value in F, pulls G's mean down and can only lower or keep its median. So F's mean and median are at least as large as G's, and neither is less for F.","cimg":[["bank/391ae4b2_A.png"],["bank/391ae4b2_B.png"],["bank/391ae4b2_C.png"],["bank/391ae4b2_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"4096a482","k":13,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/4096a482_stem.png"],"e":"A margin of error gives a range of plausible values for the population mean: 20.5 ± 1, or 19.5 to 21.5. It does not guarantee the true mean is in that range, and it says nothing about individual values.","cimg":[["bank/4096a482_A.png"],["bank/4096a482_B.png"],["bank/4096a482_C.png"],["bank/4096a482_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"57f45509","k":10,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/57f45509_stem.png"],"e":"The median is the line inside the box of a box plot. Here that line is at 5.","cimg":[["bank/57f45509_A.png"],["bank/57f45509_B.png"],["bank/57f45509_C.png"],["bank/57f45509_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"2a59eb45","k":10,"diff":"Medium","type":"spr","img":["bank/2a59eb45_stem.png"],"e":"The totals are 75 × 32 = 2,400 and 50 × 62 = 3,100. The combined mean is (2,400 + 3,100)/125 = 5,500/125 = 44.","ad":"44","a":44.0},{"id":"623dbebb","k":9,"diff":"Hard","type":"spr","img":["bank/623dbebb_stem.png"],"e":"The consumer price is 270% of $5.00: 2.7 × 5 = $13.50. Taking 70% off leaves 30%, so 0.3 × 13.50 = $4.05.","ad":"4.05","a":4.05},{"id":"2afd3cec","k":9,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/2afd3cec_stem.png"],"e":"The 360 marbles that remain are 80% of the original, so the original was 360 ÷ 0.8 = 450. The number removed is 450 − 360 = 90.","cimg":[["bank/2afd3cec_A.png"],["bank/2afd3cec_B.png"],["bank/2afd3cec_C.png"],["bank/2afd3cec_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"2e92cc21","k":9,"diff":"Hard","type":"spr","img":["bank/2e92cc21_stem.png"],"e":"90% less than 47 means 10% of 47, so b = 4.7. 110% greater than b means 210% of b, so a = 2.1 × 4.7 = 9.87.","ad":"9.87","a":9.87},{"id":"7f84b136","k":9,"diff":"Medium","type":"spr","img":["bank/7f84b136_stem.png"],"e":"Divide group C by group A and multiply by 100: 690/375 = 1.84, so p = 184.","ad":"184","a":184.0},{"id":"77cf4fa6","k":9,"diff":"Easy","type":"spr","img":["bank/77cf4fa6_stem.png"],"e":"10% of 170 is 0.10 × 170 = 17 green blocks.","ad":"17","a":17.0},{"id":"2d31caae","k":9,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/2d31caae_stem.png"],"e":"Employee A took 145 calls, and 16 of them got 1 star. 16/145 ≈ 0.110, which is 11%.","cimg":[["bank/2d31caae_A.png"],["bank/2d31caae_B.png"],["bank/2d31caae_C.png"],["bank/2d31caae_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"4a422e3e","k":14,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/4a422e3e_stem.png"],"e":"Families at a playground are not a random sample of the community, because they are more likely to have children. So the sampling method is flawed and the estimate may be biased.","cimg":[["bank/4a422e3e_A.png"],["bank/4a422e3e_B.png"],["bank/4a422e3e_C.png"],["bank/4a422e3e_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"94660ba8","k":8,"diff":"Easy","type":"spr","img":["bank/94660ba8_stem.png"],"e":"Divide by 1,760, because each mile is 1,760 yards: 24,816 ÷ 1,760 = 14.1 miles per hour.","ad":"14.1","a":14.1},{"id":"ba0e23b0","k":9,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/ba0e23b0_stem.png"],"e":"The increase is 140 − 10 = 130. As a percent of the original 10, that is 130/10 × 100 = 1,300%. The answer is not 1,400%, which is what 140 is OF 10.","cimg":[["bank/ba0e23b0_A.png"],["bank/ba0e23b0_B.png"],["bank/ba0e23b0_C.png"],["bank/ba0e23b0_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"8156d446","k":11,"diff":"Medium","type":"spr","img":["bank/8156d446_stem.png"],"e":"The line starts at about 80 people at 25°C and rises about 57 people per degree. At 32°C, that is 80 + 7 × 57 ≈ 479, which rounds to 480. Reading the line on the graph at x = 32 also gives about 480.","ad":"480","a":480.0},{"id":"c2e7fa6d","k":15,"diff":"Hard","type":"spr","img":["bank/c2e7fa6d_stem.png"],"e":"The total area is 4,640 ÷ 29 = 160 m². If the small side is s, the areas are s² and 9s², so 10s² = 160 and s² = 16. The larger square's area is 144 m², and its flux is 144 × 29 = 4,176.","ad":"4176","a":4176.0},{"id":"9b9da812","k":11,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/9b9da812_stem.png"],"e":"The data rises and starts at the origin, so the slope is positive and the y-intercept is about 0. The points rise about 0.6 per unit, so y = 0.606x fits best.","cimg":[["bank/9b9da812_A.png"],["bank/9b9da812_B.png"],["bank/9b9da812_C.png"],["bank/9b9da812_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"e821a26d","k":7,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/e821a26d_stem.png"],"e":"The data rises and then falls, so the parabola opens downward and the x² coefficient is negative. At x = 0 the value is about 745, so the constant is +745.73.","cimg":[["bank/e821a26d_A.png"],["bank/e821a26d_B.png"],["bank/e821a26d_C.png"],["bank/e821a26d_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"21e539a0","k":8,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/21e539a0_stem.png"],"e":"The rate is 88x/(5y) ounces per minute. In 9y minutes, the hose puts in (88x/(5y)) × 9y = 792x/5 ounces.","cimg":[["bank/21e539a0_A.png"],["bank/21e539a0_B.png"],["bank/21e539a0_C.png"],["bank/21e539a0_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"9eb896c5","k":11,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/9eb896c5_stem.png"],"e":"The data rises steeply, about 3 units of y for each unit of x, and starts near 0. So y = 3x + 0.8 fits best.","cimg":[["bank/9eb896c5_A.png"],["bank/9eb896c5_B.png"],["bank/9eb896c5_C.png"],["bank/9eb896c5_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"194ae3b1","k":9,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/194ae3b1_stem.png"],"e":"A 29% increase means multiplying by 1.29: 113,000 × 1.29 = 145,770, which is closest to 145,800.","cimg":[["bank/194ae3b1_A.png"],["bank/194ae3b1_B.png"],["bank/194ae3b1_C.png"],["bank/194ae3b1_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"79340403","k":10,"diff":"Easy","type":"spr","img":["bank/79340403_stem.png"],"e":"The bar for group 1 reaches 30. Check: the bar values 30, 62, 36, 50, 46, 40, 54, 60, 16, 20 add to 414, which matches the total.","ad":"30","a":30.0},{"id":"a8fabad0","k":9,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/a8fabad0_stem.png"],"e":"15% of $78.20 is 0.15 × 78.20 ≈ $11.73, which is closest to $12.00.","cimg":[["bank/a8fabad0_A.png"],["bank/a8fabad0_B.png"],["bank/a8fabad0_C.png"],["bank/a8fabad0_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"4837406c","k":8,"diff":"Easy","type":"spr","img":["bank/4837406c_stem.png"],"e":"Time = distance ÷ speed = 24 ÷ 6 = 4 seconds.","ad":"4","a":4.0},{"id":"d112bc9d","k":11,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/d112bc9d_stem.png"],"e":"From x = 2 to x = 3, the temperature rises from 60°F to about 73°F, a 13-degree increase. That is the largest increase among the choices.","cimg":[["bank/d112bc9d_A.png"],["bank/d112bc9d_B.png"],["bank/d112bc9d_C.png"],["bank/d112bc9d_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"99550621","k":8,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/99550621_stem.png"],"e":"Divide the room's area by the space each person needs: 5,400 ÷ 8 = 675 people.","cimg":[["bank/99550621_A.png"],["bank/99550621_B.png"],["bank/99550621_C.png"],["bank/99550621_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"3318d37b","k":8,"diff":"Easy","type":"spr","img":["bank/3318d37b_stem.png"],"e":"Cost = price per pound × pounds = 11.00 × 6 = 66 dollars.","ad":"66","a":66.0},{"id":"93779b53","k":10,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/93779b53_stem.png"],"e":"The bar for activity 3 reaches just below 40, at 39.","cimg":[["bank/93779b53_A.png"],["bank/93779b53_B.png"],["bank/93779b53_C.png"],["bank/93779b53_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"9d935bd8","k":10,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/9d935bd8_stem.png"],"e":"In order, the 7 values are 19.5, 21.9, 25.9, 27.9, 30.1, 35.5, 36.4, so the median is 27.9%. The difference is 27.9 − 26.95 = 0.95%.","cimg":[["bank/9d935bd8_A.png"],["bank/9d935bd8_B.png"],["bank/9d935bd8_C.png"],["bank/9d935bd8_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"8c5dbd3e","k":9,"diff":"Hard","type":"spr","img":["bank/8c5dbd3e_stem.png"],"e":"55% less than 50 means 45% of 50, so z = 22.5. 110% greater than z means 210% of z, so w = 2.1 × 22.5 = 47.25.","ad":"47.25","a":47.25},{"id":"a067c926","k":10,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/a067c926_stem.png"],"e":"August has 50 students and July has 40. The difference is 50 − 40 = 10.","cimg":[["bank/a067c926_A.png"],["bank/a067c926_B.png"],["bank/a067c926_C.png"],["bank/a067c926_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"94c65646","k":9,"diff":"Easy","type":"spr","img":["bank/94c65646_stem.png"],"e":"Write 0.96x = 432. Then x = 432 ÷ 0.96 = 450.","ad":"450","a":450.0},{"id":"5c24c861","k":7,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/5c24c861_stem.png"],"e":"On the curve, x = 55 falls between the points at 50 mph (about 180 ft) and 60 mph (about 250 ft). So the stopping distance is about 210 feet.","cimg":[["bank/5c24c861_A.png"],["bank/5c24c861_B.png"],["bank/5c24c861_C.png"],["bank/5c24c861_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"5f3ee607","k":11,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/5f3ee607_stem.png"],"e":"The data falls from left to right, so the slope is negative. The data starts near y = 10 when x = 0, so y = −1.9x + 10.1 fits best.","cimg":[["bank/5f3ee607_A.png"],["bank/5f3ee607_B.png"],["bank/5f3ee607_C.png"],["bank/5f3ee607_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"9e2bf782","k":10,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/9e2bf782_stem.png"],"e":"With 33 fish in order, the median is the 17th weight. The 10 tank A fish are the lightest and fill positions 1–10, so positions 11–21 are tank B fish (5 to 13 ounces). Only 8 is in that range.","cimg":[["bank/9e2bf782_A.png"],["bank/9e2bf782_B.png"],["bank/9e2bf782_C.png"],["bank/9e2bf782_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"9ba3e283","k":13,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/9ba3e283_stem.png"],"e":"The state has about 1,800 × 26 = 46,800 eighth graders. Fewer than two siblings is 100% − 34.6% = 65.4%, and 0.654 × 46,800 ≈ 30,600.","cimg":[["bank/9ba3e283_A.png"],["bank/9ba3e283_B.png"],["bank/9ba3e283_C.png"],["bank/9ba3e283_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"4cc05491","k":11,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/4cc05491_stem.png"],"e":"The line passes near (0, 0.3) and (8, 14.7). Its slope is about (14.7 − 0.3)/8 ≈ 1.8.","cimg":[["bank/4cc05491_A.png"],["bank/4cc05491_B.png"],["bank/4cc05491_C.png"],["bank/4cc05491_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"54cb53cf","k":9,"diff":"Hard","type":"spr","img":["bank/54cb53cf_stem.png"],"e":"Let the 2014 population be 1 unit, so the 2018 population is 1.27. Then p = (1/1.27) × 100 ≈ 78.74, which rounds to 79.","ad":"79","a":79.0},{"id":"a9647302","k":10,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/a9647302_stem.png"],"e":"The bar heights are 4, 7, 1, 3, and 6, which sum to 21. The mean is 21 ÷ 5 = 4.2.","cimg":[["bank/a9647302_A.png"],["bank/a9647302_B.png"],["bank/a9647302_C.png"],["bank/a9647302_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"7b731fc3","k":9,"diff":"Easy","type":"spr","img":["bank/7b731fc3_stem.png"],"e":"A number 40% greater than 115 is 115 × 1.40 = 161.","ad":"161","a":161.0},{"id":"e9f4521a","k":9,"diff":"Easy","type":"spr","img":["bank/e9f4521a_stem.png"],"e":"Set up 13 = (p/100) × 25, so p = 1300 ÷ 25 = 52.","ad":"52","a":52.0},{"id":"1c2f50a6","k":9,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/1c2f50a6_stem.png"],"e":"A 20% reduction leaves 80% of the price: 0.80 × $50 = $40.","cimg":[["bank/1c2f50a6_A.png"],["bank/1c2f50a6_B.png"],["bank/1c2f50a6_C.png"],["bank/1c2f50a6_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"89c39d77","k":8,"diff":"Easy","type":"spr","img":["bank/89c39d77_stem.png"],"e":"Multiply miles per hour by 1,760 yards per mile: 20.3 × 1,760 = 35,728 yards per hour.","ad":"35728","a":35728.0},{"id":"8193e8cd","k":10,"diff":"Easy","type":"spr","img":["bank/8193e8cd_stem.png"],"e":"The mean is the sum divided by 5, so the mean is always 1/5 of the sum of the five numbers (sum 28, mean 5.6, and 5.6/28 = 1/5).","ad":"1/5","tol":0.0011,"a":0.2},{"id":"dccdb20c","k":9,"diff":"Easy","type":"spr","img":["bank/dccdb20c_stem.png"],"e":"6% of 450 is 0.06 × 450 = 27 black tiles.","ad":"27","a":27.0},{"id":"661dfddd","k":11,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/661dfddd_stem.png"],"e":"The line of best fit slopes downward from left to right, so as elevation increases, temperature tends to decrease.","cimg":[["bank/661dfddd_A.png"],["bank/661dfddd_B.png"],["bank/661dfddd_C.png"],["bank/661dfddd_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"73362607","k":9,"diff":"Easy","type":"spr","img":["bank/73362607_stem.png"],"e":"10% of 750 is 0.10 × 750 = 75 tomatoes.","ad":"75","a":75.0},{"id":"89f20d9e","k":12,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/89f20d9e_stem.png"],"e":"Participants at least 10 years old are in the 10–19 and 20+ columns: 30 + 30 = 60 people. Of those, Group A has 17 + 8 = 25, so the probability is 25/60 = 5/12.","cimg":[["bank/89f20d9e_A.png"],["bank/89f20d9e_B.png"],["bank/89f20d9e_C.png"],["bank/89f20d9e_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"a03b7e02","k":1,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/a03b7e02_stem.png"],"e":"Each time x increases by 1, f(x) increases by the same amount, 1. A constant increase means f is an increasing linear function.","cimg":[["bank/a03b7e02_A.png"],["bank/a03b7e02_B.png"],["bank/a03b7e02_C.png"],["bank/a03b7e02_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"97631565","k":13,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/97631565_stem.png"],"e":"In the sample, 16/20 = 80% are enrolled in exactly three courses. Applying that to all 400 employees gives 0.80 × 400 = 320.","cimg":[["bank/97631565_A.png"],["bank/97631565_B.png"],["bank/97631565_C.png"],["bank/97631565_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"3d73a58b","k":9,"diff":"Medium","type":"spr","img":["bank/3d73a58b_stem.png"],"e":"The retail price is 290% of $7.00: 2.90 × 7 = $20.30. An 80% discount leaves 20% of that: 0.20 × 20.30 = $4.06.","ad":"4.06","a":4.06},{"id":"7b1a3200","k":10,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/7b1a3200_stem.png"],"e":"Count the dots stacked above 16 on the dot plot: there are 6.","cimg":[["bank/7b1a3200_A.png"],["bank/7b1a3200_B.png"],["bank/7b1a3200_C.png"],["bank/7b1a3200_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"79137c1b","k":11,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/79137c1b_stem.png"],"e":"The data rise about 100 thousand dollars per 1 thousand square feet (about 200 at x = 1 and 300 at x = 2), so the slope is about 100 and the intercept about 100, giving y = 100x + 100.","cimg":[["bank/79137c1b_A.png"],["bank/79137c1b_B.png"],["bank/79137c1b_C.png"],["bank/79137c1b_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"b8150b17","k":12,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/b8150b17_stem.png"],"e":"The probability equals the fraction of beads with a defect: 29 out of 100, or 29/100.","cimg":[["bank/b8150b17_A.png"],["bank/b8150b17_B.png"],["bank/b8150b17_C.png"],["bank/b8150b17_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"7d093333","k":8,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/7d093333_stem.png"],"e":"One square meter is 3.28² ≈ 10.76 square feet, and one hour is 60 minutes. So 250 ÷ 10.76 ÷ 60 ≈ 0.39 square meters per minute.","cimg":[["bank/7d093333_A.png"],["bank/7d093333_B.png"],["bank/7d093333_C.png"],["bank/7d093333_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"1dcea480","k":12,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/1dcea480_stem.png"],"e":"The number of blue marbles is the probability times the total: 0.35 × 60 = 21.","cimg":[["bank/1dcea480_A.png"],["bank/1dcea480_B.png"],["bank/1dcea480_C.png"],["bank/1dcea480_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"fdfc90e4","k":11,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/fdfc90e4_stem.png"],"e":"Read the line itself, not the data points: it runs from about (24, 10) to about (34.7, 0), a slope of about −0.93. At x = 32 the line is at about 10 − 0.93 × 8 ≈ 2.5, closest to 2.4.","cimg":[["bank/fdfc90e4_A.png"],["bank/fdfc90e4_B.png"],["bank/fdfc90e4_C.png"],["bank/fdfc90e4_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"a51e6f93","k":9,"diff":"Medium","type":"spr","img":["bank/a51e6f93_stem.png"],"e":"0.1152 = 0.0008b, so b = 144. Then 144 = 0.25c, so c = 144 ÷ 0.25 = 576.","ad":"576","a":576.0},{"id":"674a4084","k":8,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/674a4084_stem.png"],"e":"Divide feet by 3 to get yards: (3/20) ÷ 3 = 1/20 yard per second.","cimg":[["bank/674a4084_A.png"],["bank/674a4084_B.png"],["bank/674a4084_C.png"],["bank/674a4084_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"a0b165f8","k":9,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/a0b165f8_stem.png"],"e":"A 12.5% increase means 99 = 1.125 × (January count), so the January count is 99 ÷ 1.125 = 88.","cimg":[["bank/a0b165f8_A.png"],["bank/a0b165f8_B.png"],["bank/a0b165f8_C.png"],["bank/a0b165f8_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"34e18ce4","k":9,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/34e18ce4_stem.png"],"e":"4% of 350 is 0.04 × 350 = 14 balls.","cimg":[["bank/34e18ce4_A.png"],["bank/34e18ce4_B.png"],["bank/34e18ce4_C.png"],["bank/34e18ce4_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"c943acba","k":12,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/c943acba_stem.png"],"e":"2 of the 7 houses are blue, so the probability is 2/7.","cimg":[["bank/c943acba_A.png"],["bank/c943acba_B.png"],["bank/c943acba_C.png"],["bank/c943acba_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"1e562f24","k":13,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/1e562f24_stem.png"],"e":"A margin of error gives a plausible range of estimate ± margin: 0.49 − 0.04 = 0.45 to 0.49 + 0.04 = 0.53. A sample cannot show the exact value.","cimg":[["bank/1e562f24_A.png"],["bank/1e562f24_B.png"],["bank/1e562f24_C.png"],["bank/1e562f24_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"89f8d08a","k":13,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/89f8d08a_stem.png"],"e":"In the sample, 20/80 = 1/4 bought fruit. Applying that to all 1,500 customers gives an estimate of 375, but a sample supports only a best estimate, not an exact count.","cimg":[["bank/89f8d08a_A.png"],["bank/89f8d08a_B.png"],["bank/89f8d08a_C.png"],["bank/89f8d08a_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"54d93874","k":10,"diff":"Medium","type":"spr","img":["bank/54d93874_stem.png"],"e":"Andrew's masses sum to 16.8, so his mean is 2.8 and Maria's mean is 2.9. Maria's six masses must then sum to 6 × 2.9 = 17.4, and her other five sum to 14.8, so x = 17.4 − 14.8 = 2.6.","ad":"2.6","a":2.6},{"id":"6a305cd0","k":13,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/6a305cd0_stem.png"],"e":"The margin of error gives a plausible range of 37 ± 3, so the population mean is plausibly between 34 and 40.","cimg":[["bank/6a305cd0_A.png"],["bank/6a305cd0_B.png"],["bank/6a305cd0_C.png"],["bank/6a305cd0_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"048811bd","k":9,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/048811bd_stem.png"],"e":"10% of 370 is 0.10 × 370 = 37.","cimg":[["bank/048811bd_A.png"],["bank/048811bd_B.png"],["bank/048811bd_C.png"],["bank/048811bd_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"e9129a5c","k":11,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/e9129a5c_stem.png"],"e":"The line rises, so the slope is positive. It goes from about y = 2.5 at x = 0 to about y = 4.7 at x = 10, a slope of about 2.2/10 = 0.22.","cimg":[["bank/e9129a5c_A.png"],["bank/e9129a5c_B.png"],["bank/e9129a5c_C.png"],["bank/e9129a5c_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"869a32f1","k":10,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/869a32f1_stem.png"],"e":"The median, mean (405/5 = 81) and mode are all 81. The range is 82 − 80 = 2, which is not 81.","cimg":[["bank/869a32f1_A.png"],["bank/869a32f1_B.png"],["bank/869a32f1_C.png"],["bank/869a32f1_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"916ffe9b","k":13,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/916ffe9b_stem.png"],"e":"In the poll Cruz led by 483 − 320 = 163 of 803 voters. The election has 6,424 ÷ 803 = 8 times as many voters, so the expected margin is 163 × 8 = 1,304.","cimg":[["bank/916ffe9b_A.png"],["bank/916ffe9b_B.png"],["bank/916ffe9b_C.png"],["bank/916ffe9b_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"8173f32b","k":13,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/8173f32b_stem.png"],"e":"A plausible range is the estimate ± the margin of error: 4.23 − 0.08 = 4.15 to 4.23 + 0.08 = 4.31.","cimg":[["bank/8173f32b_A.png"],["bank/8173f32b_B.png"],["bank/8173f32b_C.png"],["bank/8173f32b_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"a3384df0","k":8,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/a3384df0_stem.png"],"e":"One third of the 180 females is 60. Chinstrap has 59 females, the closest to 60.","cimg":[["bank/a3384df0_A.png"],["bank/a3384df0_B.png"],["bank/a3384df0_C.png"],["bank/a3384df0_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"6670e407","k":10,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/6670e407_stem.png"],"e":"Foothill's mean is 388/5 = 77.6 and Valley's is 321/5 = 64.2. The medians are 76 for Foothill and 65 for Valley, so both statements are true.","cimg":[["bank/6670e407_A.png"],["bank/6670e407_B.png"],["bank/6670e407_C.png"],["bank/6670e407_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"0a99e5bb","k":12,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/0a99e5bb_stem.png"],"e":"Only one of the three numbers, −13, is negative, so the probability is 1/3.","cimg":[["bank/0a99e5bb_A.png"],["bank/0a99e5bb_B.png"],["bank/0a99e5bb_C.png"],["bank/0a99e5bb_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"9b5b23fc","k":1,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/9b5b23fc_stem.png"],"e":"201% of x is f(x) = 2.01x, a line through the origin with positive slope 2.01. So f is an increasing linear function, not exponential.","cimg":[["bank/9b5b23fc_A.png"],["bank/9b5b23fc_B.png"],["bank/9b5b23fc_C.png"],["bank/9b5b23fc_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"4e527894","k":12,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/4e527894_stem.png"],"e":"8 of the 20 buttons are white, so the probability is 8/20.","cimg":[["bank/4e527894_A.png"],["bank/4e527894_B.png"],["bank/4e527894_C.png"],["bank/4e527894_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"808f7d6c","k":5,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/808f7d6c_q.png"],"e":"Substitute t = 4u: 2t = 2(4u) = 8u.","cimg":[["bank/808f7d6c_A.png"],["bank/808f7d6c_B.png"],["bank/808f7d6c_C.png"],["bank/808f7d6c_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"af142f8d","k":7,"diff":"Hard","type":"mc","img":["bank/af142f8d_stem.png"],"e":"Account A earns 6% of $500 = $30 in the first year, more than Account B's fixed $25. A's balance keeps growing, so its 6% interest only gets bigger, and A always earns more per year.","cimg":[["bank/af142f8d_A.png"],["bank/af142f8d_B.png"],["bank/af142f8d_C.png"],["bank/af142f8d_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"c78bb2b8","k":10,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/c78bb2b8_stem.png"],"e":"Weight each mean by its group size: (240 × 88 + 120 × 94) ÷ 360 = (21,120 + 11,280) ÷ 360 = 90. It is not the simple average 91, because there are twice as many Muskeget seals.","cimg":[["bank/c78bb2b8_A.png"],["bank/c78bb2b8_B.png"],["bank/c78bb2b8_C.png"],["bank/c78bb2b8_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"566759ef","k":7,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/566759ef_stem.png"],"e":"Each year the value is multiplied by 0.80: 800 × 0.80 × 0.80 = 800 × 0.64 = $512.","cimg":[["bank/566759ef_A.png"],["bank/566759ef_B.png"],["bank/566759ef_C.png"],["bank/566759ef_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"6e4a60dd","k":9,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/6e4a60dd_stem.png"],"e":"20% of $25.00 is 0.20 × 25 = $5.00.","cimg":[["bank/6e4a60dd_A.png"],["bank/6e4a60dd_B.png"],["bank/6e4a60dd_C.png"],["bank/6e4a60dd_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"ad1d6adb","k":9,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/ad1d6adb_stem.png"],"e":"The increase is 90 − 9 = 81, and 81 ÷ 9 = 9, or 900%. Remember to divide the change by the original amount, 9.","cimg":[["bank/ad1d6adb_A.png"],["bank/ad1d6adb_B.png"],["bank/ad1d6adb_C.png"],["bank/ad1d6adb_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"040f2a84","k":9,"diff":"Hard","type":"spr","img":["bank/040f2a84_stem.png"],"e":"80% less than $11.70 is 0.20 × 11.70 = $2.34. That sale price is 130% of the cost, so the cost is 2.34 ÷ 1.30 = $1.80.","ad":"1.8","a":1.8},{"id":"b73025e2","k":8,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/b73025e2_stem.png"],"e":"Each quart is 4 cups, so 83 quarts = 83 × 4 = 332 cups.","cimg":[["bank/b73025e2_A.png"],["bank/b73025e2_B.png"],["bank/b73025e2_C.png"],["bank/b73025e2_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"9ee22c16","k":13,"diff":"Medium","type":"spr","img":["bank/9ee22c16_stem.png"],"e":"In the sample, 202 + 34 = 236 of 400 voters plan to vote for A, or 59%. Applying that to 6,000 voters gives 0.59 × 6,000 = 3,540.","ad":"3540","a":3540.0},{"id":"41b71b4e","k":9,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/41b71b4e_stem.png"],"e":"20% greater than 60 is 1.20 × 60 = 72.","cimg":[["bank/41b71b4e_A.png"],["bank/41b71b4e_B.png"],["bank/41b71b4e_C.png"],["bank/41b71b4e_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"eaab8bc1","k":9,"diff":"Easy","type":"spr","img":["bank/eaab8bc1_stem.png"],"e":"80% of 300 is 0.80 × 300 = 240 seeds.","ad":"240","a":240.0},{"id":"46b2e169","k":12,"diff":"Easy","type":"spr","img":["bank/46b2e169_stem.png"],"e":"There are 13 + 37 = 50 pens in all, and 13 are red, so the probability is 13/50 = 0.26.","ad":"13/50","tol":0.0011,"a":0.26},{"id":"8213b1b3","k":9,"diff":"Medium","type":"spr","img":["bank/8213b1b3_stem.png"],"e":"0.001% as a decimal is 0.00001, so the maximum is 0.00001 × 140 = 0.0014 grams.","ad":"0.0014","a":0.0014},{"id":"ecf8d15f","k":12,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/ecf8d15f_stem.png"],"e":"9 of the 50 children chose vegetarian, so the probability is 9/50.","cimg":[["bank/ecf8d15f_A.png"],["bank/ecf8d15f_B.png"],["bank/ecf8d15f_C.png"],["bank/ecf8d15f_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"f8696cd8","k":12,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/f8696cd8_q.png"],"e":"Only Human Resources counts: 4 + 2 = 6 people, 2 with a master's degree: 2/6 = 1/3.","cimg":[["bank/f8696cd8_A.png"],["bank/f8696cd8_B.png"],["bank/f8696cd8_C.png"],["bank/f8696cd8_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"bc59c2d9","k":11,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/bc59c2d9_stem.png"],"e":"The line starts near 47°F at 0 feet and falls about 3°F per 1,000 feet. At 4,000 feet the line is at about 35°F.","cimg":[["bank/bc59c2d9_A.png"],["bank/bc59c2d9_B.png"],["bank/bc59c2d9_C.png"],["bank/bc59c2d9_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"50b2807e","k":11,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/50b2807e_stem.png"],"e":"The data fall from about y = 9.4 near x = 0 as x increases, so the model needs a positive intercept near 9.4 and a negative slope. y = 9.4 − 0.9x fits (at x = 10 it gives 0.4).","cimg":[["bank/50b2807e_A.png"],["bank/50b2807e_B.png"],["bank/50b2807e_C.png"],["bank/50b2807e_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"34f8cd89","k":9,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/34f8cd89_stem.png"],"e":"The share that are green, rectangular and metal is 0.37 × 0.37 × 0.42 ≈ 0.0575, or 5.75%. The rest, 100% − 5.75% = 94.25%, are not.","cimg":[["bank/34f8cd89_A.png"],["bank/34f8cd89_B.png"],["bank/34f8cd89_C.png"],["bank/34f8cd89_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"6fca0144","k":14,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/6fca0144_stem.png"],"e":"The trees were randomly selected from 17-year-old trees in this habitat, so the results apply to all 17-year-old baobab trees in this habitat, not to all of South Africa or to other ages.","cimg":[["bank/6fca0144_A.png"],["bank/6fca0144_B.png"],["bank/6fca0144_C.png"],["bank/6fca0144_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"20b69297","k":8,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/20b69297_stem.png"],"e":"The blue-to-yellow ratio is 2:3, so yellow is 1.5 times blue. With 5 ounces of blue she needs 1.5 × 5 = 7.5 ounces of yellow, which is 1.5 times the blue in the second batch.","cimg":[["bank/20b69297_A.png"],["bank/20b69297_B.png"],["bank/20b69297_C.png"],["bank/20b69297_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"94237701","k":10,"diff":"Medium","type":"spr","img":["bank/94237701_stem.png"],"e":"Group A in order is 2, 3, 4, 4, 5, 6, 6, 6, 9, so its median (5th value) is 5. Group B in order is 5, 5, 5, 5, 6, 6, 8, 8, 9, 10, 10, so its median (6th value) is 6. The difference is 6 − 5 = 1.","ad":"1","a":1.0},{"id":"24a1e6a7","k":11,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/24a1e6a7_stem.png"],"e":"The line goes from (0, 14) to about (13, 0), so the slope is about −14/13 ≈ −1.1.","cimg":[["bank/24a1e6a7_A.png"],["bank/24a1e6a7_B.png"],["bank/24a1e6a7_C.png"],["bank/24a1e6a7_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"9d95e7ad","k":11,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/9d95e7ad_stem.png"],"e":"The line runs from about (10, 17) to about (50, 74), so its slope is about 57 ÷ 40 ≈ 1.4. The closest choice is 1.5 grams of fat per gram of protein.","cimg":[["bank/9d95e7ad_A.png"],["bank/9d95e7ad_B.png"],["bank/9d95e7ad_C.png"],["bank/9d95e7ad_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"81d0f1e6","k":8,"diff":"Easy","type":"spr","img":["bank/81d0f1e6_stem.png"],"e":"153 is 9 times 17, so a must be 9 times 63: a = 567.","ad":"567","a":567.0},{"id":"11b06e35","k":15,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/11b06e35_stem.png"],"e":"The cube's volume is 0.60³ = 0.216 cubic meters. Mass = density × volume = 813 × 0.216 ≈ 175.6, which rounds to 176 kg.","cimg":[["bank/11b06e35_A.png"],["bank/11b06e35_B.png"],["bank/11b06e35_C.png"],["bank/11b06e35_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"39aa146d","k":11,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/39aa146d_stem.png"],"e":"The line rises, so the slope is positive. It goes from about (0, 0.3) to about (5, 2.5), a slope of about 2.2 ÷ 5 = 0.44.","cimg":[["bank/39aa146d_A.png"],["bank/39aa146d_B.png"],["bank/39aa146d_C.png"],["bank/39aa146d_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"58171b5e","k":7,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/58171b5e_stem.png"],"e":"Growing by a fixed percentage of the previous value each year is multiplicative growth, so the model is increasing exponential, not linear.","cimg":[["bank/58171b5e_A.png"],["bank/58171b5e_B.png"],["bank/58171b5e_C.png"],["bank/58171b5e_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"d7a3179d","k":8,"diff":"Easy","type":"spr","img":["bank/d7a3179d_stem.png"],"e":"Divide by 36 inches per yard: 1,116 ÷ 36 = 31 yards.","ad":"31","a":31.0},{"id":"d6456c7a","k":8,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/d6456c7a_stem.png"],"e":"One square mile is 1,760² = 3,097,600 square yards. Divide: 11,863,808 ÷ 3,097,600 = 3.83 square miles.","cimg":[["bank/d6456c7a_A.png"],["bank/d6456c7a_B.png"],["bank/d6456c7a_C.png"],["bank/d6456c7a_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"4347a032","k":8,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/4347a032_stem.png"],"e":"Each tablespoon is 3 teaspoons, so 44 × 3 = 132 teaspoons.","cimg":[["bank/4347a032_A.png"],["bank/4347a032_B.png"],["bank/4347a032_C.png"],["bank/4347a032_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"51c9d65f","k":8,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/51c9d65f_stem.png"],"e":"The length is 35/10 = 3.5 times the width. If the width increases by 7, the length must increase by 3.5 × 7 = 24.5 units.","cimg":[["bank/51c9d65f_A.png"],["bank/51c9d65f_B.png"],["bank/51c9d65f_C.png"],["bank/51c9d65f_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"763e6769","k":8,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/763e6769_stem.png"],"e":"x/y = 12/t, so y = xt/12. With x = 156, y = 156t/12 = 13t.","cimg":[["bank/763e6769_A.png"],["bank/763e6769_B.png"],["bank/763e6769_C.png"],["bank/763e6769_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"25faa756","k":9,"diff":"Hard","type":"spr","img":["bank/25faa756_stem.png"],"e":"a = 1.60b and c = (1 − 0.45)a = 0.55a. So c = 0.55 × 1.60b = 0.88b. (22/25 is also correct.)","ad":"0.88","a":0.88},{"id":"ad911622","k":9,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/ad911622_stem.png"],"e":"Multiply the factors: 1.67 increase gives × 2.67, and a 16% decrease gives × 0.84. Then 2.67 × 0.84 = 2.2428, a net increase of 124.28%.","cimg":[["bank/ad911622_A.png"],["bank/ad911622_B.png"],["bank/ad911622_C.png"],["bank/ad911622_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"8d63b6f1","k":11,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/8d63b6f1_stem.png"],"e":"Find x = 50 on the horizontal axis and go up to the dot there. It sits at y = 6 offspring.","cimg":[["bank/8d63b6f1_A.png"],["bank/8d63b6f1_B.png"],["bank/8d63b6f1_C.png"],["bank/8d63b6f1_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"25fc031a","k":10,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/25fc031a_stem.png"],"e":"Company A's data cluster tightly in the middle (25 to 40), while Company B's data pile up at both extremes (15–20 and 45–50), far from its center. So A has the smaller standard deviation.","cimg":[["bank/25fc031a_A.png"],["bank/25fc031a_B.png"],["bank/25fc031a_C.png"],["bank/25fc031a_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"d72a2b4d","k":9,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/d72a2b4d_stem.png"],"e":"p/100 = 17.36 ÷ 15.50 = 1.12, so p = 112. The April price is 112% of the March price.","cimg":[["bank/d72a2b4d_A.png"],["bank/d72a2b4d_B.png"],["bank/d72a2b4d_C.png"],["bank/d72a2b4d_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"cf0ae57a","k":11,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/cf0ae57a_stem.png"],"e":"Read the line, not the dots. It falls from about 5.7 at 0.2 AU to about 3.0 at 2.8 AU, about −1.04 per AU, so at 1.2 AU it is about 5.7 − 1.04 ≈ 4.6.","cimg":[["bank/cf0ae57a_A.png"],["bank/cf0ae57a_B.png"],["bank/cf0ae57a_C.png"],["bank/cf0ae57a_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"4e375d1f","k":8,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/4e375d1f_stem.png"],"e":"Divide by 100 centimeters per meter: 2,300 ÷ 100 = 23 meters.","cimg":[["bank/4e375d1f_A.png"],["bank/4e375d1f_B.png"],["bank/4e375d1f_C.png"],["bank/4e375d1f_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"771ee744","k":9,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/771ee744_stem.png"],"e":"10% of 320 is 0.10 × 320 = 32 red marbles.","cimg":[["bank/771ee744_A.png"],["bank/771ee744_B.png"],["bank/771ee744_C.png"],["bank/771ee744_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"e9ed719f","k":12,"diff":"Easy","type":"spr","img":["bank/e9ed719f_stem.png"],"e":"The table shows 30 red tiles out of 100, so the probability is 30/100 = 0.3.","ad":"3/10","tol":0.0011,"a":0.3},{"id":"beca03de","k":7,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/beca03de_stem.png"],"e":"The area is length × width. The width is w and the length is 15 times the width, so 15w is the length in feet.","cimg":[["bank/beca03de_A.png"],["bank/beca03de_B.png"],["bank/beca03de_C.png"],["bank/beca03de_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"512bd5b4","k":7,"diff":"Hard","type":"spr","img":["bank/512bd5b4_stem.png"],"e":"Increasing x by 6 increases the exponent x/3 by 2, which multiplies f(x) by 1.20² = 1.44. That is a 44% increase, so p = 44.","ad":"44","a":44.0},{"id":"4e18fc5d","k":5,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/4e18fc5d_stem.png"],"e":"Multiply both sides of v = −w/(150x) by 150x to get 150vx = −w, so w = −150vx.","cimg":[["bank/4e18fc5d_A.png"],["bank/4e18fc5d_B.png"],["bank/4e18fc5d_C.png"],["bank/4e18fc5d_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"f5c3e3b8","k":5,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/f5c3e3b8_stem.png"],"e":"Add exponents of like bases: m^(4+1) q^(4+5) z^(−1+3) = m⁵q⁹z².","cimg":[["bank/f5c3e3b8_A.png"],["bank/f5c3e3b8_B.png"],["bank/f5c3e3b8_C.png"],["bank/f5c3e3b8_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"a5663025","k":6,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/a5663025_stem.png"],"e":"The solutions are where the graphs intersect. The line crosses the parabola at two points, one on the left and one on the right, so there are 2 solutions.","cimg":[["bank/a5663025_A.png"],["bank/a5663025_B.png"],["bank/a5663025_C.png"],["bank/a5663025_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"3c95093c","k":4,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/3c95093c_stem.png"],"e":"Divide every term of 6x − 9y > 12 by 3 (positive, so the inequality sign stays): 2x − 3y > 4.","cimg":[["bank/3c95093c_A.png"],["bank/3c95093c_B.png"],["bank/3c95093c_C.png"],["bank/3c95093c_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"d0a7871e","k":6,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/d0a7871e_stem.png"],"e":"Set x + 1 = x² + x, which gives x² = 1, so x = 1 or x = −1. Only −1 is among the choices.","cimg":[["bank/d0a7871e_A.png"],["bank/d0a7871e_B.png"],["bank/d0a7871e_C.png"],["bank/d0a7871e_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"72ebc024","k":5,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/72ebc024_stem.png"],"e":"Factor out the greatest common factor 2xy: 16x³y² + 14xy = 2xy(8x²y + 7).","cimg":[["bank/72ebc024_A.png"],["bank/72ebc024_B.png"],["bank/72ebc024_C.png"],["bank/72ebc024_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"dd4ab4c4","k":5,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/dd4ab4c4_stem.png"],"e":"4a² + 20ab + 25b² is a perfect square: (2a)² + 2(2a)(5b) + (5b)² = (2a + 5b)². So 2a + 5b is a factor.","cimg":[["bank/dd4ab4c4_A.png"],["bank/dd4ab4c4_B.png"],["bank/dd4ab4c4_C.png"],["bank/dd4ab4c4_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"b8caaf84","k":5,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/b8caaf84_stem.png"],"e":"pv = (3x + 4)(x + 5) = 3x² + 19x + 20. Then subtract 2p = 6x + 8 and add v = x + 5: 3x² + 19x + 20 − 6x − 8 + x + 5 = 3x² + 14x + 17.","cimg":[["bank/b8caaf84_A.png"],["bank/b8caaf84_B.png"],["bank/b8caaf84_C.png"],["bank/b8caaf84_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"7f81d0c3","k":6,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/7f81d0c3_q.png"],"e":"By the quadratic formula, x = (1 ± √(1 + 4))/2 = (1 ± √5)/2.","cimg":[["bank/7f81d0c3_A.png"],["bank/7f81d0c3_B.png"],["bank/7f81d0c3_C.png"],["bank/7f81d0c3_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"332cd67b","k":6,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/332cd67b_stem.png"],"e":"The discriminant is (−15)² − 4(3)(18) = 225 − 216 = 9. It is positive, so there are exactly two real solutions (x = 2 and x = 3).","cimg":[["bank/332cd67b_A.png"],["bank/332cd67b_B.png"],["bank/332cd67b_C.png"],["bank/332cd67b_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"301faf80","k":6,"diff":"Medium","type":"spr","img":["bank/301faf80_stem.png"],"e":"Let the smaller be y and the larger 2y + 5. Then y(2y + 5) = 462, so 2y² + 5y − 462 = 0, which factors as (y − 14)(2y + 33) = 0. The positive solution is y = 14 (and 14 × 33 = 462).","ad":"14","a":14.0},{"id":"128c75e2","k":7,"diff":"Hard","type":"spr","img":["bank/128c75e2_stem.png"],"e":"Because a < 0, the absolute value of 15a is −15a, so g(15a) = −15a/a − 14 = −29. Likewise g(7a) = −7 − 14 = −21. The product is (−29)(−21) = 609.","ad":"609","a":609.0},{"id":"7f2524bf","k":7,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/7f2524bf_stem.png"],"e":"The y-intercept is the value at x = 0 months, the moment of purchase. The graph starts at $225, so the tablet was worth $225 when purchased.","cimg":[["bank/7f2524bf_A.png"],["bank/7f2524bf_B.png"],["bank/7f2524bf_C.png"],["bank/7f2524bf_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"e312081b","k":5,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/e312081b_stem.png"],"e":"Combine like terms: x + 2x = 3x and 5 − 3 = 2, so the result is 3x + 2.","cimg":[["bank/e312081b_A.png"],["bank/e312081b_B.png"],["bank/e312081b_C.png"],["bank/e312081b_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"02060533","k":1,"diff":"Hard","type":"mc","img":["bank/02060533_stem.png"],"e":"f(x) = g(x)(x + 3), so f(−27) = 3(−24) = −72 and f(−9) = 0(−6) = 0. The slope is 72/18 = 4, so f(x) = 4(x + 9) = 4x + 36 and the y-intercept is (0, 36).","cimg":[["bank/02060533_A.png"],["bank/02060533_B.png"],["bank/02060533_C.png"],["bank/02060533_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"52931bfa","k":5,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/52931bfa_stem.png"],"e":"Factor out (x − 7) on top: (x − 7)(8x − 3). The denominator is 2(x − 7). Since x > 7, cancel (x − 7) to get (8x − 3)/2.","cimg":[["bank/52931bfa_A.png"],["bank/52931bfa_B.png"],["bank/52931bfa_C.png"],["bank/52931bfa_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"1e003284","k":6,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/1e003284_stem.png"],"e":"Substitute x = 49: y = √49 + 9 = 7 + 9 = 16.","cimg":[["bank/1e003284_A.png"],["bank/1e003284_B.png"],["bank/1e003284_C.png"],["bank/1e003284_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"91e7ea5e","k":7,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/91e7ea5e_stem.png"],"e":"Set h(x) = 0: 2(x − 4)² = 32, so (x − 4)² = 16 and x − 4 = ±4. That gives x = 0 or x = 8, so t = 8.","cimg":[["bank/91e7ea5e_A.png"],["bank/91e7ea5e_B.png"],["bank/91e7ea5e_C.png"],["bank/91e7ea5e_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"e9aed539","k":7,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/e9aed539_stem.png"],"e":"Translating up 4 moves the vertex from (2, −2) to (2, 2) with no horizontal change. Only graph A has its vertex at (2, 2).","cimg":[["bank/e9aed539_A.png"],["bank/e9aed539_B.png"],["bank/e9aed539_C.png"],["bank/e9aed539_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"358f18bc","k":7,"diff":"Medium","type":"spr","img":["bank/358f18bc_stem.png"],"e":"The vertex is at x = 48/2 = 24. f(24) = 576 − 1,152 + 2,304 = 1,728, which is the minimum because the parabola opens upward.","ad":"1728","a":1728.0},{"id":"3a9d60b2","k":6,"diff":"Medium","type":"spr","img":["bank/3a9d60b2_stem.png"],"e":"Combine like terms: 5 times the absolute value of (4 − x) = 25, so the absolute value of (4 − x) is 5. Then 4 − x = 5 or 4 − x = −5, giving x = −1 or x = 9. The positive solution is 9.","ad":"9","a":9.0},{"id":"8490cc45","k":7,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/8490cc45_stem.png"],"e":"At x = 0, 2⁰ = 1, so f(0) = −8(1) + 22 = 14. The y-intercept is (0, 14).","cimg":[["bank/8490cc45_A.png"],["bank/8490cc45_B.png"],["bank/8490cc45_C.png"],["bank/8490cc45_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"4fbffc0a","k":7,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/4fbffc0a_stem.png"],"e":"The x-coordinate is time in seconds and the y-coordinate is height in meters, so (1.0, 4.8) means 1.0 second after launch the ball is 4.8 meters above the ground.","cimg":[["bank/4fbffc0a_A.png"],["bank/4fbffc0a_B.png"],["bank/4fbffc0a_C.png"],["bank/4fbffc0a_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"ebed7dc6","k":7,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/ebed7dc6_stem.png"],"e":"The maximum of y = −100x² + 1,400x + 7,200 occurs at the vertex x = −b/(2a) = −1,400/(2 × −100) = 7.","cimg":[["bank/ebed7dc6_A.png"],["bank/ebed7dc6_B.png"],["bank/ebed7dc6_C.png"],["bank/ebed7dc6_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"ba0edc30","k":6,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/ba0edc30_stem.png"],"e":"Complete the square: x² − 2x + 1 = 10, so (x − 1)² = 10 and x = 1 ± √10. Matching 1 + √k gives k = 10.","cimg":[["bank/ba0edc30_A.png"],["bank/ba0edc30_B.png"],["bank/ba0edc30_C.png"],["bank/ba0edc30_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"39714777","k":7,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/39714777_stem.png"],"e":"Solving gives p(x) = x² − 57. Since x² is never less than 0, the minimum value of p is 0 − 57 = −57.","cimg":[["bank/39714777_A.png"],["bank/39714777_B.png"],["bank/39714777_C.png"],["bank/39714777_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"fc3d783a","k":6,"diff":"Hard","type":"spr","img":["bank/fc3d783a_stem.png"],"e":"The line is y = 2.25. Setting −4x² + bx = 2.25 gives 4x² − bx + 2.25 = 0, which has exactly one solution when the discriminant b² − 4(4)(2.25) = b² − 36 = 0, so b = 6 (positive).","ad":"6","a":6.0},{"id":"a9084ca4","k":7,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/a9084ca4_stem.png"],"e":"The y-intercept is where x = 0, which is the year 1997. f(0) = 9,000(0.66)⁰ = 9,000, so about 9,000 advertisements were sent in 1997.","cimg":[["bank/a9084ca4_A.png"],["bank/a9084ca4_B.png"],["bank/a9084ca4_C.png"],["bank/a9084ca4_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"075b29b0","k":5,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/075b29b0_stem.png"],"e":"Combine like terms: 9x³ + 6x³ = 15x³, the only x² term is 5x², the only x term is 5x, and 7 − 5 = 2, giving 15x³ + 5x² + 5x + 2.","cimg":[["bank/075b29b0_A.png"],["bank/075b29b0_B.png"],["bank/075b29b0_C.png"],["bank/075b29b0_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"2c6f214f","k":7,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/2c6f214f_stem.png"],"e":"This is a geometric sequence with first term 9 and ratio 4, so the nth term is 9(4ⁿ⁻¹). Check: n = 1 gives 9(4⁰) = 9.","cimg":[["bank/2c6f214f_A.png"],["bank/2c6f214f_B.png"],["bank/2c6f214f_C.png"],["bank/2c6f214f_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"781c2f6e","k":7,"diff":"Hard","type":"mc","img":["bank/781c2f6e_stem.png"],"e":"The y-intercept of f is f(0) = a(1 + 2.2ᵇ) = a + a(2.2ᵇ). In g the y-intercept is a(1 + k) and in h it is a + m, so neither form shows the y-intercept value itself as a single constant or coefficient.","cimg":[["bank/781c2f6e_A.png"],["bank/781c2f6e_B.png"],["bank/781c2f6e_C.png"],["bank/781c2f6e_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"cb29c54c","k":7,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/cb29c54c_stem.png"],"e":"In vertex form y = a(x − h)² + k the vertex is (h, k) = (5.6, 502). Since x is seconds and y is feet, the rocket reaches a maximum height of 502 feet at 5.6 seconds.","cimg":[["bank/cb29c54c_A.png"],["bank/cb29c54c_B.png"],["bank/cb29c54c_C.png"],["bank/cb29c54c_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"4661e2a9","k":6,"diff":"Hard","type":"mc","img":["bank/4661e2a9_stem.png"],"e":"From the first equation x = y + 1. Substituting gives 2y + 1 = (y + 1)² − 3 = y² + 2y − 2, so y² = 3 and y = ±√3. With y = √3, x = 1 + √3.","cimg":[["bank/4661e2a9_A.png"],["bank/4661e2a9_B.png"],["bank/4661e2a9_C.png"],["bank/4661e2a9_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"6abec9a8","k":7,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/6abec9a8_stem.png"],"e":"The y-intercept is where the graph crosses the y-axis (x = 0). The curve crosses at y = −5, so the y-intercept is (0, −5). The line y = −4 is only a horizontal asymptote.","cimg":[["bank/6abec9a8_A.png"],["bank/6abec9a8_B.png"],["bank/6abec9a8_C.png"],["bank/6abec9a8_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"ad2ec615","k":5,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/ad2ec615_stem.png"],"e":"Treat x² as a single variable u: u² − u − 6 = (u − 3)(u + 2). Substituting back gives (x² + 2)(x² − 3).","cimg":[["bank/ad2ec615_A.png"],["bank/ad2ec615_B.png"],["bank/ad2ec615_C.png"],["bank/ad2ec615_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"42c71eb5","k":5,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/42c71eb5_stem.png"],"e":"(2x + 5)² = 4x² + 20x + 25. Then −(x − 2) = −x + 2 and 2(x + 3) = 2x + 6. Adding: 4x² + 21x + 33.","cimg":[["bank/42c71eb5_A.png"],["bank/42c71eb5_B.png"],["bank/42c71eb5_C.png"],["bank/42c71eb5_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"52b1700c","k":7,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/52b1700c_stem.png"],"e":"At t = 0 the amount is 604, so the starting value is 604. Each year the amount grows by 2.42, and 2.42/604 = 0.004, so n = 604(1 + 0.004)ᵗ.","cimg":[["bank/52b1700c_A.png"],["bank/52b1700c_B.png"],["bank/52b1700c_C.png"],["bank/52b1700c_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"371cbf6b","k":5,"diff":"Hard","type":"mc","img":["bank/371cbf6b_stem.png"],"e":"Match the x³ coefficients: 5a = 20, so a = 4. Match the x² coefficients: −ab + 15 = −9, so ab = 24.","cimg":[["bank/371cbf6b_A.png"],["bank/371cbf6b_B.png"],["bank/371cbf6b_C.png"],["bank/371cbf6b_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"b4acba95","k":6,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/b4acba95_stem.png"],"e":"The discriminant is (−12)² − 4(1)(27) = 144 − 108 = 36, which is positive, so there are exactly two real solutions (x = 3 and x = 9).","cimg":[["bank/b4acba95_A.png"],["bank/b4acba95_B.png"],["bank/b4acba95_C.png"],["bank/b4acba95_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"ff8c5844","k":7,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/ff8c5844_stem.png"],"e":"g(0) = 1 so there is no extra coefficient, and each step in x multiplies g by 1/25 (25 to 1 to 1/25). So g(x) = (1/25)ˣ.","cimg":[["bank/ff8c5844_A.png"],["bank/ff8c5844_B.png"],["bank/ff8c5844_C.png"],["bank/ff8c5844_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"a05bd3a4","k":5,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/a05bd3a4_q.png"],"e":"x² − 5 is a difference of squares: x² − (√5)² = (x + √5)(x − √5).","cimg":[["bank/a05bd3a4_A.png"],["bank/a05bd3a4_B.png"],["bank/a05bd3a4_C.png"],["bank/a05bd3a4_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"c3b116d7","k":5,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/c3b116d7_stem.png"],"e":"Factoring gives 3x² + 20x − 63 = (3x − 7)(x + 9), so 3x − 7 is a factor but x − 9 is not (x + 9 is).","cimg":[["bank/c3b116d7_A.png"],["bank/c3b116d7_B.png"],["bank/c3b116d7_C.png"],["bank/c3b116d7_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"40c09d66","k":5,"diff":"Medium","type":"spr","img":["bank/40c09d66_stem.png"],"e":"√(x⁵) = x^(5/2) and ∛(x⁴) = x^(4/3). Dividing subtracts exponents: 5/2 − 4/3 = 15/6 − 8/6 = 7/6, so a/b = 7/6.","ad":"7/6","tol":0.0011,"a":1.1666666666666667},{"id":"f423771c","k":7,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/f423771c_stem.png"],"e":"At x = 0, h = 1.23, so the initial value is 1.23. Checking growth: 1.23(1.12)² ≈ 1.54 and 1.23(1.12)⁴ ≈ 1.94, matching the table, so h(x) = 1.23(1.12)ˣ.","cimg":[["bank/f423771c_A.png"],["bank/f423771c_B.png"],["bank/f423771c_C.png"],["bank/f423771c_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"b8f13a3a","k":7,"diff":"Hard","type":"spr","img":["bank/b8f13a3a_stem.png"],"e":"The y-intercept of y = f(x) − 12 is f(0) − 12 = −1 + b − 12 = −75/7, so b = 13 − 75/7 = 16/7. Then a(16/7) = 320/7 gives a = 20.","ad":"20","a":20.0},{"id":"8e1da169","k":7,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/8e1da169_stem.png"],"e":"The parabola opens upward and its zeros are 44 and 46. The minimum is at the vertex, halfway between the zeros: (44 + 46)/2 = 45.","cimg":[["bank/8e1da169_A.png"],["bank/8e1da169_B.png"],["bank/8e1da169_C.png"],["bank/8e1da169_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"1d3c5c95","k":7,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/1d3c5c95_stem.png"],"e":"In f(x) = a(b)ˣ, a is the value when x = 0. Here x = 0 is the year 2012, so 4,000 is the estimated initial beetle population in 2012.","cimg":[["bank/1d3c5c95_A.png"],["bank/1d3c5c95_B.png"],["bank/1d3c5c95_C.png"],["bank/1d3c5c95_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"ae05d37b","k":7,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/ae05d37b_stem.png"],"e":"The population doubles each time the exponent t/790 increases by 1, which happens every 790 minutes.","cimg":[["bank/ae05d37b_A.png"],["bank/ae05d37b_B.png"],["bank/ae05d37b_C.png"],["bank/ae05d37b_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"1ee962ec","k":7,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/1ee962ec_stem.png"],"e":"Read points from the graph: it starts at (0, 0), reaches its lowest point at (3, −12), and returns to sea level at (6, 0). Only table C lists these points.","cimg":[["bank/1ee962ec_A.png"],["bank/1ee962ec_B.png"],["bank/1ee962ec_C.png"],["bank/1ee962ec_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"c6a26e14","k":6,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/c6a26e14_stem.png"],"e":"The absolute value equation means x + 45 = 48 or x + 45 = −48, so x = 3 or x = −93. The positive solution is 3.","cimg":[["bank/c6a26e14_A.png"],["bank/c6a26e14_B.png"],["bank/c6a26e14_C.png"],["bank/c6a26e14_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"07bcecac","k":7,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/07bcecac_stem.png"],"e":"P(8) is the output when t = 8, which is 8 years after 1984, and the output is population in millions, so the predicted population was about 32.91 million.","cimg":[["bank/07bcecac_A.png"],["bank/07bcecac_B.png"],["bank/07bcecac_C.png"],["bank/07bcecac_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"ad03127d","k":5,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/ad03127d_stem.png"],"e":"Subtract t from both sides: 6r − t = 7s. Divide by 7: s = (6r − t)/7.","cimg":[["bank/ad03127d_A.png"],["bank/ad03127d_B.png"],["bank/ad03127d_C.png"],["bank/ad03127d_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"02add2d2","k":7,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/02add2d2_stem.png"],"e":"Growing by 7% each month means multiplying by 1 + 0.07 = 1.07 each month, starting from 1,300, so c = 1,300(1.07)ᵐ.","cimg":[["bank/02add2d2_A.png"],["bank/02add2d2_B.png"],["bank/02add2d2_C.png"],["bank/02add2d2_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"f65288e8","k":6,"diff":"Hard","type":"mc","img":["bank/f65288e8_q.png"],"e":"x² + 10x + 25 = (x + 5)², so (x + 5)² = 1/4 and x + 5 = ±1/2. 1/2 is a possible value.","cimg":[["bank/f65288e8_A.png"],["bank/f65288e8_B.png"],["bank/f65288e8_C.png"],["bank/f65288e8_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"788bfd56","k":7,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/788bfd56_stem.png"],"e":"f(144) = 4 + √144 = 4 + 12 = 16.","cimg":[["bank/788bfd56_A.png"],["bank/788bfd56_B.png"],["bank/788bfd56_C.png"],["bank/788bfd56_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"2c288148","k":6,"diff":"Hard","type":"spr","img":["bank/2c288148_stem.png"],"e":"Let u = 58 − x ≥ 0; squaring gives k − 58 + u = u², or u² − u + (58 − k) = 0. Exactly one real solution first occurs when this has a double root: 1 − 4(58 − k) = 0, so k = 57.75 and 4k = 231 (smaller k gives no solution).","ad":"231","a":231.0},{"id":"40491607","k":7,"diff":"Medium","type":"spr","img":["bank/40491607_stem.png"],"e":"g(x) = f(x) + 6. f(4) = (3)(7)(2) = 42, so b = g(4) = 42 + 6 = 48.","ad":"48","a":48.0},{"id":"369b7bb7","k":7,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/369b7bb7_stem.png"],"e":"g(3) = √(8 × 3 + 1) = √25 = 5.","cimg":[["bank/369b7bb7_A.png"],["bank/369b7bb7_B.png"],["bank/369b7bb7_C.png"],["bank/369b7bb7_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"3206b905","k":5,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/3206b905_stem.png"],"e":"Factor out the greatest common factor 8x: 8x¹⁰ − 8x⁹ + 88x = 8x(x⁹ − x⁸ + 11).","cimg":[["bank/3206b905_A.png"],["bank/3206b905_B.png"],["bank/3206b905_C.png"],["bank/3206b905_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"f89af023","k":15,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/f89af023_stem.png"],"e":"If the width is w, the length is 2w, so w × 2w = 2w² = 162. Then w² = 81 and w = 9 meters.","cimg":[["bank/f89af023_A.png"],["bank/f89af023_B.png"],["bank/f89af023_C.png"],["bank/f89af023_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"7902bed0","k":7,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/7902bed0_stem.png"],"e":"The maximum height 51.84 at t = 1.8 means the vertex is (1.8, 51.84), giving h = a(t − 1.8)² + 51.84. Only D has this vertex, and it checks: at t = 3.6, −16(1.8)² + 51.84 = −51.84 + 51.84 = 0.","cimg":[["bank/7902bed0_A.png"],["bank/7902bed0_B.png"],["bank/7902bed0_C.png"],["bank/7902bed0_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"5ba187d4","k":5,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/5ba187d4_stem.png"],"e":"Factor out 100: 100x² + 2,600 = 100(x² + 26).","cimg":[["bank/5ba187d4_A.png"],["bank/5ba187d4_B.png"],["bank/5ba187d4_C.png"],["bank/5ba187d4_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"4a0d0399","k":7,"diff":"Hard","type":"spr","img":["bank/4a0d0399_stem.png"],"e":"The y-intercept gives f(0) = a⁰ + b = 1 + b = −323, so b = −324. (The x-intercept then gives a² = 324.)","ad":"-324","a":-324.0},{"id":"768b60d2","k":7,"diff":"Hard","type":"mc","img":["bank/768b60d2_stem.png"],"e":"f(0) = 22(1.5)¹ = 33, so c = 33. All four forms are equivalent, but only f(x) = 33(1.5)ˣ shows 33 as the coefficient.","cimg":[["bank/768b60d2_A.png"],["bank/768b60d2_B.png"],["bank/768b60d2_C.png"],["bank/768b60d2_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"e53add44","k":9,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/e53add44_stem.png"],"e":"A 4% increase each year means multiplying by 1 + 0.04 = 1.04 each year, so a = 1.04.","cimg":[["bank/e53add44_A.png"],["bank/e53add44_B.png"],["bank/e53add44_C.png"],["bank/e53add44_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"f2f3fa00","k":0,"diff":"Medium","type":"spr","img":["bank/f2f3fa00_stem.png"],"e":"Multiply both sides by 5: 5a = v_f − 12. Add 12: v_f = 5a + 12, so x = 5.","ad":"5","a":5.0},{"id":"b4a6ed81","k":5,"diff":"Easy","type":"spr","img":["bank/b4a6ed81_stem.png"],"e":"Factor out the greatest common factor: 90y⁵ − 54y⁴ = 6y⁴(15y − 9), so r = 6.","ad":"6","a":6.0},{"id":"9654add7","k":7,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/9654add7_stem.png"],"e":"The x-intercepts are where y = f(x) = 0. Since x is the unit price and f(x) is revenue, a is a unit price (other than $0) that results in revenue of $0.","cimg":[["bank/9654add7_A.png"],["bank/9654add7_B.png"],["bank/9654add7_C.png"],["bank/9654add7_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"4618501a","k":7,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/4618501a_stem.png"],"e":"In f(x) = a(b)ˣ, a is the value when x = 0. Here x = 0 is 2008, so 3,000 is the estimated initial population in 2008.","cimg":[["bank/4618501a_A.png"],["bank/4618501a_B.png"],["bank/4618501a_C.png"],["bank/4618501a_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"34847f8a","k":5,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/34847f8a_stem.png"],"e":"Combine over the common denominator: 2(x + 5) + 3(x − 2) = 5x + 4, so r = 5 and t = 4, giving rt = 20.","cimg":[["bank/34847f8a_A.png"],["bank/34847f8a_B.png"],["bank/34847f8a_C.png"],["bank/34847f8a_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"253985c2","k":5,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/253985c2_stem.png"],"e":"Combine the like terms 6x + 5x = 11x. The 4y term cannot be combined with x terms, so the result is 11x + 4y.","cimg":[["bank/253985c2_A.png"],["bank/253985c2_B.png"],["bank/253985c2_C.png"],["bank/253985c2_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"cc776a04","k":5,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/cc776a04_q.png"],"e":"(1.5x − 2.4)² = 2.25x² − 7.2x + 5.76. Subtract 5.2x² − 6.4: −2.95x² − 7.2x + 12.16.","cimg":[["bank/cc776a04_A.png"],["bank/cc776a04_B.png"],["bank/cc776a04_C.png"],["bank/cc776a04_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"263f9937","k":7,"diff":"Hard","type":"mc","img":["bank/263f9937_stem.png"],"e":"The count doubles each day, so on day n it is 2.5 × 10⁵ × 2ⁿ⁻¹. Setting this equal to 5.12 × 10⁸ gives 2ⁿ⁻¹ = 2,048 = 2¹¹, so n = 12.","cimg":[["bank/263f9937_A.png"],["bank/263f9937_B.png"],["bank/263f9937_C.png"],["bank/263f9937_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"4ac59df6","k":5,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/4ac59df6_stem.png"],"e":"Multiply the coefficients 8 × 7 = 56 and the variables y × y = y² and z × z = z², giving 56y²z².","cimg":[["bank/4ac59df6_A.png"],["bank/4ac59df6_B.png"],["bank/4ac59df6_C.png"],["bank/4ac59df6_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"fada6b03","k":6,"diff":"Hard","type":"spr","img":["bank/fada6b03_stem.png"],"e":"By the quadratic formula, x = (8 ± √(64 − 4(2)(−7)))/(2 × 2) = (8 ± √120)/4. Matching (8 − √k)/4 gives k = 120.","ad":"120","a":120.0},{"id":"926c246b","k":7,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/926c246b_stem.png"],"e":"5,640 is the value of D when t = 0, which is the year 2010, so it is the estimated data traffic in 2010.","cimg":[["bank/926c246b_A.png"],["bank/926c246b_B.png"],["bank/926c246b_C.png"],["bank/926c246b_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"84e5e36c","k":6,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/84e5e36c_stem.png"],"e":"Substitute y = 76: 76 = x² − 5, so x² = 81 and x = 9 or x = −9. Only −9 is listed.","cimg":[["bank/84e5e36c_A.png"],["bank/84e5e36c_B.png"],["bank/84e5e36c_C.png"],["bank/84e5e36c_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"ff2c1431","k":5,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/ff2c1431_stem.png"],"e":"Divide both sides by 5: 7m/5 = n + p. Subtract p: n = 7m/5 − p.","cimg":[["bank/ff2c1431_A.png"],["bank/ff2c1431_B.png"],["bank/ff2c1431_C.png"],["bank/ff2c1431_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"137cc6fd","k":5,"diff":"Hard","type":"spr","img":["bank/137cc6fd_stem.png"],"e":"The fifth root is (70n)^(1/5), and (⁶√(70n))² = (70n)^(2/6) = (70n)^(1/3). Multiplying adds exponents: 1/5 + 1/3 = 8/15, so 30x = 8/15 and x = 8/450 = 4/225.","ad":"4/225","tol":0.0011,"a":0.017777777777777778},{"id":"6ce95fc8","k":6,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/6ce95fc8_q.png"],"e":"Rewrite as 2x² − 2x − 5 = 0. The quadratic formula gives x = (2 ± √44)/4 = (1 ± √11)/2, so (1 + √11)/2 is a solution.","cimg":[["bank/6ce95fc8_A.png"],["bank/6ce95fc8_B.png"],["bank/6ce95fc8_C.png"],["bank/6ce95fc8_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"4dd4efcf","k":7,"diff":"Hard","type":"mc","img":["bank/4dd4efcf_stem.png"],"e":"Since f(−9) = f(3), the vertex is at x = −3, so −4/(2a) = −3 and a = 2/3, which makes II false. Then k = f(−3) = 6 − 12 + c = c − 6 < 0 only requires c < 6, so c could be positive and I need not be true.","cimg":[["bank/4dd4efcf_A.png"],["bank/4dd4efcf_B.png"],["bank/4dd4efcf_C.png"],["bank/4dd4efcf_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"cc2601cb","k":7,"diff":"Easy","type":"spr","img":["bank/cc2601cb_stem.png"],"e":"The graph touches the x-axis at only one point, its vertex (7, 0), so x = 7.","ad":"7","a":7.0},{"id":"6bdcac03","k":6,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/6bdcac03_stem.png"],"e":"The square of any real number is never negative, so x² cannot equal −841. There are zero real solutions.","cimg":[["bank/6bdcac03_A.png"],["bank/6bdcac03_B.png"],["bank/6bdcac03_C.png"],["bank/6bdcac03_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"f5aa5040","k":6,"diff":"Hard","type":"spr","img":["bank/f5aa5040_stem.png"],"e":"The line is y = c/2. Setting −2x² + 9x = c/2 gives 2x² − 9x + c/2 = 0, which has exactly one solution when the discriminant 81 − 4(2)(c/2) = 81 − 4c = 0, so c = 81/4 (20.25).","ad":"81/4","tol":0.0011,"a":20.25},{"id":"252a3b3a","k":7,"diff":"Hard","type":"mc","img":["bank/252a3b3a_stem.png"],"e":"The graph crosses the x-axis at x = 0 and x = 4 and only touches it at x = −5, so x = −5 is a double root. That requires the factor (x + 5)², which matches y = −(1/10)x(x − 4)(x + 5)².","cimg":[["bank/252a3b3a_A.png"],["bank/252a3b3a_B.png"],["bank/252a3b3a_C.png"],["bank/252a3b3a_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"2992ac30","k":7,"diff":"Hard","type":"mc","img":["bank/2992ac30_stem.png"],"e":"The population grows by 4% each time the exponent (6/4)t increases by 1, which happens when t = 4/6 = 2/3 year. Two-thirds of 12 months is 8 months.","cimg":[["bank/2992ac30_A.png"],["bank/2992ac30_B.png"],["bank/2992ac30_C.png"],["bank/2992ac30_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"58443765","k":6,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/58443765_stem.png"],"e":"Set 5x + 4 = 5x² + 4, so 5x² − 5x = 0 and x = 0 or x = 1. When x = 0, y = 4, giving (0, 4).","cimg":[["bank/58443765_A.png"],["bank/58443765_B.png"],["bank/58443765_C.png"],["bank/58443765_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"3d7d7534","k":6,"diff":"Easy","type":"spr","img":["bank/3d7d7534_stem.png"],"e":"Add 7 to both sides: (d − 30)(d + 30) = 0, so d = 30 or d = −30. Either value is correct.","ad":"30 or -30","a":30.0,"alts":[30.0,-30.0]},{"id":"841ef26c","k":7,"diff":"Hard","type":"mc","img":["bank/841ef26c_stem.png"],"e":"f has its minimum at x = −64/(2 × 4) = −8. Since g(x) = f(x + 5), g reaches its minimum when x + 5 = −8, so x = −13.","cimg":[["bank/841ef26c_A.png"],["bank/841ef26c_B.png"],["bank/841ef26c_C.png"],["bank/841ef26c_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"cc6ccd71","k":7,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/cc6ccd71_stem.png"],"e":"f(x) = 0 at each x-intercept. The graph crosses the x-axis three times (near x = −1, x = 4, and x = 7), so there are three values.","cimg":[["bank/cc6ccd71_A.png"],["bank/cc6ccd71_B.png"],["bank/cc6ccd71_C.png"],["bank/cc6ccd71_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"70482e20","k":5,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/70482e20_stem.png"],"e":"These are like terms, so subtract the coefficients: 11x³ − 5x³ = 6x³. The exponent does not change.","cimg":[["bank/70482e20_A.png"],["bank/70482e20_B.png"],["bank/70482e20_C.png"],["bank/70482e20_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"8452c42b","k":5,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/8452c42b_stem.png"],"e":"These are like terms, so add the coefficients: 50x² + 5x² = 55x².","cimg":[["bank/8452c42b_A.png"],["bank/8452c42b_B.png"],["bank/8452c42b_C.png"],["bank/8452c42b_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"b39d74a0","k":7,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/b39d74a0_stem.png"],"e":"The table fits y = x³: it passes through (0, 0) and (1, 1) and rises steeply, with y = 8 at x = 2. Graph B passes through the origin and (1, 1); C is shifted up, D rises too fast, and A is decreasing.","cimg":[["bank/b39d74a0_A.png"],["bank/b39d74a0_B.png"],["bank/b39d74a0_C.png"],["bank/b39d74a0_D.png","bank/b39d74a0_D1.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"ea6d05bb","k":5,"diff":"Medium","type":"spr","img":["bank/ea6d05bb_stem.png"],"e":"The x-terms of the product are 3x × 6 = 18x and −23 × 19x = −437x. Adding them gives b = 18 − 437 = −419.","ad":"-419","a":-419.0},{"id":"09d21d79","k":7,"diff":"Hard","type":"spr","img":["bank/09d21d79_stem.png"],"e":"The y-intercept is (0, −6), so c = −6. The vertex is at x = −1, so −b/(2 × 2) = −1 and b = 4. Then bc = 4 × (−6) = −24.","ad":"-24","a":-24.0},{"id":"722de804","k":6,"diff":"Easy","type":"spr","img":["bank/722de804_stem.png"],"e":"x − 47 = 1 or x − 47 = −1, so x = 48 or x = 46. Their sum is 48 + 46 = 94.","ad":"94","a":94.0},{"id":"95d1c344","k":7,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/95d1c344_stem.png"],"e":"The end of November 2012 is x = 0, and the graph meets the y-axis at y = 5, so the company had about 5 active projects.","cimg":[["bank/95d1c344_A.png"],["bank/95d1c344_B.png"],["bank/95d1c344_C.png"],["bank/95d1c344_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"0536ad4f","k":5,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/0536ad4f_stem.png"],"e":"First combine inside the parentheses: 4w + 3w = 7w. Then 20w − 7w = 13w.","cimg":[["bank/0536ad4f_A.png"],["bank/0536ad4f_B.png"],["bank/0536ad4f_C.png"],["bank/0536ad4f_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"433184f1","k":5,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/433184f1_stem.png"],"e":"Use the common denominator (x + 1)(4x − 5): the numerator is 4(x + 1) − (4x − 5) = 4x + 4 − 4x + 5 = 9, giving 9/((x + 1)(4x − 5)).","cimg":[["bank/433184f1_A.png"],["bank/433184f1_B.png"],["bank/433184f1_C.png"],["bank/433184f1_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"d135f4bf","k":7,"diff":"Medium","type":"spr","img":["bank/d135f4bf_stem.png"],"e":"g(x) = f(x) + 4. f(0) = (−6)(−2)(6) = 72, so g(0) = 72 + 4 = 76.","ad":"76","a":76.0},{"id":"b0543157","k":7,"diff":"Hard","type":"mc","img":["bank/b0543157_stem.png"],"e":"g(−22) = 0 means the numerator is 0: 484 + 22 − a = 0, so a = 506. Then g(0) = (−a)/(−b) = 506/b = 22, so b = 23.","cimg":[["bank/b0543157_A.png"],["bank/b0543157_B.png"],["bank/b0543157_C.png"],["bank/b0543157_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"1d3fee25","k":5,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/1d3fee25_stem.png"],"e":"Distribute: 3(x + 5) = 3x + 15. Then 3x + 15 − 6 = 3x + 9.","cimg":[["bank/1d3fee25_A.png"],["bank/1d3fee25_B.png"],["bank/1d3fee25_C.png"],["bank/1d3fee25_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"4ca30186","k":6,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/4ca30186_stem.png"],"e":"The solution to a system is the point where the graphs intersect. The line and the curve meet at the marked point (2, 4).","cimg":[["bank/4ca30186_A.png"],["bank/4ca30186_B.png"],["bank/4ca30186_C.png"],["bank/4ca30186_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"911383f2","k":6,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/911383f2_stem.png"],"e":"By the zero product property the solutions are x = 4, x = −2, and x = 1. Their product is 4 × (−2) × 1 = −8.","cimg":[["bank/911383f2_A.png"],["bank/911383f2_B.png"],["bank/911383f2_C.png"],["bank/911383f2_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"d8789a4c","k":5,"diff":"Hard","type":"mc","img":["bank/d8789a4c_stem.png"],"e":"If (x² − c)/(x − b) = x + b, then x² − c = (x − b)(x + b) = x² − b², so c = b². Among the choices, only 4 is a perfect square (b = 2).","cimg":[["bank/d8789a4c_A.png"],["bank/d8789a4c_B.png"],["bank/d8789a4c_C.png"],["bank/d8789a4c_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"b80d10d7","k":6,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/b80d10d7_stem.png"],"e":"Multiply both sides by x + 5: 2(x + 1) = (x + 5) − 1, so 2x + 2 = x + 4 and x = 2. This does not make the denominator zero.","cimg":[["bank/b80d10d7_A.png"],["bank/b80d10d7_B.png"],["bank/b80d10d7_C.png"],["bank/b80d10d7_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"fde6f3bb","k":5,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/fde6f3bb_stem.png"],"e":"Multiply out: (3/5)x × 6x = 18x²/5; the x-terms are (3/5)(−5)x + (7/6)(6x) = −3x + 7x = 4x; and the constant is (7/6)(−5) = −35/6.","cimg":[["bank/fde6f3bb_A.png"],["bank/fde6f3bb_B.png"],["bank/fde6f3bb_C.png"],["bank/fde6f3bb_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"ffdfe1e1","k":7,"diff":"Hard","type":"mc","img":["bank/ffdfe1e1_stem.png"],"e":"Half the remaining players are eliminated each round: 120 in round 1, then 60, 30, 15. That is 240(1/2)ʳ, since 240(1/2)¹ = 120.","cimg":[["bank/ffdfe1e1_A.png"],["bank/ffdfe1e1_B.png"],["bank/ffdfe1e1_C.png"],["bank/ffdfe1e1_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"d4950429","k":6,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/d4950429_stem.png"],"e":"x(x − 15) = 76 gives x² − 15x − 76 = 0, which factors as (x − 19)(x + 4) = 0. A length must be positive, so x = 19.","cimg":[["bank/d4950429_A.png"],["bank/d4950429_B.png"],["bank/d4950429_C.png"],["bank/d4950429_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"752055d1","k":7,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/752055d1_stem.png"],"e":"At t = 0, P = C = 12,000. At t = 4, 12,000(2)^(4r) = 24,000, so 2^(4r) = 2, meaning 4r = 1 and r = 1/4.","cimg":[["bank/752055d1_A.png"],["bank/752055d1_B.png"],["bank/752055d1_C.png"],["bank/752055d1_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"d0a53ef5","k":6,"diff":"Hard","type":"spr","img":["bank/d0a53ef5_stem.png"],"e":"Square both sides: (x − 2)² = 3x + 34, so x² − 7x − 30 = 0 and (x − 10)(x + 3) = 0. Both x = 10 and x = −3 check (at x = −3 both sides equal 5), so the smallest solution is −3.","ad":"-3","a":-3.0},{"id":"fcdf87b7","k":6,"diff":"Medium","type":"spr","img":["bank/fcdf87b7_stem.png"],"e":"Set x² − 4x + 4 = 4 − x, so x² − 3x = 0 and x(x − 3) = 0. So x = 0 or x = 3.","ad":"0 or 3","a":0.0,"alts":[0.0,3.0]},{"id":"3148fe3e","k":6,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/3148fe3e_stem.png"],"e":"From the second equation y = 8x + 16. Substituting: x² + 8x + 16 + 10 = 10, so x² + 8x + 16 = 0, which is (x + 4)² = 0 and x = −4.","cimg":[["bank/3148fe3e_A.png"],["bank/3148fe3e_B.png"],["bank/3148fe3e_C.png"],["bank/3148fe3e_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"271ffad7","k":7,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/271ffad7_stem.png"],"e":"A parabola is symmetric about its vertex at t = 3. The height is 7 m at t = 0, which is 3 seconds before the vertex, so it is 7 m again 3 seconds after: t = 6.","cimg":[["bank/271ffad7_A.png"],["bank/271ffad7_B.png"],["bank/271ffad7_C.png"],["bank/271ffad7_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"ee857afb","k":7,"diff":"Easy","type":"spr","img":["bank/ee857afb_stem.png"],"e":"For y = x² − 14x + 22 the minimum is at the vertex x = −b/(2a) = 14/2 = 7.","ad":"7","a":7.0},{"id":"a520ba07","k":5,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/a520ba07_stem.png"],"e":"The cube root divides each exponent by 3: ∛(x³y⁶) = x^(3/3) y^(6/3) = xy².","cimg":[["bank/a520ba07_A.png"],["bank/a520ba07_B.png"],["bank/a520ba07_C.png"],["bank/a520ba07_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"5b6af6b1","k":5,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/5b6af6b1_stem.png"],"e":"Distribute: d(8d² − 3) − 6(8d² − 3) = 8d³ − 3d − 48d² + 18 = 8d³ − 48d² − 3d + 18.","cimg":[["bank/5b6af6b1_A.png"],["bank/5b6af6b1_B.png"],["bank/5b6af6b1_C.png"],["bank/5b6af6b1_D.png"]],"a":2},{"id":"652054da","k":0,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/652054da_q.png"],"e":"Multiply both sides of s = (3/2)p by 2/3: p = (2/3)s.","cimg":[["bank/652054da_A.png"],["bank/652054da_B.png"],["bank/652054da_C.png"],["bank/652054da_D.png"]],"a":0},{"id":"0380bbdc","k":6,"diff":"Medium","type":"mc","img":["bank/0380bbdc_stem.png"],"e":"Divide by 4: √(2x) = 4. Square: 2x = 16, so x = 8 and 6x = 48.","cimg":[["bank/0380bbdc_A.png"],["bank/0380bbdc_B.png"],["bank/0380bbdc_C.png"],["bank/0380bbdc_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"837e9da7","k":7,"diff":"Easy","type":"mc","img":["bank/837e9da7_stem.png"],"e":"Substitute x = 3: f(3) = 1/(6 × 3) = 1/18.","cimg":[["bank/837e9da7_A.png"],["bank/837e9da7_B.png"],["bank/837e9da7_C.png"],["bank/837e9da7_D.png"]],"a":3},{"id":"a255ae72","k":5,"diff":"Hard","type":"mc","img":["bank/a255ae72_stem.png"],"e":"x² − y² = (a + b) − (a + c) = b − c, so (x² − y²)² = (b − c)² = b² − 2bc + c².","cimg":[["bank/a255ae72_A.png"],["bank/a255ae72_B.png"],["bank/a255ae72_C.png"],["bank/a255ae72_D.png"]],"a":1},{"id":"dd3b1e1a","k":7,"diff":"Easy","type":"spr","img":["bank/dd3b1e1a_stem.png"],"e":"The point (0, b) is the y-intercept, so b = f(0) = 0⁵ + 9(0) + 17 = 17.","ad":"17","a":17.0}];
